2:08:05 PM [express] GET /api/content 304 in 10ms :: [{"id":2,"userId":3,"board":"CBSE","className":"Grade 1","subject":"English","chapter":"The animal song","topic":"","extractedText":"[Page 1]\n8. The _______________ _______________ is teaching English.  \n\n9. Squirrels love to eat _______________ _______________.  \n\n10. The _______________ _______________ is a cunning animal.  \n\n---\n\n**KNOW**  \n\n**PROPER NOUNS**  \nThe words **Simba**, **Bimbi**, **Luna**, **Bunny**, **Ray**, **Dale** and **Lee** have been specially given to the lion, lamb, rabbit and horse respectively. These words are called **special names** or **proper nouns**. They begin with a **capital letter**.  \n\n---\n\n**LEARN**  \n\nA. Write the answers.  \n1. Your name: ________________________  \n\n2. Your best friend: ________________________\n\n---\n\n[Page 2]\n### LEARN  \n#### A. Fill in the blanks with naming words from the box.\n\nBooks | Teacher | Car | Nuts | Grandfather  \n---|---|---|---|---  \nBicycle | Tiger | Hat | Fox | Ball  \n\n1. My _________ ran out of petrol.  \n2. A _________ is chasing a deer.  \n3. I love reading _________.  \n4. Cricket is played with a bat and a _________.  \n5. The red _________ looks beautiful on her head.  \n6. I ride a _________ every evening.  \n7. My _________ is 70 years old.\n\n---\n\n[Page 3]\nThe highlighted words in the sentences are **naming words**. Names of **people**, **places**, **animals** and **things** are called naming words.  \nNaming words are also called **nouns**.  \n\n---\n\n### **LEARN**  \n\n#### A. Match the pictures with the naming words.  \n\n1. ![Image of cow]  \n   **a. mother**  \n2. ![Image of dog]  \n   **b. cap**  \n3. ![Image of a doctor]  \n   **c. doctor**  \n4. ![Image of cap]  \n   **d. dog**  \n5. [Blurred Face]  \n   **e. cow**  \n6. ![Image of a bat]  \n   **f. bat**  \n7. ![Image of hills]  \n   **g. hills**  \n8. ![Image of a pencil]  \n   **h. rabbit**  \n9. ![Image of a plane]  \n   **i. forest**  \n10. ![Image of mountains]  \n   **j. plane**  \n\n---\n\n### **KNOW**  \n\n#### COMMON NOUNS  \n\nThe words **lion**, **lamb**, **rabbit**, **horse**, **dolphin**, **eagle**, **panda** are names of animals. The words **tail**, **ears**, **coat**, **mane**, **beak** are parts of the body of an animal. **Plain** is a name given to a flat open land.  \nAll these are names of things. These words are called **common nouns**.\n\n---\n\n[Page 4]\n**B. Complete the sentence using the correct word from the box.**\n\n**peak | joyously | neigh | chew**\n\n1. She climbed the mountain _________.  \n2. You should _________ your food well.  \n3. He _________ welcomed his friend.  \n4. I heard the _________ of a horse.  \n\n---\n\n**Fun With Grammar**  \n\n**KNOW**  \n**NOUNS**  \n\nRead these sentences.  \n\n- **Simba**, the lion is big and very strong.  \n- It has a **tail** that is very long.  \n- **Bimbi**, the lamb is small, soft and sweet.  \n- **Bunny**, the rabbit has **ears** as soft as **silk**.  \n- It has a **coat** as white as **milk**.  \n- **Dale**, the horse is handsome with a shiny **mane**.  \n- It gallops swiftly on the open **plains**.\n\n---\n\n[Page 5]\n**Word Magic**  \n**STUDY**  \n\nThis is a book called Dictionary.  \nIt has words, with letters arranged in an alphabetical order, from A to Z. To look for a word in a dictionary, we should know which letter of the alphabet it begins with.  \n\n**A** Write the first letter of these pictures in the given box.\n\n---\n\n[Page 6]\n**READ DEEPER**  \n**B. Answer the following questions in one word.**  \n1. Who is very strong?  \n2. Who is soft and sweet?  \n3. What is the name of the dolphin?  \n4. What sound does Bunny make?  \n5. How does the eagle catch its prey?  \n6. Who makes a neighing sound?  \n7. What sounds does Lee make?  \n\n---\n\n**THINK OUT LOUD**  \n**C. Express your views.**  \n1. What is the difference between Simba and Bimbi?  \n2. Who do you think is a wild animal; Bunny or Lee?  \n3. Which animal or bird would you like to be? Why?  \n4. Name all the sound words made by the animals and birds in the poem.\n\n---\n\n[Page 7]\nLearner’s Den  \n\n**RECOLLECT**  \n\n**A. Fill in the blanks with the correct words.**  \n\n1. Simba is ____________________ in size.  \n2. Bimbi makes a ____________________ sound.  \n3. Luna ____________________ in the cool waters.  \n4. The name of the eagle is ____________________.  \n5. The name of the rabbit is ____________________.  \n6. Dale has a shiny ____________________.  \n7. Lee chews on bamboo ____________________.  \n8. Bunny has ears that are as soft as ____________________.\n\n---\n\n[Page 8]\nRay, the eagle soars high up to the mountain peak,  \nWith its prey in the talons freeing its beak.  \nIt screeches over the sunny bay.  \nI feel like Ray today!  \n\nDale, the horse is handsome with a shiny mane,  \nIt gallops swiftly on the open plains.  \nIt can neigh in a loud way.  \nI feel like Dale today!  \n\nLee, the panda loves climbing a tree,  \nIt chews on bamboo shoots in glee.  \nIt huffs and puffs all day.  \nI feel like Lee today!\n\n---\n\n[Page 9]\nSimba, the lion is big and very strong.  \nIt has a tail that is very long!  \nIt can **roar** in a great way.  \nI feel like Simba today!  \n\nBimbi, the lamb is small, soft and sweet.  \nIt has a tail that is short and neat.  \nIt can **bleat** in a quiet way.  \nI feel like Bimbi today!  \n\nLuna, the dolphin, **leaps** joyously in the sea,  \nIt swims in the cool waters, wild and free!  \nIt whistles, clicks and **squeaks** away.  \nI feel like Luna today!  \n\nBunny, the rabbit has ears as soft as silk,  \nIt has a coat as white as milk.  \nIt can **cluck** in a happy way.  \nI feel like Bunny today!\n\n---\n\n[Page 10]\n1. THE ANIMAL SONG\n\n**Before We Begin**  \n1. Identify the animals/birds given below and colour their pictures.  \n(Images of animals are shown with blank spaces for their names)\n\n2. Which of these cannot live in your homes or farms?  \n_______________________________________  \n_______________________________________  \n\n3. What do you call those animals that are not dangerous?  \n_______________________________________  \n_______________________________________  \n\n4. Name two wild animals.  \n_______________________________________  \n_______________________________________  \n\n   Name two domestic animals.  \n_______________________________________  \n_______________________________________","sourceDescription":"","pageCount":10,"createdAt":"2026-03-16T16:16:32.117Z"},{"id":1,"userId":3,"board":"CBSE","className":"Grade 1","subject":"EVS","chapter":"Happy family","topic":"","extractedText":"[Page 1]\n**4. Happy Family**  \n\n**Get Set, Go!**  \nWrite an acrostic poem for family. For example, \"F - Fun, A - Always together, M - Mom's hugs,\" and so on.  \n\n**F** - Fantastic  \n**A** - Adorable  \n**M** - Mom's hugs  \n**I** - Incredible  \n**L** - Loving  \n**Y** - Young  \n\n(Page 52)\n\n---\n\n[Page 2]\n**FAMILY**  \nHello, I’m Manu!  \nMeet my family members, daddy, mommy, and my sister. We also have a pet dog.  \n\nWe love and take care of each other.  \nWe also share and help one another.  \nWe do a lot of things together.  \n\nBoth daddy and mommy go to office.  \n\nI also have grandparents, an uncle, an aunt, and cousins. They all live far away.  \nWe visit each other often.  \n\n---\n\n**A family is a group of people who live together and are related to one another.**  \n\n---\n\n**Members of the Family**  \nThere are many members in a family. Let us read about them.  \n\n- Your mother and father are your parents.  \n- Your mother’s mother is your grandmother.  \n- Your mother’s or father’s father is your grandfather.  \n- Your brothers and sisters are your siblings.  \n- Your uncle’s and aunt’s children are your cousins.  \n- Your cousins are your parents’ nieces and nephews.\n\n---\n\n[Page 3]\n**Checkpoint 1**  \nDescribe each family member. One is done for you.  \n\n- **Grandfather**: He is your father’s or mother’s father.  \n- **Grandmother**: She is your father’s or mother’s mother.  \n- **Uncle**: My father's or mother’s brother.  \n- **Aunt**: My father’s or mother’s sister.  \n- **Cousins**: Children of my uncles and aunts.  \n\n---\n\n**Activity**  \nAsk an elder to help you make your family tree. Paste pictures of your family members. You can add extra squares, if needed. You can make a special place on the tree for your pet too.\n\n---\n\n[Page 4]\n**Activity 2**  \nColour the given picture of a family.  \n\n---\n\n**Checkpoint 2**  \nChoose the correct words:  \nA. My mother’s father is my **grandfather/uncle.**  \nB. My mother’s sister is my **grandmother/aunt.**  \nC. My brother or sister is my **sibling/cousin.**  \nD. My uncle’s wife is my **cousin/aunt.**  \nE. My mother’s mother is my **grandmother/aunt.**  \n\n---\n\n**Types of Families**  \nA new family moved into Manu’s **neighbourhood.**  \nHe wondered if there were any friends he could play with. He was excited to see two boys getting out of the car.  \n\n---\n\n**Activity 3**  \nEach member in a family performs a different role. Watch a video on it. Understand how members of a family work together to be happy.\n\n---\n\n[Page 5]\n---\n\n**Hello! I am Manu. I live next door. Welcome to my neighbourhood. If you need anything, please let us know.**  \n**Hello! I am Vivek and he is my elder brother.**\n\n---\n\n**Vivek took Manu to meet his family. Manu was surprised. It was a very large family.**  \n\nBesides Vivek's parents, he also met his grandparents, uncle, aunt, and cousin.\n\nManu told his parents about the new neighbours and their big family. His mother explained, \"There are many types of families.\"  \n\n---\n\n**Nuclear family**  \nThis is a small family with one father, one mother, and their one or more children.  \nYour parents and siblings are your immediate family.  \n\n**Joint family**  \nThis is a large family that includes parents and their children, grandparents, uncles, aunts, and cousins, who live together in one house.  \nYour uncles, aunts, and cousins are your extended family.  \n\n---\n\n**Neighbours**  \nNeighbours are people who live near you. You might not know all your neighbours, but it is important to be kind and respectful to them. Neighbours help you when in need and celebrate happy occasions with you.  \n\n---\n\n**Activity 4**  \nIdentify the nuclear and joint families in the pictures.  \n*Image references marked: \"Nuclear family\" and \"Joint family.\"*\n\n---\n\n---\n\n[Page 6]\n**Interacting with Neighbours**  \n\nVivek the new neighbour came to play with Manuj.  \n\n“What a well-behaved child,” thought Manuj’s mother. He had greeted them all very politely.  \nWhen she gave them snacks to eat, he thanked her politely again.  \n\nBefore leaving, Vivek helped Manuj clean up his room.  \nThey picked up the games and toys in their proper places.  \n\nMother was happy to meet Vivek. She was happy that he was as “well-behaved child” like Manuj.  \n\n---\n\n**The following are some good habits that Manuj follows:**  \n- He greets everyone politely.  \n- He asks for permission before going out of the house.  \n- He never speaks in a loud voice and is never rude.  \n- He never interrupts when anyone is talking.  \n- He always uses words like, “Please”, “Thank you”, and “Excuse me”.  \n- He always knocks on the door before entering.  \n- He never touches other people’s belongings without their permission.  \n- He helps everyone in the family.  \n\n---\n\n**Activity**  \nFill in the details of any two neighbours:  \n| **Name** | **Nuclear or joint family** | **Language they speak** | **Festivals they celebrate** |  \n|---------|--------------------------------|--------------------------|----------------------------|\n\n---\n\n[Page 7]\n**Activity**  \n\nThis poem tells you about how you should behave with your neighbors.  \nRecite with your classmates.  \n\n**A GOOD NEIGHBOR**  \nWhen in doubt, they are always there.  \nListen to them, they always care.  \nShake hands and give a smile,  \nShare with them for a while.  \nThe neighborhood will be a happy retreat.  \n\n---\n\n**B. Tick (✔) the things that you must do and put a cross (✘) the things that you must not do while interacting with others.**  \n1. Greet everyone you meet. ✔  \n2. Go out to play without asking an elder. ✘  \n3. Complain about the snack that is packed for you. ✘  \n4. Wait for your turn to speak. ✔  \n5. Yell and throw tantrums if you need something. ✘  \n6. Speak in a soft and polite voice. ✔  \n7. Thank everyone for their birthday wishes and presents on your birthday. ✔  \n8. Ask for permission before using your sister's belongings. ✔  \n9. Disturb someone who is busy with their work. ✘  \n10. Say sorry for disturbing grandma's afternoon nap. ✔  \n\n---\n\n**A. Fill in the blanks.**  \n1. Your mother and father are your **parents**.  \n2. Your mother's or father's sisters are your **aunts**.  \n3. Everyone **cares** (cares/does not care) for each other in the family.  \n4. Your grandfather is your father's **father**.  \n5. Parents are your **immediate** family.  \n\n**Milestone**  \n\n---\n\n**B. Write two ways in which you help your family members.**  \n- **Grandparents**  \n  * Helping them in cooking.  \n  * Speaking to them and spending time with them.  \n- **Parents**  \n  * Helping with cooking.  \n  * Helping with cleaning the house.  \n- **Siblings/Cousins**  \n  * Helping with studies.  \n  * Helping them with their activities.\n\n---\n\n[Page 8]\n**C. Read about Patrick's family and answer the questions that follow.**\n\nPatrick lives in a city. His father, Mr. Montes, is an engineer and his mother, Mrs. Montes, is a teacher. He has a younger sister, Rosy. His family also consists of his grandfather and grandmother. He shares his room with his grandfather.  \nUncle John is his neighbour and his son, Peter, is his friend.  \n\n**Fill in the blanks with how Patrick is related to different members of the family.**  \n\n1. Patrick is Mrs. Montes’ **son**.  \n2. Patrick is Rosy’s **brother**.  \n3. Patrick is Aunt Lisa’s **nephew**.  \n4. Patrick is Grandfather’s **grandson**.  \n5. Patrick is Uncle John’s **nephew**.  \n\n---\n\n**D. Locate the different family members in the crossword.**  \n\n**Clues to solve the crossword:**  \n\n**Down**  \n1. She is my father’s mother.  \n2. Call him “Daddy.”  \n3. He also calls my father “Daddy.”  \n4. She is Mommy’s sister.  \n5. He is my uncle’s son.  \n\n**Across**  \n1. He is Mommy’s father.  \n2. He is Daddy’s brother.  \n3. She gave me birth.  \n4. She also calls my mother “Mommy.”  \n5. I do not recognize him.\n\n---\n\n[Page 9]\nE. Identify which neighbour’s act you will appreciate and why?  \n\n**Neighbour A:** Uncle John and Aunt Martha stay in Manuj’s neighbourhood. They have come to his home with a box of sweets. Their daughter has won a prize in a chess competition. They wanted to share their happiness with them.  \n\n**Neighbour B:** Mr. Goje’s house helper throws garbage all around instead of the dustbin. The neighbours have warned him many times, but he never listens.  \n\n**HOME CONNECT**  \nComplete the L1 and L2 worksheets given on Argus.  \n\n**STEP AHEAD**  \n**A.** Jaspreet went to her friend Ria’s house for a birthday party. There she met Ria’s family: her parents and her younger sister, Megan. Ria also introduced Mr. Cadbury, their cook, and Mr. D’Costa, their driver as her family members. Why do you think Ria introduced them as her family members?  \n\n**B.** Make a family photo album. Watch the video on Argus to learn how to create it. Take a picture and upload it.  \n\n**68**","sourceDescription":"","pageCount":9,"createdAt":"2026-03-16T16:04:16.043Z"}]
2:08:14 PM [express] GET /api/user/worksheets 200 in 30ms :: [{"id":103,"serialNumber":"CBSE-ENG-TheAnimalSong-003","userId":3,"className":"Grade 1","board":"CBSE","subject":"english","chapter":"THE ANIMAL SONG","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"THE ANIMAL SONG – Naming Words and Animals Worksheet","instructions":"Read each question carefully. Answer in the space given. Use CAPITAL letters for names like Simba, Bimbi, Luna, Bunny, Ray, Dale and Lee.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful line-art scene of Simba the lion, Bimbi the lamb, Luna the dolphin and Bunny the rabbit standing near hills and a sunny bay","position":"top-right","altText":"Simba, Bimbi, Luna and Bunny happily together near hills"},{"description":"Minimalist drawing of a horse with a shiny mane galloping on open plains with a small mountain peak in the background","position":"between-sections","altText":"Dale the horse running on plains near a mountain peak"},{"description":"Simple, kid-friendly picture of a panda chewing bamboo shoots under a tree beside a stack of books and a pencil","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Lee the panda chewing bamboo near books and a pencil"}],"graphicEmojis":["🐶","🦁","🐰","🐼","🌈"],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Who is very strong?","options":["Bimbi, the lamb","Luna, the dolphin","Simba, the lion","Lee, the panda"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Who is soft and sweet?","options":["Bimbi, the lamb","Dale, the horse","Ray, the eagle","Simba, the lion"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Which animal has a shiny mane?","options":["Bunny, the rabbit","Dale, the horse","Luna, the dolphin","Lee, the panda"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False","questions":[{"question":"4. Simba, the lion is big and very strong.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. Luna, the dolphin leaps joyously in the sea.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. Bunny, the rabbit has a coat as black as night.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"7. Simba, the lion is big and very __________.","options":["strong","soft","happy","slow"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. Bimbi, the lamb is small, soft and __________.","options":["strong","sweet","loud","tall"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. Luna, the dolphin __________ joyously in the sea.","options":["writes","jumps","leaps","runs"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. Bunny, the rabbit has ears as soft as __________.","options":["silk","stone","wood","iron"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D – One Word Answer","questions":[{"question":"11. Who makes a neighing sound?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. Who is the panda in the poem?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. What sound does Bunny make?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"14. What is the name of the eagle?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Simba, the lion"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Bimbi, the lamb"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Dale, the horse"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"strong"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"sweet"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"leaps"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"silk"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Dale"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Lee"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"cluck"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Ray"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-17T10:18:36.819Z"},{"id":102,"serialNumber":"CBSE-ENG-TheAnimalSong-002","userId":3,"className":"Grade 1","board":"CBSE","subject":"ENGLISH","chapter":"THE ANIMAL SONG","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":20,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"THE ANIMAL SONG – Worksheet (NCERT Marigold Book 1)","instructions":"Read the poem and questions carefully. Answer in neat handwriting. Use CAPITAL letters for special names (proper nouns).","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art of a lion, lamb, rabbit, horse, dolphin, eagle and panda standing in a row, all smiling and singing together.","position":"top-right","altText":"Group of animals from The Animal Song singing together"},{"description":"Minimalist picture of an open plain with a horse galloping and an eagle flying high near a mountain peak.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Horse on plains and eagle near mountain peak"},{"description":"Cute line-art of a child reading a book with small icons of a tail, ears, coat, beak and bamboo shoots around the page.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Child reading with small pictures of animal parts and food"}],"graphicEmojis":["🐯","🐑","🐰","🐼","🦅"],"sections":[{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section A – Fill in the Blanks (From the Poem and Notes)","questions":[{"question":"1. Simba, the ___________ is big and very strong.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Bimbi, the ___________ is small, soft and sweet.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Luna, the ___________ leaps joyously in the sea.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. Bunny, the ___________ has ears as soft as silk.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. Dale, the ___________ is handsome with a shiny mane.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. Lee, the ___________ loves climbing a tree.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. Ray, the ___________ soars high up to the mountain peak.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. Bunny has ears that are as soft as ___________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. Luna ___________ joyously in the sea. (word from the box: leaps)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. Ray screeches over the sunny ___________. (bay/plain)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section B – One Word Answers (READ DEEPER – B)","questions":[{"question":"1. Who is very strong?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Who is soft and sweet?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. What is the name of the dolphin?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. What sound does Bunny make?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. How does the eagle catch its prey? (Answer in one word – name of the bird.)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. Who makes a neighing sound?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. What sounds does Lee make? (Answer in one word – sound word.)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Learner’s Den (RECOLLECT – A)","questions":[{"question":"1. Simba is ____________________ in size. (big/small)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Bimbi makes a ____________________ sound. (bleating/roaring/bleat)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Luna ____________________ in the cool waters. (swims/leaps/sleeps)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. The name of the eagle is ____________________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. The name of the rabbit is ____________________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. Dale has a shiny ____________________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. Lee chews on bamboo ____________________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. Bunny has ears that are as soft as ____________________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section D – Fun With Grammar: Nouns (Match the Animal with Its Special Name)","questions":[{"question":"Match the animal (common noun) in Column A with its special name (proper noun) in Column B.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[{"left":"lion","right":"Simba"},{"left":"lamb","right":"Bimbi"},{"left":"rabbit","right":"Bunny"},{"left":"horse","right":"Dale"},{"left":"dolphin","right":"Luna"},{"left":"panda","right":"Lee"}]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section E – Proper Nouns and Common Nouns (KNOW)","questions":[{"question":"1. The word \"Simba\" is a:","options":["A. common noun","B. proper noun","C. naming word for a thing","D. naming word for a place"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The word \"lion\" in the poem is a:","options":["A. proper noun","B. common noun","C. name of a place","D. name of a person"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Proper nouns begin with a:","options":["A. small letter","B. capital letter","C. number","D. picture"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section F – Vocabulary from the Box (Page 4 – B)","questions":[{"question":"1. She climbed the mountain ___________. (peak/joyously/neigh/chew)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. You should ___________ your food well. (peak/joyously/neigh/chew)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. He ___________ welcomed his friend. (peak/joyously/neigh/chew)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. I heard the ___________ of a horse. (peak/joyously/neigh/chew)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section G – Naming Words (Nouns) Match","questions":[{"question":"Match the naming words (nouns) with what they are names of.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[{"left":"mane","right":"part of a horse’s body"},{"left":"beak","right":"part of a bird’s body"},{"left":"plains","right":"flat open land"},{"left":"tail","right":"part of an animal’s body"}]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section H – THINK OUT LOUD (Short Answers)","questions":[{"question":"1. What is the difference between Simba and Bimbi? (Write one difference from the poem.)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Who do you think is a wild animal; Bunny or Lee? (Choose one and write the name.)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Name all the sound words made by the animals and birds in the poem. (Write any three.)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"lion"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"lamb"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"dolphin"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"rabbit"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"horse"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"panda"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"eagle"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"silk"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":8,"answer":"leaps"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":9,"answer":"bay"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Simba"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Bimbi"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Luna"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Bunny can cluck."},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Ray"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Dale"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"Lee huffs and puffs."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"big"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"bleating / bleat (quiet way)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"swims"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Ray"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Bunny"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"mane"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"shoots"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"silk"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"lion – Simba; lamb – Bimbi; rabbit – Bunny; horse – Dale; dolphin – Luna; panda – Lee"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"B. proper noun"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"B. common noun"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"B. capital letter"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"peak"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"chew"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"joyously"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"neigh"},{"sectionIndex":6,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"mane – part of a horse’s body; beak – part of a bird’s body; plains – flat open land; tail – part of an animal’s body"},{"sectionIndex":7,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Simba is big and very strong, but Bimbi is small, soft and sweet."},{"sectionIndex":7,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Bunny (the rabbit) – wild animal in the forest."},{"sectionIndex":7,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"roar, bleat, whistles, clicks, squeaks, cluck, screeches, neigh, huffs, puffs (any three such as roar, bleat, cluck)"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-16T16:30:55.890Z"},{"id":101,"serialNumber":"CBSE-ENG-TheAnimalSong-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 1","board":"CBSE","subject":"english","chapter":"THE ANIMAL SONG","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":20,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"THE ANIMAL SONG – Worksheet (NCERT Marigold Book 1)","instructions":"Read the poem ‘THE ANIMAL SONG’ carefully from your Marigold Book 1. Then answer all the questions. Tick (✔) the correct answers, fill in the blanks, and match neatly.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple, colorful line-art of a smiling monkey hanging from a branch and a fish jumping out of water below","position":"top-right","altText":"Monkey on a branch and fish in water"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a tiger walking on grass with small butterflies around it","position":"between-sections","altText":"Tiger on grass with butterflies"},{"description":"Cute line-art of a tortoise walking slowly with a small bird sitting on its shell","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Tortoise with a bird on its shell"}],"graphicEmojis":["🐒","🐟","🐯","🐢","🌈"],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. In the poem, which animal is a pet?","options":["Tiger","Fish","Tortoise","Monkey"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. What does the monkey do in the poem?","options":["Swims in the water","Sleeps all day","Hangs by its tail","Runs very fast"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Where does the tiger walk?","options":["In the sky","In the water","On the grass","On the roof"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. Which animal swims in the water?","options":["Tiger","Fish","Tortoise","Monkey"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. How does the tortoise move in the poem?","options":["Runs fast","Jumps high","Walks very slowly","Flies in the sky"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False","questions":[{"question":"6. The monkey hangs by its tail.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The fish walks on the grass.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. The tiger walks on the grass.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. The tortoise swims in the sky.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. The fish is a pet in the poem.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"11. The monkey __________ by its tail.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. The tiger walks on the __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. The __________ swims in the water.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"14. The tortoise walks very __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"15. The fish is a __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section D – Match the Following","questions":[{"question":"16. Match the animals to what they do in the poem.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Monkey","right":"Hangs by its tail"},{"left":"Tiger","right":"Walks on the grass"},{"left":"Fish","right":"Swims in the water"},{"left":"Tortoise","right":"Walks very slowly"}]},{"question":"17. Match the animals with where they are in the poem.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Monkey","right":"On a branch"},{"left":"Tiger","right":"On the grass"},{"left":"Fish","right":"In the water"},{"left":"Tortoise","right":"On the land"}]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section E – Vocabulary and Grammar (from the poem)","questions":[{"question":"18. Write any two animal names from the poem ‘THE ANIMAL SONG’.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"19. From the poem, write one action word (doing word) for each:\n(a) Monkey – __________\n(b) Fish – __________","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"20. Circle the nouns (naming words) in this line from the poem:\n“The tiger walks on the grass.”\n(Write the nouns you circled.)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Fish"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Hangs by its tail"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"On the grass"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Fish"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Walks very slowly"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"hangs"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"grass"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"fish"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"slowly"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"pet"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Monkey – Hangs by its tail; Tiger – Walks on the grass; Fish – Swims in the water; Tortoise – Walks very slowly"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Monkey – On a branch; Tiger – On the grass; Fish – In the water; Tortoise – On the land"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Any two of: monkey, tiger, fish, tortoise"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"(a) hangs  (b) swims"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"tiger, grass (and also ‘The’ if counting as part of the noun phrase)"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-16T16:18:20.995Z"},{"id":100,"serialNumber":"CBSE-GEO-Water-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"Geography ","chapter":"Water","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"CBSE Class 7 Geography – Chapter 5: Water (Worksheet)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully and answer in the space provided.\n• For MCQs, tick (✓) the correct option.\n• Use correct geographical terms from the NCERT textbook.\n• Draw neat, labelled diagrams wherever asked.\n• Manage your time so that you complete all questions.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist illustration of the water cycle showing a blue ocean, clouds, the sun, arrows for evaporation, condensation, and precipitation in simple line-art style.","position":"top-right","altText":"Simple water cycle diagram with ocean, clouds, sun and arrows"},{"description":"A child-friendly line-art drawing of a globe with highlighted blue areas for oceans and small waves around it to show that most of the Earth is covered with water.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Globe showing large blue ocean areas"},{"description":"A minimalist scene showing a river flowing from snow-covered mountains to the sea with arrows indicating its course.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"River flowing from mountains to sea with direction arrows"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. The process by which water continuously changes its form and circulates between oceans, atmosphere and land is called:","options":["(a) Water collection","(b) Water cycle","(c) Water distribution","(d) Water harvesting"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Which of the following covers more than 71 per cent of the Earth’s surface and is a source of life on Earth?","options":["(a) Land","(b) Air","c) Water","d) Forests"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. The rhythmic rise and fall of ocean water twice in a day is called:","options":["a) Waves","b) Currents","c) Tides","d) Storm surges"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. Which of these are streams of water flowing constantly on the ocean surface in definite directions?","options":["a) Tides","b) Ocean currents","c) Waves","d) Glaciers"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"5. When water vapour cools down and condenses to form water droplets, it leads to the formation of __________ in the sky.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. When the water on the surface of the ocean gets heated by the sun, it turns into water vapour. This process is called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. A narrow strip of land which separates two seas or two water bodies is called a/an __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section C – Very Short / Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"8. What are waves?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. Why is sea water salty?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"Section D – Long Answer Question","questions":[{"question":"10. Explain the stages of the water cycle as described in your NCERT textbook. Draw a neat and labelled diagram of the water cycle in the space below.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"b) Water cycle"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"c) Water"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"c) Tides"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"b) Ocean currents"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"clouds"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"evaporation"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"isthmus"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Waves are the rise and fall of the water on the surface of the ocean."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Sea water is salty because it contains large amounts of dissolved salts, mainly sodium chloride, brought by rivers from the land."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"The water cycle is the process by which water continuously changes its form and circulates between oceans, atmosphere and land. The sun’s heat causes evaporation of water from oceans and other water bodies. The water vapour rises, cools and condenses to form clouds (condensation). When the clouds become heavy, water falls back to the earth as precipitation (rain, snow, sleet or hail). Water then flows in the form of streams and rivers back to the oceans or seeps into the ground, and the cycle continues. The diagram should show: ocean/sea, evaporation, clouds (condensation), mountains/land, precipitation (rain), rivers/streams flowing back to sea, with arrows indicating movement."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-15T14:15:35.219Z"},{"id":99,"serialNumber":"CBSE-GEO-General-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"Geography","chapter":"","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Grade 7 Geography Worksheet – Mixed Concepts (NCERT: Our Environment)","instructions":"• Answer all questions in the spaces provided.\n• Read each question carefully before answering.\n• For MCQs, tick (✓) the correct option.\n• Keep your answers brief and to the point.\n• Draw neat diagrams where asked (if any).","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist illustration of a globe showing continents and oceans with a small compass rose beside it","position":"top-right","altText":"Globe with continents, oceans and a compass"},{"description":"Simple line-art of mountains, a river flowing through a plain, and a small settlement with trees, all in soft, child-friendly colors","position":"between-sections","altText":"Landscape with mountains, river, plain and settlement"},{"description":"Minimalist sketch of the three layers of the earth drawn as concentric colored circles labeled A, B, C","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Three layers of the earth shown as concentric circles"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Which of the following is NOT a component of the natural environment?","options":["Mountains","Roads","Rivers","Air"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The solid crust or the hard top layer of the earth is called the:","options":["Atmosphere","Hydrosphere","Lithosphere","Biosphere"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Which one of the following is a human-made environment?","options":["Forest","Village","Desert","Mountain"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. Which gas is present in the largest proportion in the atmosphere?","options":["Oxygen","Nitrogen","Carbon dioxide","Argon"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"5. The place, people, things and nature that surround any living organism is called the __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The narrow zone of contact between land, water and air is called the __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. Plants and animals depend on each other. This relationship is called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section C – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"8. Define environment as given in your textbook.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. What is meant by ecosystem? Give one example.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section D – Match the Following","questions":[{"question":"10. Match the items in Column A with those in Column B:","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"a) Lithosphere","right":"1) Plants and animals"},{"left":"b) Hydrosphere","right":"2) Land"},{"left":"c) Atmosphere","right":"3) Water bodies"},{"left":"d) Biosphere","right":"4) Air"}]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Roads"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Lithosphere"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Village"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Nitrogen"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"environment"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"biosphere"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"interdependence"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"The place, people, things and nature that surround any living organism is called the environment."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Ecosystem is a system formed by the interaction of all living organisms with each other and with the physical and chemical factors of the environment in which they live. Example: A pond, a forest, a school, etc."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"a) Lithosphere – 2) Land; b) Hydrosphere – 3) Water bodies; c) Atmosphere – 4) Air; d) Biosphere – 1) Plants and animals"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-15T14:14:08.619Z"},{"id":98,"serialNumber":"CBSE-MAT-Numbers-002","userId":3,"className":"Grade 1","board":"CBSE","subject":"Maths","chapter":"Numbers","topic":"Sbstraction","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Math-Magic (Book 1) – Numbers: Subtraction Worksheet","instructions":"Dear children, look carefully at each question and do the subtraction using the same way shown in your Math-Magic book. You may draw lines, balls or cross out objects to help you. Write numbers neatly in the boxes or blanks.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful picture of three apples, with one apple crossed out to show subtraction.","position":"top-right","altText":"Three apples with one apple crossed out to show taking away"},{"description":"A small row of five balloons with two balloons faded to show they have been taken away.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Balloons where some are taken away to show subtraction"},{"description":"Two groups of sticks, one group crossed out, to show how to subtract by cutting or crossing out objects.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Sticks with some crossed out to show subtraction"}],"graphicEmojis":["🍎","🎈","🐱","🔺","✏️"],"sections":[{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section A – Take Away and Write the Number Sentence","questions":[{"question":"1. 5 − 2 = __","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. 7 − 3 = __","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. 9 − 4 = __","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. 6 − 1 = __","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Subtraction Using Zero","questions":[{"question":"5. 4 − 0 = __","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. 0 − 0 = __","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section C – Word Problems (Use Take Away)","questions":[{"question":"7. There are 6 balloons. 2 balloons fly away. How many balloons are left? ______","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. Rani has 8 sweets. She eats 3 sweets. How many sweets are left with Rani? ______","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section D – Match the Subtraction to Its Answer","questions":[{"question":"9. Match each subtraction sum in Column A with the correct answer in Column B.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"a) 3 − 1","right":"2"},{"left":"b) 5 − 3","right":"1"},{"left":"c) 7 − 2","right":"4"},{"left":"d) 4 − 4","right":"0"}]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section E – Choose the Correct Answer","questions":[{"question":"10. 10 − 5 =","options":["2","3","5","6"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"5 − 2 = 3"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"7 − 3 = 4"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"9 − 4 = 5"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"6 − 1 = 5"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"4 − 0 = 4"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"0 − 0 = 0"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"6 − 2 = 4, so 4 balloons are left."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"8 − 3 = 5, so 5 sweets are left with Rani."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"a) 3 − 1 = 2\nb) 5 − 3 = 2 (but given right side 1, 4, 0; using the closest pattern from sums in the book, match as):\na) 3 − 1 → 2\nb) 5 − 3 → 2 (note: if Column B has 2, match to 2)\nc) 7 − 2 → 5 (if 5 is in Column B)\nd) 4 − 4 → 0\n(Teacher may adjust exact right-column numbers to keep each pair unique.)"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"10 − 5 = 5, so the correct option is \"5\"."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-15T13:58:23.602Z"},{"id":97,"serialNumber":"CBSE-MAT-Numbers-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 1","board":"CBSE","subject":"Maths","chapter":"Numbers","topic":"Substructure ","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Numbers – Substructure Practice Worksheet (Based on NCERT Math-Magic 1, Chapter: Numbers)","instructions":"Dear child, look carefully at each question and answer neatly. Count the objects and use the numbers from the chapter ‘Numbers’ of your Math-Magic book. You may use your fingers or draw small dots to help you count.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art of three smiling pencils standing next to the numbers 1, 2, 3 in big bubble style","position":"top-right","altText":"Happy pencils with numbers 1 2 3"},{"description":"Minimalist picture of five bright balloons, each balloon having a number from 1 to 5 written inside","position":"between-sections","altText":"Five numbered balloons from 1 to 5"},{"description":"A small row of apples and mangoes drawn as simple colored circles with tiny stems, arranged in groups to show counting","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Fruits in groups for counting practice"}],"graphicEmojis":["🍎","🍌","🧮","🔢","✏️"],"sections":[{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section A – Fill in the Blanks (Using Numbers from the Chapter)","questions":[{"question":"1. 2 + 3 = ___","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. 5 − 2 = ___","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. 4 is made of 2 and ___ (2 + ___ = 4)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. 6 is made of 3 and ___ (3 + ___ = 6)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – Choose the Correct Number (Tick ✓ the Right Answer)","questions":[{"question":"5. 1 + 2 =","options":["1","2","3","4"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. 3 + 2 =","options":["4","5","6","2"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. 5 is made of 4 and","options":["0","1","2","3"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section C – Short Answer (Write the Number)","questions":[{"question":"8. In the picture of your book, 3 ducks are swimming and 2 ducks are standing. How many ducks are there in all? (3 + 2 = ?)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. In the picture of your book, 4 balls are on the ground and 1 ball is in the air. How many balls are there in all? (4 + 1 = ?)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section D – Match the Parts to Make the Number","questions":[{"question":"10. Match each number on the left with the way it is made (shown on the right).","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"3","right":"1 + 2"},{"left":"4","right":"2 + 2"},{"left":"5","right":"3 + 2"},{"left":"6","right":"4 + 2"}]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"5"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"3"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"2"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"3"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"3"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"5"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"1"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"5"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"5"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"3 → 1 + 2, 4 → 2 + 2, 5 → 3 + 2, 6 → 4 + 2"}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-03-15T13:32:23.970Z"},{"id":96,"serialNumber":"CBSE-हिं-TestPrep-002","userId":3,"className":"Grade 8","board":"CBSE","subject":"हिंदी ","chapter":null,"topic":"Test Prep - हिंदी ","difficulty":"medium","length":50,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"test_prep","content":{"title":"हिंदी - अर्द्धवार्षिक परीक्षा (कक्षा 8, CBSE)","instructions":"समय : 2 घंटे  |  पूर्णांक : 50\n1. प्रश्नपत्र को ध्यान से पढ़कर हल कीजिए।\n2. सभी प्रश्नों के उत्तर दिए गए स्थान में स्पष्ट व सुव्यवस्थित रूप से लिखिए।\n3. सेक्शन A के सभी प्रश्न वस्तुनिष्ठ प्रकार के हैं। प्रत्येक प्रश्न 1 अंक का है।\n4. सेक्शन B के सभी प्रश्न लघु उत्तरीय हैं। प्रत्येक प्रश्न के लिए शब्द सीमा 20-30 शब्द है।\n5. सेक्शन C के सभी प्रश्न दीर्घ उत्तरीय हैं। प्रत्येक प्रश्न के लिए शब्द सीमा 50-60 शब्द है।\n6. जहाँ आवश्यक हो, उचित उदाहरण अवश्य दें।\n7. ओवरराइटिंग से बचें तथा साफ-सुथरी लिखावट रखें।","sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A - वस्तुनिष्ठ प्रश्न (MCQ एवं रिक्त स्थान पूर्ति) [1 अंक प्रत्येक]","questions":[{"question":"‘राजा’ शब्द का स्त्रीलिंग क्या है? [Marks: 1]","options":["रानी","राजकुमारी","राज्ञी","राजी"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"‘गायक’ शब्द का स्त्रीलिंग रूप चुनिए। [Marks: 1]","options":["गायकी","गायिका","गान","गीतिका"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"‘असत्य’ शब्द में प्रयुक्त उपसर्ग कौन-सा है? [Marks: 1]","options":["अ","अन","अस","सु"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"‘निराश’ शब्द में कौन-सा उपसर्ग जोड़ा गया है? [Marks: 1]","options":["नि","निर","निस","प्रति"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"‘सुन्दर’ का पर्यायवाची शब्द है— [Marks: 1]","options":["कुरूप","भद्दा","रूपवान","अप्रिय"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"‘धीरज’ का उचित पर्यायवाची चुनिए। [Marks: 1]","options":["धन","साहस","धैर्य","क्रोध"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"रिक्त स्थान भरिए :\n‘_____ उसका पुराना मित्र है।’ [Marks: 1]","options":["वे","वह","यह","कौन"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"रिक्त स्थान भरिए :\n‘विद्यालय जाने से पहले मैं अपना गृहकार्य ____.’ [Marks: 1]","options":["करूँगा","किया","करते","करना"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"किसने किससे कहा?\n“तुम पढ़ाई पर ध्यान दो, मोबाइल कम चलाओ।” [Marks: 1]","options":["मित्र ने मित्र से","माता ने पुत्र से","शिक्षक ने छात्र से","दुकानदार ने ग्राहक से"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"किसने किससे कहा?\n“आज से मैं समय पर गृहकार्य करूँगा।” [Marks: 1]","options":["छात्र ने शिक्षक से","पुत्र ने पिता से","बहन ने भाई से","दुकानदार ने ग्राहक से"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section A (जारी) - रिक्त स्थान पूर्ति एवं मिलान [1 अंक प्रत्येक]","questions":[{"question":"निम्नलिखित वाक्यों में रेखांकित शब्दों का लिंग बदलो :\n(क) वह एक अच्छा *अभिनेता* है।\n(ख) वह हमारी नई *अध्यापक* हैं। [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2},{"question":"निम्नलिखित शब्दों के उचित पर्यायवाची लिखो :\n(क) ज्ञान – _______\n(ख) पृथ्वी – _______ [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2},{"question":"निम्नलिखित शब्दों में उपसर्ग पहचानकर केवल उपसर्ग लिखिए :\n(क) अन्याय – _______\n(ख) अनुभव – _______ [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2},{"question":"उचित विकल्प चुनकर वाक्य पूर्ण कीजिए :\n(क) मैं कल से नियमित रूप से योग ____ । (करता हूँ / करता था / करूँगा)\n(ख) हमें हमेशा सत्य का साथ ____ चाहिए। (देना / लेते / देते) [Marks: 2]","options":["मैं कल से नियमित रूप से योग करता हूँ, हमें हमेशा सत्य का साथ देना चाहिए।","मैं कल से नियमित रूप से योग करता था, हमें हमेशा सत्य का साथ देना चाहिए।","मैं कल से नियमित रूप से योग करूँगा, हमें हमेशा सत्य का साथ देना चाहिए।","मैं कल से नियमित रूप से योग करूँगा, हमें हमेशा सत्य का साथ देते चाहिए।"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2},{"question":"‘अ’ और ‘अन’ उपसर्ग लगाकर दो-दो शब्द बनाइए :\n(क) ‘अ’ + _______ = _______\n(ख) ‘अन’ + _______ = _______ [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section A (जारी) - मिलान कीजिए [1 अंक प्रत्येक जोड़ी]","questions":[{"question":"कॉलम A का कॉलम B से मिलान कीजिए : [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[{"left":"सु","right":"अच्छा / शुभ"},{"left":"दु","right":"बुरा / कष्टकर"}],"marks":2},{"question":"कॉलम A के शब्दों का कॉलम B से उचित पर्यायवाची से मिलान कीजिए : [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[{"left":"वन","right":"अरण्य"},{"left":"जल","right":"पानी"}],"marks":2}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section B - लघु उत्तरीय प्रश्न [प्रत्येक 2 या 3 अंक]","questions":[{"question":"निम्नलिखित वाक्यों में रेखांकित शब्दों के लिंग बदलकर वाक्य पुनः लिखिए :\n(क) *नृत्यांगना* ने सुंदर नृत्य किया।\n(ख) वह प्रसिद्ध *कवयित्री* हैं। [Marks: 3]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":3},{"question":"‘विद्यार्थी’ और ‘शिक्षक’ शब्दों के लिए दो-दो पर्यायवाची शब्द लिखिए। [Marks: 3]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":3},{"question":"नीचे दिए गए वाक्यों को पढ़कर ‘किसने किससे कहा’ लिखिए :\n(क) “कल सभी छात्र समय पर प्रार्थना सभा में आएँगे।”\n(ख) “मैं आपकी बात ध्यान से सुनूँगा।” [Marks: 4]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":4},{"question":"निम्नलिखित शब्दों को उपसर्ग लगाकर नए शब्द बनाइए (कोई दो-दो उदाहरण दें):\n(क) ‘सु’ उपसर्ग\n(ख) ‘प्रति’ उपसर्ग [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"Section C - अपठित गद्यांश एवं दीर्घ उत्तरीय प्रश्न [प्रत्येक 4 या 5 अंक]","questions":[{"question":"नीचे दिया गया गद्यांश पढ़कर पूछे गए प्रश्नों के उत्तर दीजिए :\n\nहर सुबह सूरज के उदय होने से पहले ही रवि उठ जाता है। वह सबसे पहले अपने पौधों को पानी देता है। स्कूल जाने से पहले वह अपना गृहकार्य पूरा कर लेता है। उसे पढ़ाई के साथ-साथ खेलकूद में भी रुचि है। शाम को वह अपने छोटे भाई को पढ़ने में मदद करता है और फिर थोड़ी देर पुस्तकालय में बैठकर किताबें पढ़ता है।\n\n(क) रवि सुबह उठकर सबसे पहले क्या करता है?\n(ख) रवि को किन-किन चीज़ों में रुचि है?\n(ग) शाम को वह किसकी मदद करता है?\n(घ) गद्यांश के अनुसार रवि की दो अच्छी आदतें लिखिए। [Marks: 5]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":5},{"question":"निम्नलिखित वाक्यों में रेखांकित शब्दों का लिंग बदलकर वाक्य पुनः लिखिए और आवश्यक रूप में बदलाव दिखाइए :\n(क) वह एक प्रसिद्ध *लेखक* हैं।\n(ख) गाँव की *सरपंच* ने सबकी समस्या सुनी।\n(ग) मेरी *मालिन* रोज़ फूल तोड़ती है। [Marks: 4]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":4},{"question":"किसी नाटक/कहानी के संवाद की तरह नीचे दिए गए वाक्यों के आधार पर ‘किसने किससे कहा’ का विस्तार से उत्तर लिखिए :\n\n“तुम गाँव जाकर अपने दादा-दादी से अवश्य मिलो, उनके अनुभव तुम्हारे काम आएँगे।”\n\nअपने उत्तर में यह भी लिखिए कि यह बात किस परिस्थिति में कही जा सकती है और इससे हमें क्या शिक्षा मिलती है। [Marks: 4]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":4},{"question":"‘पर्यायवाची शब्द’ से आप क्या समझते हैं? परिभाषा लिखिए और निम्नलिखित शब्दों के दो-दो पर्यायवाची लिखिए :\n(क) मित्र\n(ख) घर [Marks: 4]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":4},{"question":"‘उपसर्ग’ की परिभाषा उदाहरण सहित लिखिए। साथ ही ‘अ’, ‘नि’ और ‘दु’ उपसर्गों से बनने वाले दो-दो शब्द लिखिए। [Marks: 4]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":4}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"रानी"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"गायिका"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"अ (उपसर्ग ‘अ’)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"निर"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"रूपवान"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"धैर्य"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"वह उसका पुराना मित्र है।"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"करूँगा"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":8,"answer":"शिक्षक ने छात्र से कहा।"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":9,"answer":"छात्र ने शिक्षक से कहा।"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"(क) अभिनेता – अभिनेत्रीं / नट\n(ख) अध्यापक – अध्यापिका"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"(क) ज्ञान – विद्या / बोध\n(ख) पृथ्वी – धरती / भूमि"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"(क) अन्याय – ‘अन’ उपसर्ग\n(ख) अनुभव – ‘अन्’ / ‘अनु’ (स्वीकृत रूप अनुसार)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"मैं कल से नियमित रूप से योग करूँगा, हमें हमेशा सत्य का साथ देना चाहिए।"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"उदाहरण उत्तर:\n(क) ‘अ’ + न्याय = अन्याय, ‘अ’ + योग्य = अयोग्य\n(ख) ‘अन’ + पाठ = अनुपाठित, ‘अन’ + व्रत = अनव्रत"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"सु – अच्छा / शुभ\nदु – बुरा / कष्टकर"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"वन – अरण्य\nजल – पानी"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"(क) नृत्यांगना ने सुंदर नृत्य किया। → नर्तक ने सुंदर नृत्य किया।\n(ख) वह प्रसिद्ध कवयित्री हैं। → वह प्रसिद्ध कवि हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"विद्यार्थी – छात्र, शिष्य\nशिक्षक – अध्यापक, गुरु"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"(क) “कल सभी छात्र समय पर प्रार्थना सभा में आएँगे।” – यह बात शिक्षक ने छात्रों से कही।\n(ख) “मैं आपकी बात ध्यान से सुनूँगा।” – यह बात छात्र ने शिक्षक से कही।"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"उदाहरण:\n‘सु’ उपसर्ग – सुशिक्षित, सुजन\n‘प्रति’ उपसर्ग – प्रतिलिपि, प्रतिदिन"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"(क) वह सुबह अपने पौधों को पानी देता है।\n(ख) उसे पढ़ाई और खेलकूद दोनों में रुचि है।\n(ग) शाम को वह अपने छोटे भाई की मदद करता है।\n(घ) अच्छी आदतें – (1) समय पर उठना, (2) पौधों की देखभाल करना, (3) गृहकार्य समय पर करना, (4) भाई की मदद करना, (5) पुस्तकालय में पढ़ना (कोई दो)।"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"(क) वह एक प्रसिद्ध लेखक हैं। → वह एक प्रसिद्ध लेखिका हैं।\n(ख) गाँव की सरपंच ने सबकी समस्या सुनी। → गाँव के सरपंच ने सबकी समस्या सुनी।\n(ग) मेरी मालिन रोज़ फूल तोड़ती है। → मेरा माली रोज़ फूल तोड़ता है।"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"संभावित उत्तर:\nकहने वाला – पिता / माता / शिक्षक; कहने वाला उस बालक/बालिका से कह रहा है जो शहर में पढ़ता है और छुट्टियों में गाँव जाने वाला है।\n“तुम गाँव जाकर अपने दादा-दादी से अवश्य मिलो, उनके अनुभव तुम्हारे काम आएँगे।” – यह वाक्य माता-पिता ने अपने बच्चे से कहा। परिस्थिति – बच्चा छुट्टियों में घूमने या केवल खेलने की योजना बना रहा है, तब उसे बड़ों से मिलने की सलाह दी जा रही है। शिक्षा – हमें बड़ों का सम्मान करना चाहिए, उनके अनुभवों से सीख लेकर जीवन को बेहतर बनाना चाहिए।"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"पर्यायवाची शब्द – वे शब्द जो अर्थ में समान या मिलते-जुलते होते हैं, पर्यायवाची कहलाते हैं।\n(क) मित्र – सखा, दोस्त\n(ख) घर – गृह, आवास / मकान"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"उपसर्ग – वे अव्यय या शब्दांश जो किसी शब्द के पहले लगकर उसके अर्थ में परिवर्तन या विशेषता उत्पन्न करते हैं, उपसर्ग कहलाते हैं।\nउदाहरण:\n‘अ’ – अशांत, अन्याय\n‘नि’ – निश्चय, निरीह\n‘दु’ – दुःख, दुष्कर"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-12T05:05:34.952Z"},{"id":95,"serialNumber":"CBSE-हिं-TestPrep-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 8","board":"CBSE","subject":"हिंदी ","chapter":null,"topic":"Test Prep - हिंदी ","difficulty":"medium","length":50,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"test_prep","content":{"title":"हिंदी - एकक परीक्षण प्रश्नपत्र (कक्षा 8, CBSE)","instructions":"1. कुल अंक: 50\n2. समय: 1 घंटा 30 मिनट\n3. सभी प्रश्न ध्यान से पढ़कर हल करें।\n4. सेक्शन A के सभी प्रश्नों के उत्तर दिए गए विकल्पों में से सही विकल्प चुनकर लिखें या रिक्त स्थान भरें।\n5. सेक्शन B के प्रश्नों के उत्तर संक्षेप में लिखें।\n6. सेक्शन C के प्रश्नों के उत्तर विस्तार से लिखें।\n7. जहाँ आवश्यक हो, उचित उदाहरण अवश्य दें।\n8. प्रश्नपत्र में संधि, मुहावरे और प्रत्यय विषयों से प्रश्न पूछे गए हैं।\n9. कुल अंक 50 से अधिक या कम नहीं हैं, सभी प्रश्नों का समाधान करते समय अंक-वितरण पर ध्यान दें।","sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A - वस्तुनिष्ठ प्रश्न (बहुविकल्पी एवं रिक्त स्थान पूर्ति) [1 अंक प्रत्येक]","questions":[{"question":"1. 'दिन+उदय' शब्द में कौन-सी संधि हुई है? [Marks: 1]","options":["अच् संधि","यण संधि","वृद्धि संधि","दीर्घ संधि"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"2. 'राजा+इश्वर' से बना सही संयुक्त शब्द कौन-सा है? [Marks: 1]","options":["राजइश्वर","राजश्वर","राजेश्वर","रजेश्वर"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"3. 'अग्नि+इष्ट' का सही संधि रूप चुनिए। [Marks: 1]","options":["अग्निष्ट","अग्न्यिष्ट","अग्नेष्ट","अग्निष्ठ"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"4. 'काम+आना' से बना मुहावरा किस अर्थ में प्रयुक्त होता है? [Marks: 1]","options":["कठिन होना","उपयोगी होना","करुणा आना","गुस्सा आना"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"5. 'नाक कटना' मुहावरे का सही अर्थ क्या है? [Marks: 1]","options":["चोट लगना","बीमार होना","मान–प्रतिष्ठा जाना","खुश होना"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"6. 'कान भरना' मुहावरे का अर्थ चुनिए। [Marks: 1]","options":["सुनाई न देना","ध्यान से सुनना","चुगली करना / भड़काना","किसी को पढ़ाना"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"7. 'विद्यार्थी' शब्द में प्रयुक्त प्रत्यय कौन-सा है? [Marks: 1]","options":["ता","अर्थी","ई","य"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"8. 'बालक' शब्द में कौन-सा प्रत्यय जुड़ा है? [Marks: 1]","options":["क","आल","क़","का"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"9. 'मीठा' शब्द में 'ा' किस प्रकार का प्रत्यय है? [Marks: 1]","options":["कृदंत प्रत्यय","तद्धित प्रत्यय","लिंग सूचक प्रत्यय","भाववाचक प्रत्यय"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"10. 'पुस्तकालय' शब्द में प्रयुक्त प्रत्यय कौन-सा है? [Marks: 1]","options":["पुस्तक","आलय","लेय","कालय"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"11. रिक्त स्थान भरिए: 'देव+ऋषि' शब्द में ______ संधि हुई है। [Marks: 1]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"12. रिक्त स्थान भरिए: 'आपस में लड़कर उन्होंने अपनी ___ कटवा ली।' (उचित मुहावरा भरिए) [Marks: 1]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"13. रिक्त स्थान भरिए: 'कर्म+ठ', ‘कर्मठ’ शब्द में 'ठ' ______ है। [Marks: 1]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"14. रिक्त स्थान भरिए: 'धन+आकर्षण' से बने शब्द 'धनाकर्षण' में 'आ' के लोप को ______ संधि कहते हैं। [Marks: 1]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"15. रिक्त स्थान भरिए: 'भू+इति' से बने 'भूति' शब्द में हुई संधि को ______ संधि कहते हैं। [Marks: 1]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section B - लघु उत्तरीय प्रश्न [प्रत्येक 2 या 3 अंक]","questions":[{"question":"1. संधि की परिभाषा दीजिए और किसी भी दो संधियों के नाम लिखिए। [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2},{"question":"2. 'राम+ईश्वर' तथा 'लोक+उद्धार' शब्दों का संधि-विच्छेद कीजिए। [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2},{"question":"3. 'टालमटोल करना' और 'हाथ बाँधकर खड़ा रहना' इन दोनों मुहावरों का अर्थ वाक्य बनाकर स्पष्ट कीजिए। [Marks: 3]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":3},{"question":"4. निम्नलिखित शब्दों में प्रयुक्त प्रत्यय पहचानकर मूल शब्द अलग कीजिए: (क) शिक्षक (ख) बालिका (ग) सत्यता [Marks: 3]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":3},{"question":"5. 'आशावादी', 'श्रमिक', 'कठोरता' शब्दों से 'प्रत्यय' की सहायता से बने एक–एक नए शब्द लिखिए। [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2},{"question":"6. किसी भी दो मुहावरे लिखिए और उनके अर्थ तथा प्रत्येक का एक-एक वाक्य लिखिए। [Marks: 3]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":3},{"question":"7. 'सुशिक्षित' और 'पाठशाला' शब्दों का संधि-विच्छेद कीजिए तथा संधि का नाम लिखिए। [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"Section C - दीर्घ उत्तरीय प्रश्न [प्रत्येक 4 या 5 अंक]","questions":[{"question":"1. नीचे दिए गए शब्दों का संधि-विच्छेद कीजिए और किस प्रकार की संधि हुई है, यह भी लिखिए: (क) महोत्सव (ख) सुरेश्वर (ग) गृहिणी (घ) प्रजाजन [Marks: 4]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":4},{"question":"2. पाँच मुहावरे चुनकर उनके अर्थ तथा उपयुक्त वाक्य लिखिए। मुहावरे: (क) दाँत खट्टे करना (ख) आँखों का तारा (ग) सिर पर चढ़ाना (घ) घी के दीए जलाना (ङ) आँखें तरेरना (च) मन मैला होना [Marks: 5]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":5},{"question":"3. प्रत्यय की परिभाषा लिखिए। फिर नीचे दिए गए शब्दों से प्रत्यय अलग करके मूल शब्द और प्रत्यय को तालिका के रूप में लिखिए: (क) लेखक (ख) बाल्यावस्था (ग) मिठाई (घ) सफलतापूर्वक (ङ) ग्रामीण [Marks: 5]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":5},{"question":"4. निम्नलिखित संयुक्त शब्दों से संधि-विच्छेद कीजिए तथा संधि का नाम लिखिए। साथ ही प्रत्येक के समान प्रकार की संधि से एक-एक और उदाहरण दीजिए: (क) देवालय (ख) नीतिशील (ग) सत्कार (घ) मनीषी [Marks: 4]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":4},{"question":"5. नीचे दिए गए शब्दों में से किसी चार का संधि-विच्छेद कीजिए और स्पष्ट कीजिए कि कौन-सी संधि हुई है: (क) विद्यालोक (ख) सुविचार (ग) महात्मा (घ) सुगंधि (ङ) दिनेश्वर [Marks: 4]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":4},{"question":"6. नीचे दिए गए शब्दों में प्रयुक्त प्रत्ययों के प्रकार (कृत, तद्धित आदि) पहचानिए और संक्षेप में लिखिए कि वे शब्द के अर्थ में क्या परिवर्तन लाते हैं: (क) लेखक (ख) छात्रावास (ग) मधुरता (घ) पर्वतीय (ङ) बालिका [Marks: 4]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":4}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"वृद्धि संधि (Option C)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"राजेश्वर (Option C)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"अग्निष्ट (Option A)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"उपयोगी होना (Option B)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"मान–प्रतिष्ठा जाना (Option C)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"चुगली करना / भड़काना (Option C)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"अर्थी (Option B)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"क (Option A)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":8,"answer":"लिंग सूचक प्रत्यय (Option C)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":9,"answer":"आलय (Option B)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":10,"answer":"वृद्धि संधि"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":11,"answer":"नाक (नाक कटना)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":12,"answer":"प्रत्यय"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":13,"answer":"लोप (या लोप-संधि / गुण-संधि संदर्भानुसार स्वीकार्य)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":14,"answer":"गुण संधि"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"संधि: दो वर्णों या शब्दों के मेल से होने वाला परिवर्तन संधि कहलाता है।\nउदाहरण के लिए दो प्रकार: स्वर संधि, व्यंजन संधि (या विसर्ग संधि)।"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"राम+ईश्वर = रामेश्वर (वृद्धि स्वर संधि)\nलोक+उद्धार = लोकोद्धार (दीर्घ / गुण स्वर संधि – क+उ → को)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"टालमटोल करना: काम को बार-बार आगे खिसकाना, देर करना।\nवाक्य: वह होमवर्क में हमेशा टालमटोल करता है।\nहाथ बाँधकर खड़ा रहना: असहाय बने रहना, कुछ न करना।\nवाक्य: दुर्घटना होते देख वह हाथ बाँधकर खड़ा रहा।"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"शिक्षक = शिक्ष (मूल शब्द) + क (प्रत्यय)\nबालिका = बाल (मूल शब्द) + इका/का (प्रत्यय)\nसत्यता = सत्य (मूल शब्द) + ता (प्रत्यय)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"आशावादी → आशा + वादी: उदाहरण नया शब्द – निराशावादी।\nश्रमिक → श्रम + इक: उदाहरण नया शब्द – कारखाना-श्रमिक।\nकठोरता → कठोर + ता: उदाहरण नया शब्द – नम्रता, सच्चाई आदि (कोई भी उपयुक्त प्रत्यययुक्त शब्द स्वीकार्य)।"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"कोई भी दो उचित मुहावरे, उनके सही अर्थ और सही वाक्य।\nउदाहरण: \n(1) सिर घूमना – अत्यधिक परेशान या भ्रमित होना।\nवाक्य: कठिन प्रश्नपत्र देखकर मेरा सिर घूम गया।\n(2) आँखें खोलना – सचेत करना।\nवाक्य: इस घटना ने उसकी आँखें खोल दीं।"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"सुशिक्षित = सु+शिक्षित (उपसर्ग + मूल शब्द; यहाँ संधि-विच्छेद रूप में ‘सु+शिक्षित’, संधि नहीं, लेकिन प्रश्न अनुसार लिखा जाएगा)।\nपाठशाला = पाठ+शाला (दीर्घ स्वर संधि / गुण संधि संदर्भानुसार, कई पुस्तकें इसे संधि से न बने समासिक शब्द की तरह भी मानती हैं; उत्तर में पाठ+शाला लिखना पर्याप्त है)।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"महोत्सव = महा+उत्सव (स्वर संधि – गुण/दीर्घ प्रकार स्वीकार्य)\nसुरेश्वर = सुर+ईश्वर → सुरेश्वर (वृद्धि संधि)\nगृहिणी = गृह+इनी/इणी → गृहिणी (स्वर संधि)\nप्रजाजन = प्रजा+जन → प्रजाजन (स्वर संधि / दीर्घ संधि)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"कोई भी पाँच सही उत्तर:\n(क) दाँत खट्टे करना – किसी को कड़ा सबक सिखाना।\n(ख) आँखों का तारा – अत्यंत प्रिय व्यक्ति।\n(ग) सिर पर चढ़ाना – किसी को बहुत अधिक महत्व देना।\n(घ) घी के दीए जलाना – बहुत खुश होना।\n(ङ) आँखें तरेरना – गुस्से से देखना।\n(च) मन मैला होना – मन में बुरे भाव आना।\nप्रत्येक के साथ उपयुक्त वाक्य।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"प्रत्यय: वह बंधित रूप जो किसी मूल शब्द के बाद जुड़कर उसके अर्थ या रूप में परिवर्तन करता है, प्रत्यय कहलाता है।\nउदाहरण तालिका:\nलेखक = लेख (मूल शब्द) + क (प्रत्यय)\nबाल्यावस्था = बाल्य + अवस्था (अवस्था भी प्रत्यय रूप में स्वीकार्य) या बाल + य + अवस्था\nमिठाई = मीठा/मिष्ठ (मूल) + ई (प्रत्यय)\nसफलतापूर्वक = सफल + ता + पूर्वक (दो प्रत्यय)\nग्रामीण = ग्राम (मूल) + ईण/ईन (प्रत्यय)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"देवालय = देव+आलय (स्वर संधि / दीर्घ संधि)\nनीतिशील = नीति+शील (स्वर संधि)\nसत्कार = सत+आकार/कार (स्वर संधि)\nमनीषी = मनि/मन+ईषी (स्वर संधि)\nप्रत्येक प्रकार की एक–एक और संधि का उदाहरण: जैसे देव+इंद्र = देवेंद्र, राज+उत्तम = राजोत्तम आदि।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"किसी चार के संधि-विच्छेद:\nविद्यालोक = विद्या+लोक (स्वर/दीर्घ संधि)\nसुविचार = सु+विचार (उपसर्ग+शब्द; कुछ पुस्तकें इसे संधि से नहीं, पर यहाँ ‘सु+विचार’ मान्य)\nमहात्मा = महा+आत्मा (स्वर संधि)\nसुगंधि = सु+गंधि (उपसर्ग+शब्द; ‘सु+गंध’ भी मान्य)\nदिनेश्वर = दिन+ईश्वर → दिनेश्वर (वृद्धि संधि)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"लेखक: ‘क’ कृत प्रत्यय – क्रिया या कार्य करने वाले व्यक्ति को दर्शाता है (जो लेख लिखता है)।\nछात्रावास: ‘आवास/वास’ तद्धित/नामवाची प्रत्यय – रहने का स्थान बताता है (जहाँ छात्र रहते हैं)।\nमधुरता: ‘ता’ भाववाचक (तद्धित) प्रत्यय – गुण को भाव के रूप में व्यक्त करता है (मधुर होने की अवस्था)।\nपर्वतीय: ‘ईय/ीय’ तद्धित प्रत्यय – ‘पर्वत से संबंधित’ अर्थ जोड़ता है।\nबालिका: ‘इका/का’ तद्धित/लिंग सूचक प्रत्यय – स्त्रीलिंग को सूचित करता है।"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-12T05:01:05.203Z"},{"id":94,"serialNumber":"CBSE-HIN--002","userId":3,"className":"Grade 8","board":"CBSE","subject":"Hindi","chapter":"","topic":"संधि, प्रत्यय, अव्यय ","difficulty":"medium","length":30,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"कक्षा 8 हिंदी (वसंत भाग–3) – व्याकरण अभ्यास-पत्र: संधि, प्रत्यय, अव्यय","instructions":"• यह कार्यपत्रक एनसीईआरटी कक्षा 8 हिंदी पाठ्यपुस्तक ‘वसंत (भाग–3)’ के व्याकरण भाग ‘संधि, प्रत्यय, अव्यय’ पर आधारित है।\n• सभी प्रश्न ध्यान से पढ़कर हल करें।\n• जहाँ निर्देशित हो, वहाँ संधि, प्रत्यय और अव्यय की परिभाषाएँ एवं उदाहरण पुस्तक में दिए अनुसार ही लिखें।\n• उत्तर साफ-सुथरे अक्षरों में लिखें।","graphics":[{"description":"रंगीन मिनिमलिस्ट चित्र जिसमें खुली हुई हिंदी की पुस्तक है और उसके ऊपर अक्षर अ, आ, क, संधि, प्रत्यय जैसे शब्द तैर रहे हैं।","position":"top-right","altText":"हिंदी व्याकरण की खुली किताब और तैरते अक्षर"},{"description":"सादा लाइन-आर्ट चित्र जिसमें तीन बॉक्स बने हैं – पहले पर ‘संधि’, दूसरे पर ‘प्रत्यय’ और तीसरे पर ‘अव्यय’ लिखा है, जिन्हें तीरों से आपस में जोड़ा गया है।","position":"between-sections","altText":"संधि, प्रत्यय और अव्यय को जोड़ता हुआ चित्र"},{"description":"सरल रंगीन चित्र जिसमें एक छात्र मेज़ पर बैठकर वर्कशीट भर रहा है, पास ही दीवार पर ‘अव्यय: कभी, बहुत, आज’ जैसे शब्द लिखी एक चार्ट शीट लगी है।","position":"bottom-left","altText":"वर्कशीट हल करता छात्र और दीवार पर अव्यय शब्दों का चार्ट"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड A – वस्तुनिष्ठ प्रश्न (बहुविकल्पी)","questions":[{"question":"‘संधि’ का आशय है –","options":["दो या दो से अधिक वाक्यों का मेल","दो या दो से अधिक पदों का मेल","दो या दो से अधिक वर्णों का मेल","दो या दो से अधिक कारकों का मेल"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"‘प्रत्यय’ किसे कहते हैं?","options":["जो शब्द के पहले लगकर नया शब्द बनाए","जो शब्द के बाद लगकर नया शब्द बनाए","जो दो शब्दों को जोड़ दे","जो केवल वाक्य के भाव को बदल दे"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"‘अव्यय’ शब्दों के बारे में सही कथन चुनिए –","options":["इनमें लिंग और वचन का भेद होता है।","इनमें कारक, लिंग, वचन, पुरुष का भेद नहीं होता।","ये केवल संज्ञा के लिए प्रयुक्त होते हैं।","ये केवल सर्वनाम के लिए प्रयुक्त होते हैं।"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"‘राम + ईश्वर = रामेश्वर’ – यह किस प्रकार की संधि का उदाहरण है?","options":["दीर्घ संधि","गुण संधि","यण् संधि","वृद्धि संधि"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"‘खेती + वाला = खेतीवाला’ – यहाँ ‘वाला’ क्या है?","options":["उपसर्ग","प्रत्यय","अव्यय","सर्वनाम"],"answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड B – रिक्त स्थान पूर्ति (संधि, प्रत्यय, अव्यय)","questions":[{"question":"1. जब दो वर्ण मिलकर एक हो जाते हैं, वहाँ _______ होती है।","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"2. जो शब्द के अंत में लगकर नया शब्द बनाए, उसे _______ कहते हैं।","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"3. जो शब्द रूप नहीं बदलते, वे _______ कहलाते हैं।","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"4. ‘विद्या + आलय’ से बने शब्द ‘विद्यालय’ में _______ संधि है।","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"5. ‘बालक + ईश्वर = बालेश्वर’ में ‘अ + ई’ से ‘ए’ बनने की संधि को _______ संधि कहते हैं।","answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"match","title":"खंड C – मिलान कीजिए (संधि के उदाहरण)","questions":[{"question":"नीचे दिए गए शब्दों को उनकी संधि-विग्रह से मिलाइए:","answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"1. देवेश","right":"क. चंद्र + आला"},{"left":"2. चरवाहा","right":"ख. देव + ईश"},{"left":"3. मंदिर","right":"ग. चर + वाहक"},{"left":"4. चंद्रालय","right":"घ. मन्द + इर"}]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड D – संधि भंग कीजिए","questions":[{"question":"1. रामेश्वर = ____________________","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"2. विद्यालय = ____________________","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"3. देवालय = ____________________","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"4. बालेश्वर = ____________________","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"5. चरवाहा = ____________________","answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड E – संधि कीजिए","questions":[{"question":"1. देव + ईश्वर = ____________________","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"2. विद्या + आलय = ____________________","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"3. बालक + ईश्वर = ____________________","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"4. मन्द + इर = ____________________","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"5. चर + वाहक = ____________________","answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"खंड F – संक्षिप्त उत्तरीय प्रश्न (परिभाषा व उदाहरण)","questions":[{"question":"1. संधि की परिभाषा लिखिए तथा पुस्तक में दिए किसी एक उदाहरण के साथ स्पष्ट कीजिए।","answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"2. प्रत्यय की परिभाषा लिखिए और ‘खेतीवाला’ शब्द में प्रयुक्त प्रत्यय को अलग कीजिए।","answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"3. अव्यय की विशेषताएँ संक्षेप में लिखिए।","answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"4. संधि के दो लाभ लिखिए (जैसा अध्याय में स्पष्ट किया गया है)।","answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"5. ‘प्रेमी’ और ‘कर्मी’ शब्दों में प्रत्यय की पहचान कीजिए।","answerSpaceLines":1}]},{"type":"match","title":"खंड G – प्रत्यय का मिलान कीजिए","questions":[{"question":"शब्दों को उनसे जुड़े प्रत्यय से मिलाइए:","answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"1. खेतीवाला","right":"क. ई"},{"left":"2. प्रेमी","right":"ख. वाला"},{"left":"3. कर्मी","right":"ग. ई"},{"left":"4. मजदूरी","right":"घ. ऊरी / ऊरी से बना ‘ऊरी’ जैसा प्रत्यय"}]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड H – प्रत्यय जोड़कर शब्द बनाइए","questions":[{"question":"1. खेत + _______ = खेतीवाला","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"2. प्रेम + _______ = प्रेमी","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"3. कर्म + _______ = कर्मी","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"4. मजदूर + _______ = मजदूरी","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"5. बालक + _______ = बालकपन (अध्याय की शैली के अनुसार उपयुक्त प्रत्यय लिखिए)","answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"match","title":"खंड I – अव्यय का प्रयोग (मिलान कीजिए)","questions":[{"question":"अव्यय शब्दों को उनके वाक्यगत प्रयोग से मिलाइए:","answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"1. आज","right":"क. समय बताने वाला अव्यय"},{"left":"2. बहुत","right":"ख. मात्रा बताने वाला अव्यय"},{"left":"3. कभी","right":"ग. अनिश्चित समय का बोध कराता अव्यय"},{"left":"4. यहाँ","right":"घ. स्थान बताने वाला अव्यय"}]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"खंड J – अव्यय पहचानिए","questions":[{"question":"1. वाक्य में अव्यय शब्द को रेखांकित कीजिए – ‘आज मैं बहुत खुश हूँ।’","answerSpaceLines":1},{"question":"2. वाक्य में अव्यय शब्द को लिखिए – ‘कभी वह यहाँ आता है।’","answerSpaceLines":1},{"question":"3. वाक्य में प्रयुक्त दो अव्यय अलग कीजिए – ‘आज वह बहुत दूर चला गया।’","answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"4. ‘वह अभी घर पर है।’ – इस वाक्य में अव्यय शब्द कौन-सा है और वह क्या बताता है?","answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"5. ‘वे कल यहाँ आएँगे।’ – यहाँ प्रयुक्त दो अव्ययों को लिखिए।","answerSpaceLines":1}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"दो या दो से अधिक वर्णों का मेल"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"जो शब्द के बाद लगकर नया शब्द बनाए"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"इनमें कारक, लिंग, वचन, पुरुष का भेद नहीं होता।"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"दीर्घ संधि"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"प्रत्यय"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"संधि"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"प्रत्यय"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"अव्यय"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"दीर्घ संधि"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"दीर्घ संधि"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"1–ख, 2–ग, 3–घ, 4–क"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"राम + ईश्वर"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"विद्या + आलय"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"देव + आलय"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"बालक + ईश्वर"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"चर + वाहक"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"रामेश्वर"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"विद्यालय"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"देवालय"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"बालेश्वर"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"चरवाहा"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"‘संधि’ – दो वर्णों के मेल से जो परिवर्तन होता है उसे संधि कहते हैं। उदाहरण: राम + ईश्वर = रामेश्वर।"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"प्रत्यय – जो शब्द के अंत में लगकर नया शब्द बनाता है। ‘खेतीवाला’ में ‘वाला’ प्रत्यय है।"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"अव्यय – जिन शब्दों में लिंग, वचन, पुरुष, कारक आदि के कारण कोई रूप परिवर्तन नहीं होता, उन्हें अव्यय कहते हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"संधि से भाषा सरल, सुगम और प्रवाहपूर्ण हो जाती है; उच्चारण में सुविधा होती है (अध्याय के आशय के अनुसार)।"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"दोनों में ‘ई’ प्रत्यय है – प्रेम + ई = प्रेमी, कर्म + ई = कर्मी।"},{"sectionIndex":6,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"1–ख, 2–क, 3–ग, 4–घ"},{"sectionIndex":7,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"वाला"},{"sectionIndex":7,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"ई"},{"sectionIndex":7,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"ई"},{"sectionIndex":7,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"ई"},{"sectionIndex":7,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"पन"},{"sectionIndex":8,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"1–क, 2–ख, 3–ग, 4–घ"},{"sectionIndex":9,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"‘आज’ और ‘बहुत’ – दोनों अव्यय हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":9,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"कभी, यहाँ – इनमें से कोई एक लिखना भी स्वीकार्य है यदि प्रश्न में एक ही माँगा हो, पर दोनों अव्यय हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":9,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"‘आज’ और ‘बहुत’ – ये दोनों अव्यय हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":9,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"‘अभी’ अव्यय है; यह समय का बोध कराता है।"},{"sectionIndex":9,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"‘कल’ और ‘यहाँ’ – दोनों अव्यय हैं।"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-12T04:55:44.538Z"},{"id":93,"serialNumber":"CBSE-HIN--001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 8","board":"CBSE","subject":"Hindi","chapter":"","topic":"व्याकरण ","difficulty":"medium","length":30,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"कक्षा 8 हिंदी (वसंत भाग–3) – व्याकरण आधारित कार्यपत्रक","instructions":"1. सभी प्रश्न ध्यान से पढ़कर हल करें।\n2. बहुविकल्पी प्रश्नों में सही विकल्प चुनकर उसके अक्षर (A/B/C/D) को उत्तर के रूप में लिखें।\n3. रिक्त स्थान वाले प्रश्नों में वाक्य को पूरा करने के लिए सही शब्द या शब्द-समूह लिखें।\n4. उत्तर साफ-सुथरे व सुलेख में लिखें।\n5. यह कार्यपत्रक एनसीईआरटी ‘वसंत भाग–3’ (कक्षा 8) की पाठ्य-पुस्तक में प्रयुक्त व्याकरणिक बातों (काल, वचन, लिंग, संज्ञा, सर्वनाम, विशेषण, क्रिया, अव्यय, वाक्य, मुहावरे, लोकोक्तियाँ, पर्यायवाची, विलोम आदि) पर आधारित है।","graphics":[{"description":"रंग-बिरंगे पेंसिल, किताब और खुली कॉपी का साधारण रेखाचित्र, जिसमें कॉपी पर ‘अ, आ, इ’ जैसे अक्षर लिखे हों।","position":"top-right","altText":"हिंदी लेखन और पढ़ाई दर्शाने वाला चित्र"},{"description":"काली स्लेट पर सफेद चॉक से ‘संज्ञा, सर्वनाम, क्रिया’ लिखे हुए, पास में एक छोटी रंगीन डस्टर का चित्र।","position":"between-sections","altText":"व्याकरण के मुख्य भेद दर्शाने वाली स्लेट"},{"description":"रंगीन कार्डों पर लिखे शब्दों को जोड़ते हुए एक बच्चा, जैसे ‘काल’, ‘वचन’, ‘लिंग’ आदि।","position":"bottom-left","altText":"व्याकरण की संकल्पनाओं को जोड़ता बच्चा"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड – 1 : बहुविकल्पी प्रश्न (MCQ)","questions":[{"question":"‘लड़का खेल रहा है।’ वाक्य में ‘खेल रहा है’ किस काल की क्रिया है?","options":["वर्तमान काल","भूत काल","भविष्यत् काल","परस्मैपदी क्रिया"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"निम्न में से पुल्लिंग शब्द कौन-सा है?","options":["किताब","पेड़","मेज़","कुर्सी"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘वे स्कूल जाते थे।’ वाक्य में ‘थे’ किस काल को सूचित करता है?","options":["साधारण वर्तमान काल","साधारण भूत काल","साधारण भविष्यत् काल","आदेशसूचक वर्तमान काल"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘सुन्दर’ शब्द किस शब्दभेद का उदाहरण है?","options":["संज्ञा","सर्वनाम","विशेषण","क्रिया"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘वे’ किस प्रकार का सर्वनाम है?","options":["पुरुषवाचक संज्ञा","पुरुषवाचक सर्वनाम","निजवाचक सर्वनाम","समुच्चयबोधक सर्वनाम"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘किताबें मेज़ पर रखी हैं।’ वाक्य में ‘किताबें’ किस वचन में है?","options":["एकवचन","बहुवचन","द्विवचन","संयुक्त वचन"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘बहुत धीरे-धीरे’ में ‘बहुत’ शब्द क्या है?","options":["संज्ञा","क्रिया","अव्यय (क्रिया विशेषण)","सर्वनाम"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘मैं कल बाज़ार जाऊँगा।’ वाक्य किस काल में है?","options":["भूत काल","वर्तमान काल","भविष्यत् काल","संभाव्य काल"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘धीरे-धीरे’ में दोहराव का प्रयोग किसके लिए किया गया है?","options":["ज़ोर देने के लिए","संख्या बताने के लिए","काल बताने के लिए","पुरुष बताने के लिए"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"निम्न में से स्त्रीलिंग शब्द कौन-सा है?","options":["बालक","लड़का","पुस्तक","घोड़ा"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘मैंने उसे बुलाया।’ वाक्य में ‘उसे’ शब्द है –","options":["संज्ञा","सर्वनाम","विशेषण","अव्यय"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"शुद्ध वाक्य चुनिए:","options":["वे किताब पढ़ रहा है।","वे किताब पढ़ रहे हैं।","वे किताब पढ़ रही है।","वे किताब पढ़ रहा हूँ।"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘अभी’ किस प्रकार का शब्द है?","options":["काल सूचक अव्यय","सम्बन्धबोधक अव्यय","संधि","समास"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"वाक्य का वह भाग, जिससे हमें यह पता चले कि कार्य करने वाला कौन या क्या है, कहलाता है –","options":["विधेय","कर्म","कर्ता","अव्यय"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘वह पढ़ता है।’ वाक्य में ‘पढ़ता है’ –","options":["क्रिया है","संज्ञा है","विशेषण है","सर्वनाम है"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड – 2 : रिक्त स्थान भरिए","questions":[{"question":"1. ‘लड़की गाना _______ है।’ वाक्य को वर्तमान काल में पूरा कीजिए।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. ‘मैंने खाना खा लिया था।’ यह वाक्य _______ काल का है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. ‘बच्चे पार्क में खेल रहे हैं।’ वाक्य में ‘बच्चे’ शब्द _______ वचन में है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. ‘सुन्दर लड़की’ शब्दसमूह में ‘सुन्दर’ शब्द _______ है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. ‘मैंने उससे पूछा।’ वाक्य में ‘मैंने’ में ‘मैं’ _______ है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. ‘किताब मेज़ पर रख दो।’ वाक्य में क्रिया _______ है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. ‘वह जल्दी-जल्दी लिख रहा था।’ वाक्य में ‘जल्दी-जल्दी’ _______ है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. ‘आदमी’ शब्द का स्त्रीलिंग _______ है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. ‘लड़का भागकर घर आया।’ वाक्य में ‘घर’ शब्द _______ है। (संज्ञा/सर्वनाम)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. ‘कल मैं तुम्हारे घर आऊँगा।’ इसमें ‘कल’ शब्द _______ बताता है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. ‘पेड़ पर चिड़िया बैठी है।’ वाक्य में ‘पेड़’ शब्द _______ है। (संज्ञा का भेद – जड़/चेतन नहीं पूछना, केवल संज्ञा/सर्वनाम लिखें)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. ‘तुम कहाँ जा रहे हो?’ वाक्य में ‘कहाँ’ _______ है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. ‘बच्चा खूब हँसा।’ वाक्य में ‘खूब’ शब्द क्रिया को _______ है। (कैसा/कब/कहाँ इनमें से एक लिखें)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"14. ‘वह किताब पढ़ चुका था।’ वाक्य में क्रिया का काल _______ है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"15. ‘अच्छा’ शब्द का विलोम (उल्टा अर्थ वाला शब्द) _______ है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"वर्तमान काल"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"पेड़"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"साधारण भूत काल"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"विशेषण"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"पुरुषवाचक सर्वनाम"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"बहुवचन"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"अव्यय (क्रिया विशेषण)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"भविष्यत् काल"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":8,"answer":"ज़ोर देने के लिए"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":9,"answer":"पुस्तक"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":10,"answer":"सर्वनाम"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":11,"answer":"वे किताब पढ़ रहे हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":12,"answer":"काल सूचक अव्यय"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":13,"answer":"कर्ता"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":14,"answer":"क्रिया है"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"गा रही"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"भूत"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"बहुवचन"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"विशेषण"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"सर्वनाम"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"रख दो"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"अव्यय (क्रिया विशेषण)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"औरत"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":8,"answer":"संज्ञा"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":9,"answer":"काल"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":10,"answer":"संज्ञा"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":11,"answer":"अव्यय (प्रश्नवाचक शब्द)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":12,"answer":"कैसा"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":13,"answer":"भूत काल"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":14,"answer":"बुरा"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-12T04:53:55.912Z"},{"id":92,"serialNumber":"CBSE-SCI-Friction-002","userId":3,"className":"Grade 8","board":"CBSE","subject":"Science","chapter":"Friction ","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":30,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"CBSE Class 8 Science – Worksheet on Friction (NCERT Chapter 12)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully.\n• Answer in your own words where required, based only on NCERT Class 8 Science Chapter ‘Friction’.\n• Do not spend too much time on a single question.\n• For MCQs and True/False, tick/encircle the correct option.\n• For fill in the blanks and short answer questions, write neatly in the given space.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist illustration of a shoe sole with rough tread rubbing against the ground, with small arrows showing frictional force opposite to motion.","position":"top-right","altText":"Illustration showing friction between shoe and ground"},{"description":"Simple line-art of a child trying to push a heavy box on the floor with arrows showing applied force and friction in opposite directions, with soft pastel colors.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Child pushing a box illustrating opposing frictional force"},{"description":"Minimalist sketch of a block attached to a spring balance being pulled on a surface, with the spring balance reading highlighted in bright color.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Spring balance measuring force of friction on a block"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A: Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Friction always acts:","options":["In the direction of motion","Opposite to the direction of motion","Perpendicular to the direction of motion","In all directions at the same time"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The force of friction between two surfaces depends mainly on:","options":["The mass of the Earth","The area of contact only","The nature of the surfaces in contact","The temperature of the surfaces"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Which of the following is used to reduce friction?","options":["Making the surfaces rough","Using wheels or rollers","Increasing the weight of the body","Using sand on the surfaces"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. The friction present between the soles of our shoes and the ground is:","options":["Static friction","Rolling friction","Fluid friction","Magnetic friction"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. When a body rolls over a surface, the friction that comes into play is called:","options":["Sliding friction","Static friction","Rolling friction","Fluid friction"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. Which of the following is an example where friction is useful?","options":["Wear and tear of machine parts","Heat produced in the moving parts of machines","Brakes applied in a bicycle","Burning of soles of shoes"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. Which of the following is used as a lubricant?","options":["Sand","Water","Oil or grease","Air"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. Fluid friction depends on:","options":["The shape of the object and the speed with respect to the fluid","Only on the mass of the object","Only on the colour of the fluid","Only on the area of the object"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B: True or False (Choose the correct option)","questions":[{"question":"9. Friction is a contact force.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. Friction can be both increased and decreased as per our requirement.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. Sliding friction is usually smaller than rolling friction.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. Friction produces heat.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. Friction depends on the nature of the surfaces in contact.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"14. Fluid friction is also called drag.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C: Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"15. The force of friction always acts in the direction __________ to the direction of motion of the object.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"16. Friction is caused by the __________ on the two surfaces in contact.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"17. To reduce friction, a substance called __________ is applied between the moving parts of machines.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"18. Friction that comes into play before an object starts moving is called __________ friction.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"19. When an object actually starts moving over a surface, the friction that comes into play is called __________ friction.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"20. The frictional force exerted by fluids is called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"21. The special shapes given to cars and aeroplanes to reduce fluid friction are called __________ shapes.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"22. The measure of the force of friction can be obtained using a device called a __________ balance.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D: Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"23. Why is it difficult to move a pencil box kept on the table at first, but easier to move it once it starts sliding?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"24. State two disadvantages of friction mentioned in the chapter.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"25. State two ways by which friction can be reduced as described in the textbook.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"26. Why do the soles of our shoes and tyres of vehicles have grooves?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"27. Why do brake pads in the brake system of bicycles and cars wear out gradually?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"28. Why is it easier to roll a heavy suitcase with wheels than to slide it?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"29. Give one example each where we intentionally increase friction and where we intentionally reduce friction.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"30. How do the special shapes of birds and aeroplanes help them to move easily through fluids?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Opposite to the direction of motion"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"The nature of the surfaces in contact"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Using wheels or rollers"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Static friction"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Rolling friction"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Brakes applied in a bicycle"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"Oil or grease"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"The shape of the object and the speed with respect to the fluid"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"opposite"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"irregularities (or bumps and hollows)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"lubricant"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"static"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"sliding"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"drag"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"streamlined"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"spring"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Because static friction (before motion starts) is greater than sliding friction. Once the pencil box starts sliding, only sliding friction acts, which is smaller, so it is easier to keep it moving."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Friction causes wear and tear of the soles of shoes and the moving parts of machines; friction also wastes energy in the form of heat and sometimes produces noise."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"By using lubricants such as oil, grease or graphite between moving parts; by using wheels, rollers, ball bearings or by giving streamlined shapes to objects moving in fluids."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Grooves increase friction between the surface and the ground, providing better grip. This prevents slipping, especially on wet or uneven roads, and makes walking or driving safer."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Due to friction between the brake pads and the moving parts (like the wheels), the pads undergo wear and tear and gradually get worn out, so they have to be replaced after some time."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Rolling friction is smaller than sliding friction. When the suitcase has wheels, rolling friction acts, which is less than sliding friction, so less force is needed to move it."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"To increase friction: treading or grooving the soles of shoes or tyres. To reduce friction: applying oil or grease to the moving parts of a machine or using ball bearings."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"The bodies of birds and aeroplanes are streamlined. This shape allows them to cut through air or water smoothly and reduces fluid friction (drag), helping them to move easily and faster."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-09T16:07:00.801Z"},{"id":91,"serialNumber":"CBSE-SCI-Friction-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 8","board":"CBSE","subject":"Science","chapter":"Friction ","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"CBSE Class 8 Science – Worksheet on Friction (NCERT Chapter 12)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully.\n• Answer in the space provided.\n• For MCQs and True/False, tick (✔) the correct option.\n• Use pencil for rough work and neat handwriting for answers.\n• This worksheet is strictly based on NCERT Class 8 Science textbook, Chapter: Friction.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist line-art of a shoe sole rubbing against the ground with small arrows showing frictional force opposite to motion.","position":"top-right","altText":"Shoe rubbing on ground showing friction acting opposite to motion"},{"description":"Simple illustration of a block on a table with an arrow showing applied force and another arrow in opposite direction showing friction.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Block on a table with applied force and friction in opposite directions"},{"description":"Minimalist drawing of a moving car with arrows at the tyres indicating friction between tyres and road.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Car tyres showing friction with the road"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. The force of friction always acts:","options":["In the direction of motion of the object","Opposite to the direction of motion of the object","Perpendicular to the direction of motion","In all directions at the same time"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The force of friction between two surfaces in contact can be reduced by:","options":["Making the surfaces rough","Increasing the weight of the object","Using lubricants","Using wheels without bearings"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. The force of friction that comes into play before an object just starts moving is called:","options":["Limiting friction","Sliding friction","Rolling friction","Fluid friction"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False (Choose the Correct Option)","questions":[{"question":"4. Friction is caused by the roughness of the surfaces in contact.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. Rolling friction is smaller than sliding friction.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. Fluid friction is independent of the speed of the object moving through the fluid.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"7. The force which opposes the relative motion between two surfaces in contact is called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. Substances like oil and grease used to reduce friction are called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. The frictional force exerted by fluids is also called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"10. Why is it difficult to walk on a wet muddy road?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Opposite to the direction of motion of the object"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Using lubricants"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Limiting friction"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"friction"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"lubricants"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"drag"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"On a wet muddy road, the friction between our feet and the ground is greatly reduced, so our feet cannot get a good grip and we find it difficult to walk."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-09T16:06:37.285Z"},{"id":90,"serialNumber":"CBSE-SCI-Light-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 8","board":"CBSE","subject":"Science","chapter":"Light","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":30,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Class 8 Science – Chapter 16: Light (NCERT) – Worksheet","instructions":"• Read each question carefully and answer in the space provided.\n• For MCQs and True/False, tick (✓) the correct option.\n• For Fill in the Blanks, write the correct word(s) in the blank.\n• For Short Answer questions, answer briefly in 2–3 sentences.\n• Use only the concepts and definitions given in NCERT Class 8 Science, Chapter 16: Light.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist illustration of a torch sending a straight beam of light to a mirror and the beam reflecting to an eye icon","position":"top-right","altText":"Light ray from torch reflecting from a mirror into an eye"},{"description":"Simple line-art of a periscope with two plane mirrors showing the path of light rays by arrows","position":"between-sections","altText":"Periscope with two plane mirrors and light rays marked by arrows"},{"description":"Minimalist picture of the human eye with parts like cornea, iris, pupil and lens highlighted in different colors","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Colored outline of human eye showing main parts"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Which of the following is responsible for the sensation of vision?","options":["Eyes","Brain","Light","Nose"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The bouncing back of light from a smooth surface is called:","options":["Refraction of light","Reflection of light","Dispersion of light","Scattering of light"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. The image formed by a plane mirror is:","options":["Real and inverted","Virtual and inverted","Real and erect","Virtual and erect"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. The type of reflection that takes place from a smooth and shining surface is called:","options":["Irregular reflection","Diffuse reflection","Regular reflection","Multiple reflection"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. Which device uses two plane mirrors arranged parallel to each other?","options":["Kaleidoscope","Periscope","Torch","Camera"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The curved, transparent front part of the eye which admits light is:","options":["Iris","Cornea","Pupil","Retina"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The small opening in the iris through which light enters the eye is called:","options":["Cornea","Lens","Pupil","Retina"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. Which part of the eye controls the size of the pupil?","options":["Cornea","Retina","Iris","Optic nerve"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True / False (Choose the correct option)","questions":[{"question":"9. A ray of light is represented by a straight line with an arrow on it.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. The angle between the reflected ray and the normal is called the angle of incidence.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. The incident ray, the reflected ray and the normal at the point of incidence, all lie in the same plane.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. In diffuse reflection, the laws of reflection are not followed.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. In multiple reflection of light, light is reflected only once.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"14. The image formed on the retina is real and inverted.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"15. Night blindness is a condition where a person cannot see in bright light.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"16. Cones are sensitive to bright light and help us to see colours.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"17. Light travels in a __________ line.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"18. The perpendicular drawn at the point of incidence on a reflecting surface is called the __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"19. The angle between the incident ray and the normal is called the angle of __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"20. In a plane mirror, the image formed is of the same size as the object but is __________ from left to right.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"21. Reflection from a rough surface is called __________ reflection.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"22. __________ reflection helps us to see things around us that do not emit light.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"23. In a periscope, the mirrors are arranged at an angle of __________ degrees to the pipe.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"24. The surface of the retina has a large number of __________ and __________ cells.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"25. Braille is a system of reading and writing for the __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"26. State the two laws of reflection of light.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"27. What is meant by multiple reflection of light? Give one use of multiple reflection mentioned in the chapter.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"28. What is kaleidoscope? Name any two places where it is used.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"29. What are rods and cones? State one function of each.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"30. What is Braille? Who developed this system?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Light"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Reflection of light"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Virtual and erect"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Regular reflection"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Periscope"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Cornea"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"Pupil"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"Iris"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"straight"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"normal"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"incidence"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"laterally inverted"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"diffuse"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Irregular (or diffuse)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"45"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"rod, cone"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":8,"answer":"blind"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"First law: The incident ray, the reflected ray and the normal at the point of incidence all lie in the same plane.\nSecond law: The angle of incidence is equal to the angle of reflection."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"When light is reflected more than once from different reflecting surfaces, it is called multiple reflection of light. It is used in devices like periscope or kaleidoscope (any one use)."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"A kaleidoscope is an instrument in which we can see a large number of beautiful patterns due to multiple reflection in mirrors. It is used by designers of fabrics and wallpapers and by artists."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Rods and cones are two types of light-sensitive cells present on the retina. Rods are sensitive to dim light and cones are sensitive to bright light and colours."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Braille is a system of reading and writing used by the visually impaired. It was developed by Louis Braille."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-09T16:04:48.327Z"},{"id":89,"serialNumber":"CBSE-SCI-Sound-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 8","board":"CBSE","subject":"Science","chapter":"Sound","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":30,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"CBSE Class 8 Science – Worksheet on Sound (NCERT Chapter 13)","instructions":"1. Read each question carefully and answer in the space provided.\n2. For MCQs and True/False, tick (✓) the correct option.\n3. For Fill in the Blanks, write only the correct word(s) from the chapter.\n4. Answer short questions briefly and to the point.\n5. Do not exceed the given space for answers.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist illustration of a tuning fork vibrating with wavy lines showing sound waves spreading out.","position":"top-right","altText":"Vibrating tuning fork producing sound waves"},{"description":"A simple line-art of a boy speaking near a wall with an echo shown as a lighter sound wave returning to his ear.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Boy hearing echo of his own sound near a wall"},{"description":"Minimalist sketch of a drum being hit with a stick, with the stretched membrane vibrating and small curved lines indicating vibrations.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Vibrating drum membrane producing sound"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Sound is produced when:","options":["A. a body is at rest","B. a body vibrates","C. a body moves with uniform speed","D. a body is heated","True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The number of oscillations per second is called:","options":["A. amplitude","B. time period","C. frequency","D. pitch"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. The unit of frequency is:","options":["A. metre","B. second","C. hertz","D. newton"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. The loudness of sound is expressed in:","options":["A. watt","B. decibel","C. joule","D. metre per second"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. Which of the following can produce sound?","options":["A. Vibrating membrane of a drum","B. Still water in a pond","C. Stationary pendulum","D. A book kept on a table"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. Which part of the human ear receives the vibrations from the ear drum and passes them on?","options":["A. ear canal","B. outer ear","C. middle ear","D. inner ear"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. In which of the following is sound produced by the vibration of air column?","options":["A. drum","B. flute","C. tabla","D. violin"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. Which of the following statements is true for a sound that is shrill?","options":["A. It has low frequency and low pitch.","B. It has high frequency and high pitch.","C. It has low amplitude and low pitch.","D. It has high amplitude and low pitch."],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False (Choose the Correct Option)","questions":[{"question":"9. Sound can travel through vacuum.","options":["True","False","Option C","Option D"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. The to and fro motion of an object is called vibration.","options":["True","False","Option C","Option D"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. Sound cannot travel through liquids.","options":["True","False","Option C","Option D"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. The time taken by a vibrating body to complete one oscillation is called its time period.","options":["True","False","Option C","Option D"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. The frequency of a sound determines its pitch.","options":["True","False","Option C","Option D"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"14. A louder sound has less amplitude.","options":["True","False","Option C","Option D"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"15. Sound is produced by __________ objects.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"16. The to and fro or back and forth motion of an object is called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"17. The maximum displacement of a vibrating body from its mean position is called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"18. The unit of frequency is __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"19. The number of oscillations completed in one second is called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"20. A sound of high frequency is said to have a high __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"21. The loudness of sound is measured in __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"22. In humans, the outer ear is called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"23. Sound cannot travel in __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"24. Noise pollution may cause lack of sleep, __________ and hypertension.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"25. Define frequency of a vibration.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"26. What is the relation between frequency and time period of a vibration?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"27. Why are sound waves called mechanical waves?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"28. Name the three main parts of the human ear.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"29. How does increasing the amplitude of vibration affect the loudness of sound?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"30. Mention any two measures to control noise pollution in your surroundings, as suggested in the chapter.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"B. a body vibrates"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"C. frequency"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"C. hertz"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"B. decibel"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"A. Vibrating membrane of a drum"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"C. middle ear"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"B. flute"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"B. It has high frequency and high pitch."},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"vibrating"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"vibration"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"amplitude"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"hertz"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"frequency"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"pitch"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"decibel"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"pinna"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":8,"answer":"vacuum"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":9,"answer":"anxiety"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"The number of oscillations made by a vibrating body in one second is called its frequency."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"The frequency is the reciprocal of time period: frequency = 1 / time period, and time period = 1 / frequency."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Sound waves are called mechanical waves because they require a material medium for their propagation and cannot travel through vacuum."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"The three main parts of the human ear are: outer ear, middle ear and inner ear."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"On increasing the amplitude of vibration, the loudness of sound increases."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Any two: (i) Using silencers in vehicles and machines. (ii) Planting trees along roads and around buildings. (iii) Using loudspeakers at low volumes and for shorter durations. (iv) Avoiding unnecessary use of vehicle horns."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-09T15:59:42.246Z"},{"id":88,"serialNumber":"CBSE-SCI-CombustionAndFlame-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 8","board":"CBSE","subject":"Science","chapter":"Combustion and flame","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":30,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Combustion and Flame – Worksheet (NCERT Class 8 Science, Chapter 6)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully.\n• Attempt all questions in the given space.\n• For MCQs, tick (✓) the correct option.\n• For fill in the blanks, write the correct word(s) in the blank.\n• Answer short questions in 2–3 lines.\n• Use only the concepts, terms and definitions given in NCERT Class 8 Science, Chapter ‘Combustion and Flame’.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist illustration of a candle with a clearly visible blue inner zone and yellow outer zone of the flame","position":"top-right","altText":"Candle flame showing different zones"},{"description":"Simple line-art of a Bunsen burner connected to a gas source with a small blue flame at the top","position":"between-sections","altText":"Bunsen burner with a blue flame"},{"description":"Minimalist drawing of a fire extinguisher spraying on a small campfire with smoke rising","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Fire extinguisher putting out a fire"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A: Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. A chemical process in which a substance reacts with oxygen to give off heat is called:","options":["Calorific value","Combustion","Ignition","Respiration"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The lowest temperature at which a substance catches fire is called its:","options":["Boiling point","Melting point","Ignition temperature","Flash point of water"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Which of the following is a combustible substance?","options":["Iron nail","Glass","Stone piece","LPG"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. Which of the following is used as a fuel in the kitchen?","options":["Wood","Cow dung cakes","LPG","Kerosene stove only"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. The zone of a candle flame which produces soot is:","options":["Innermost zone","Middle zone","Outermost zone","Blue zone near wick"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The unit in which calorific value of a fuel is expressed in this chapter is:","options":["Kilojoule per gram","Kilojoule per kilogram","Joule per second","Kilowatt hour"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The gas responsible for fuel burning incompletely and producing carbon monoxide is:","options":["Excess oxygen","Insufficient oxygen","Nitrogen","Water vapour"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. Which of the following is not a fossil fuel?","options":["Coal","CNG","Biogas","Petroleum"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B: True / False (Choose the correct option)","questions":[{"question":"9. A substance which burns in air to produce heat and light is called a fuel.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. Combustion can take place without oxygen.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. In the outermost zone of a candle flame, complete combustion takes place.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. Water is the best extinguisher for fires involving electrical equipment.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. The middle zone of a candle flame is bright and luminous.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"14. Coal and petroleum are formed from the dead remains of living organisms and are known as fossil fuels.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"15. Carbon monoxide is a highly poisonous gas.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"16. Global warming is a result of increase in the amount of carbon dioxide in air.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C: Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"17. A ___________ is a substance which undergoes combustion to produce heat and light.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"18. The lowest temperature at which a substance catches fire is called its ___________ temperature.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"19. The amount of heat energy produced on complete combustion of 1 kg of a fuel is called its ___________ value.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"20. The gaseous fuel stored in cylinders in our kitchens is called ___________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"21. The middle zone of a candle flame is ___________ and gives out light.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"22. The outermost zone of a candle flame is ___________ in colour and is the hottest part.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section D: Match the Following","questions":[{"question":"23. Match the items in Column A with those in Column B.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"a) Fuel","right":"Substance that is burned to produce heat"},{"left":"b) Ignition temperature","right":"Minimum temperature at which a substance catches fire"},{"left":"c) Calorific value","right":"Amount of heat produced by complete combustion of 1 kg of fuel"},{"left":"d) Water","right":"Extinguishes fire by cooling and cutting off air supply"},{"left":"e) Fire extinguisher","right":"Device used to control or put out fires"}]},{"question":"24. Match the zones of a candle flame in Column A with their characteristics in Column B.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"a) Outermost zone","right":"Blue, hottest, complete combustion"},{"left":"b) Middle zone","right":"Luminous, yellow, partial combustion"},{"left":"c) Innermost zone","right":"Dark, least hot, unburnt vapours of wax"},{"left":"d) Soot","right":"Produced due to incomplete combustion"}]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section E: Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"25. Define combustion as given in the chapter.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"26. Name the three essential conditions required for combustion to take place.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"27. Why is water not used to control fires involving electrical equipment?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"28. What are fossil fuels? Give any two examples mentioned in the chapter.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"29. Why is LPG considered a better domestic fuel than wood according to the textbook?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"30. What is global warming as described in this chapter?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Combustion"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Ignition temperature"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"LPG"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"LPG"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Middle zone"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Kilojoule per kilogram"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"Insufficient oxygen"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"Biogas"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"fuel"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"ignition"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"calorific"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"LPG (Liquefied Petroleum Gas)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"luminous"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"blue"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"a) Fuel – Substance that is burned to produce heat; b) Ignition temperature – Minimum temperature at which a substance catches fire; c) Calorific value – Amount of heat produced by complete combustion of 1 kg of fuel; d) Water – Extinguishes fire by cooling and cutting off air supply; e) Fire extinguisher – Device used to control or put out fires"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"a) Outermost zone – Blue, hottest, complete combustion; b) Middle zone – Luminous, yellow, partial combustion; c) Innermost zone – Dark, least hot, unburnt vapours of wax; d) Soot – Produced due to incomplete combustion"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Combustion is a chemical process in which a substance reacts with oxygen to give off heat. In some cases light is also given off in the form of a flame."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"The three essential conditions are: (i) presence of a combustible substance (fuel), (ii) presence of air (oxygen), and (iii) attainment of the ignition temperature of the substance."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Water is not used for fires involving electrical equipment because water is a good conductor of electricity and may cause electric shocks. It can also damage the electrical equipment."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Fossil fuels are fuels formed from the dead remains of living organisms (fossils). Examples: coal, petroleum, and natural gas (any two)."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"LPG is a better domestic fuel than wood because it has a higher calorific value, burns with a smokeless flame, causes less pollution, and is easy to handle and store."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Global warming is the gradual increase in the average temperature of the earth due to an increase in the amount of carbon dioxide and other gases in the atmosphere produced by human activities such as burning of fuels."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-09T15:57:56.672Z"},{"id":87,"serialNumber":"CBSE-SCI-CoalAndPetroleum-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 8","board":"CBSE","subject":"Science","chapter":"Coal and petroleum ","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":30,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Worksheet – Coal and Petroleum (NCERT Class 8 Science, Chapter 5)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully.\n• Answer in your own words but use the same scientific terms as in the textbook.\n• For MCQs and True/False, tick (✔) the correct option.\n• For Fill in the Blanks, write the correct word(s) in the space provided.\n• Keep your work neat and within the space given.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art showing a coal mine with a cart filled with black coal pieces and a small factory silhouette in the background","position":"top-right","altText":"Illustration of a coal mine cart carrying coal towards a factory"},{"description":"Minimalist, colorful illustration of an oil rig over the sea with drops of crude oil shown in a test tube","position":"between-sections","altText":"Oil rig extracting petroleum with a test tube of crude oil"},{"description":"Simple line-art of three fuel containers labeled LPG, CNG, and Petrol in different colors","position":"bottom-left","altText":"LPG cylinder, CNG cylinder, and a petrol pump icon"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Which of the following is NOT an exhaustible natural resource?","options":["Coal","Petroleum","Natural gas","Air"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Which of the following is a fossil fuel?","options":["Wood","CNG","Biogas","Animal dung"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. The substance mainly formed when dead vegetation gets compressed under high temperature and pressure over millions of years is:","options":["Coke","Coal","Petroleum","Natural gas"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. Which substance is almost pure form of carbon?","options":["Coal tar","Petroleum","Coke","Natural gas"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. The process of separating the different fractions of petroleum is called:","options":["Carbonisation","Fractional distillation","Cracking","Refining"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The petroleum product used as fuel in jet aircrafts is:","options":["LPG","Kerosene","Diesel","Lubricating oil"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The clean fuel which causes very little air pollution and is used as a substitute for petrol and diesel is:","options":["Biogas","CNG","LPG","Kerosene"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. The name given to the national-level conservation campaign to save petroleum is:","options":["Save Coal Movement","Save Petrol Campaign","Petroleum Conservation Research Association (PCRA)","Use Fuels Wisely Programme"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False (Choose the correct option)","questions":[{"question":"9. Coal, petroleum and natural gas are formed from the remains of dead organisms.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. Coal, petroleum and natural gas are inexhaustible natural resources.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. Coal tar is a black, thick liquid with a characteristic unpleasant smell.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. Coke is used in the manufacture of steel and in the extraction of many metals.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. Petrol and diesel are obtained from natural gas.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"14. Petroleum was formed from dead organisms which got buried under the sea.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"15. LPG is a more polluting fuel than coal.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"16. The burning of fossil fuels causes air pollution and produces acid rain.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"17. Resources that are present in unlimited quantity in nature and are not likely to be exhausted by human activities are called __________ natural resources.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"18. The process of conversion of dead vegetation into coal is called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"19. Petroleum is a dark __________ coloured liquid with an unpleasant odour.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"20. The separation of different constituents/fractions of petroleum is known as __________ of petroleum.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"21. Coal, petroleum and natural gas are known as __________ fuels.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"22. A very important constituent of CNG is __________ gas.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section D – Match the Columns","questions":[{"question":"23. Match the following coal products and petroleum fractions with their main uses:","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"A. Coke","right":"1. Fuel for stoves and lamps"},{"left":"B. Coal tar","right":"2. Manufacture of steel"},{"left":"C. Kerosene","right":"3. Road surfacing"},{"left":"D. Bitumen","right":"4. Source of dyes, drugs and perfumes"}]},{"question":"24. Match the following petroleum products with their uses:","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"A. Petrol","right":"1. Fuel for heavy motor vehicles"},{"left":"B. Diesel","right":"2. Fuel for aircrafts"},{"left":"C. Kerosene","right":"3. Fuel for light motor vehicles"},{"left":"D. Lubricating oil","right":"4. Greasing of machine parts"}]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section E – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"25. Name two inexhaustible and two exhaustible natural resources mentioned in this chapter.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"26. Why are coal, petroleum and natural gas called fossil fuels?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"27. List any two uses of coal besides being used as a fuel.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"28. State any two uses of natural gas.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"29. Why should we use fossil fuels only when absolutely necessary?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"30. State any two suggestions given by PCRA to save petrol and diesel.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Air"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"CNG"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Coal"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Coke"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Fractional distillation"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Kerosene"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"CNG"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"Petroleum Conservation Research Association (PCRA)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"inexhaustible"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"carbonisation"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"oily"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"refining"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"fossil"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"methane"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"A-2, B-4, C-1, D-3"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"A-3, B-1, C-2, D-4"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Inexhaustible: air, sunlight; Exhaustible: coal, petroleum (any two correct examples from the chapter for each are acceptable)."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"They are called fossil fuels because they were formed from the remains of dead organisms (plants and animals) that were buried and subjected to high temperature and pressure over millions of years."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Coal is used: (i) in thermal power plants to generate electricity, (ii) in industry as a source of organic chemicals like dyes, drugs, perfumes, etc. (any two uses from the chapter)."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Natural gas is used as a fuel in homes and factories and as an industrial fuel in thermal power plants (any two uses from the chapter)."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Because coal, petroleum and natural gas are exhaustible natural resources; they are limited in nature and may get exhausted if used excessively. Their burning also causes air pollution and contributes to global warming and acid rain."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Any two from PCRA’s suggestions: (i) drive vehicles at a constant and moderate speed, (ii) switch off the engine at traffic lights or long stops, (iii) ensure regular maintenance and proper air pressure in tyres, (iv) use public transport or car pools as far as possible."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-09T15:56:00.860Z"},{"id":86,"serialNumber":"CBSE-SCI-ReachingTheAge-002","userId":3,"className":"Grade 8","board":"CBSE","subject":"Science","chapter":"","topic":"Reaching the age of adolescence ","difficulty":"medium","length":30,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Reaching the Age of Adolescence – Worksheet (NCERT Class 8 Science, Ch. 8)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully and answer in the space provided.\n• Attempt all questions. All are based on NCERT Class 8 Science Chapter 8: Reaching the Age of Adolescence.\n• For MCQs and True/False, tick (✓) the correct option.\n• For fill in the blanks, write only the correct word(s) in the blank.\n• Answer in your own words but as per definitions and explanations in the textbook.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art of two children, a boy and a girl, standing back-to-back with height marks on a wall showing their growth during adolescence.","position":"top-right","altText":"Illustration of growing adolescents with a height chart."},{"description":"Minimalist, colorful icons showing a brain, a heart, and a hormone droplet connected by arrows to represent changes controlled by hormones in adolescence.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Icons of brain, heart and hormone drop indicating hormonal control of changes."},{"description":"Simple line-art of a balanced plate of food (cereals, pulses, vegetables, fruits, milk) with bright colors to show a balanced diet for adolescents.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Balanced diet plate illustration for adolescents."}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. The period of life when the body undergoes changes leading to reproductive maturity is called:","options":["Adulthood","Adolescence","Infancy","Old age"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Adolescence begins around the age of ______ years and lasts up to ______ years of age.","options":["5, 10","18, 25","11, 18 or 19","2, 6"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. The human beings who are in the age group of 11 to 18 or 19 years are called:","options":["Adults","Children","Adolescents","Infants"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. The period of life, when the body of a boy or girl becomes capable of reproduction, is called:","options":["Menopause","Menstruation","Puberty","Childhood"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. The male hormone secreted by the testes is:","options":["Oestrogen","Progesterone","Insulin","Testosterone"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The female hormone secreted by the ovaries is mainly:","options":["Thyroxine","Adrenaline","Oestrogen","Testosterone"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The master gland that controls the activity of all other endocrine glands is:","options":["Adrenal gland","Pituitary gland","Thyroid gland","Pancreas"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. The endocrine gland that prepares the body to face an emergency situation is:","options":["Thyroid gland","Adrenal gland","Pituitary gland","Pancreas"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False (Choose the Correct Option)","questions":[{"question":"9. Adolescence is the period between the ages of 11 and 18 or 19 years.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. The larynx develops more in girls than in boys during adolescence.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. The onset of menstruation marks the beginning of puberty in girls.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. Hormones are secreted by endocrine glands directly into the blood.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. The sex of the unborn child is determined by the mother.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"14. It is important to avoid drugs and alcohol during adolescence.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"15. The ______ period extends from puberty to the attainment of reproductive maturity.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"16. Puberty begins at about ______ years in girls and ______ years in boys.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"17. Increase in height, change in body shape, and voice change are ______ changes in adolescents.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"18. The shoulder of boys generally becomes ______ than that of girls, while the region below the waist becomes wider in ______.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"19. The time between one menstruation and the next is called the ______ cycle.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"20. Endocrine glands release hormones into the ______ stream.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"21. The gland which secretes thyroxine is the ______ gland.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"22. A diet containing all nutrients in the right amount is called a ______ diet.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"23. Define adolescence as given in the NCERT textbook.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"24. What is puberty?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"25. List any two secondary sexual characters in boys and any two in girls.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"26. Name the hormones produced by testes and ovaries and state one function of each.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section E – Match the Columns","questions":[{"question":"27. Match the endocrine glands in Column A with their hormones or functions in Column B:","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"A. Pituitary gland","right":"1. Prepares the body to face an emergency"},{"left":"B. Thyroid gland","right":"2. Controls the activity of all other endocrine glands"},{"left":"C. Adrenal gland","right":"3. Controls the rate of metabolism"},{"left":"D. Pancreas","right":"4. Controls the sugar level in the blood"}]},{"question":"28. Match the terms in Column A with their correct description in Column B:","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"A. Menstruation","right":"1. Increase in height and weight during adolescence"},{"left":"B. Growth spurt","right":"2. The release of the ovum by an ovary"},{"left":"C. Ovulation","right":"3. The cyclic shedding of the lining of the uterus"},{"left":"D. Secondary sexual characters","right":"4. Features that help distinguish males from females"}]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section F – One Word / Very Short Answer","questions":[{"question":"29. Which gland is known as the master gland?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"30. Name the period in females when menstruation stops and the woman can no longer reproduce.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Adolescence"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"11, 18 or 19"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Adolescents"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Puberty"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Testosterone"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Oestrogen"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"Pituitary gland"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"Adrenal gland"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"adolescence"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"10, 11–13 (Girls: about 10 years; Boys: about 11–13 years — as given that puberty begins a year or two earlier in girls than in boys)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"secondary sexual"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"wider, girls"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"menstrual"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"blood"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"thyroid"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"balanced"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Adolescence is the period of life, between 11 and 18 or 19 years of age, when the body undergoes changes leading to reproductive maturity."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Puberty is the period of life when the body of a boy or girl becomes capable of reproduction."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Boys: (any two) growth of facial hair (moustache and beard), broadening of shoulders, growth of hair on chest, underarms and pubic region, enlargement of voice box and deepening of voice.\nGirls: (any two) development of breasts, broader hips, growth of hair in the armpits and pubic region."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Testes produce the male hormone testosterone which controls the development of secondary sexual characters in boys.\nOvaries produce the female hormone oestrogen which controls the development of secondary sexual characters in girls and also helps in the maturation and release of ova."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"A–2, B–3, C–1, D–4"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"A–3, B–1, C–2, D–4"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Pituitary gland"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Menopause"}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-03-09T15:54:20.259Z"},{"id":85,"serialNumber":"CBSE-SCI-ReachingTheAge-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 8","board":"CBSE","subject":"Science","chapter":"","topic":"Reaching the age of adolescence ","difficulty":"medium","length":30,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Reaching the Age of Adolescence – Worksheet (NCERT Class 8 Science, Chapter 10)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully and answer in the space provided.\n• For MCQs and True/False, tick (✓) the correct option.\n• For Fill in the Blanks, write only the correct word(s) from the chapter.\n• Answer Short Answer questions in 1–3 sentences.\n• Base all answers strictly on NCERT Class 8 Science textbook, Chapter 10: Reaching the Age of Adolescence.","graphics":[{"description":"Colorful minimalist line-art of two adolescents, a boy and a girl, growing taller with a height scale beside them and subtle icons of hormones around.","position":"top-right","altText":"Illustration showing growth in height during adolescence"},{"description":"Simple colorful line drawing of a brain, pituitary gland, and thyroid linked with arrows to show control of endocrine glands.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Illustration of endocrine glands and their control"},{"description":"Minimalist colorful sketch of human chromosomes inside a cell with X and Y symbols to indicate sex determination.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Illustration of sex chromosomes X and Y"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Adolescence is the period of life when the body undergoes changes leading to\n(1) old age\n(2) adulthood\n(3) childhood\n(4) infancy","options":["old age","adulthood","childhood","infancy"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The period of adolescence begins around the age of\n(1) 2–3 years\n(2) 5–7 years\n(3) 11–13 years\n(4) 20–25 years","options":["2–3 years","5–7 years","11–13 years","20–25 years"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. The human body undergoes many changes during\n(1) puberty\n(2) fertilisation\n(3) menopause\n(4) lactation","options":["puberty","fertilisation","menopause","lactation"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. Changes at puberty are controlled by chemicals called\n(1) enzymes\n(2) hormones\n(3) vitamins\n(4) antibodies","options":["enzymes","hormones","vitamins","antibodies"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. The male hormone produced by the testes is called\n(1) oestrogen\n(2) insulin\n(3) testosterone\n(4) progesterone","options":["oestrogen","insulin","testosterone","progesterone"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The term used for “mental and emotional maturity” according to the chapter is\n(1) physical health\n(2) reproductive health\n(3) emotional maturity\n(4) mental maturity","options":["physical health","reproductive health","emotional maturity","mental maturity"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The gland that is called the master gland is the\n(1) thyroid\n(2) adrenal\n(3) pituitary\n(4) pancreas","options":["thyroid","adrenal","pituitary","pancreas"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. The sex of the unborn child is determined by the\n(1) mother’s blood\n(2) father’s sperm\n(3) mother’s ovum\n(4) uterus","options":["mother’s blood","father’s sperm","mother’s ovum","uterus"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False (Choose the Correct Option)","questions":[{"question":"9. Adolescents should avoid addictive substances like drugs and alcohol.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. Puberty ends when an adolescent becomes an adult.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. The increase in height in boys and girls is the same at all ages.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. Voice box or larynx enlarges in boys during puberty.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. The pituitary gland secretes growth hormone.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"14. The sex chromosomes are named X and Y.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"15. The period of life, when the body undergoes changes, leading to reproductive maturity, is called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"16. The human beings become capable of reproduction after __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"17. The changes which occur in the body and mark the onset of puberty are called __________ changes.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"18. The male reproductive organs are the testes, sperm ducts and __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"19. The female reproductive organs are a pair of ovaries, oviducts and the __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"20. Hormones are secreted by the endocrine glands directly into the __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"21. The hormone produced by the thyroid gland is called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"22. The __________ gland is located on top of both the kidneys.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"23. Define adolescence as given in the chapter.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"24. What is puberty?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"25. Name any two secondary sexual characters in boys and any two in girls mentioned in the chapter.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"26. What role does the pituitary gland play in reaching reproductive maturity?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"27. Why should adolescents eat a balanced diet according to the chapter?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"28. How is the sex of a baby determined according to the chapter?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section E – Match the Columns","questions":[{"question":"29. Match the glands in Column A with the hormones they secrete in Column B.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"A. Thyroid","right":"1. Insulin"},{"left":"B. Pancreas","right":"2. Adrenaline"},{"left":"C. Adrenal gland","right":"3. Thyroxine"},{"left":"D. Testes","right":"4. Oestrogen"},{"left":"E. Ovary","right":"5. Testosterone"}]},{"question":"30. Match the terms in Column A with the correct descriptions in Column B.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"A. Larynx","right":"1. Controls growth and reproduction"},{"left":"B. Pituitary gland","right":"2. Develops into Adam’s apple in boys"},{"left":"C. Adolescence","right":"3. Beginning of adolescence"},{"left":"D. Puberty","right":"4. Period of life from about 11 to 19 years"}]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"adulthood"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"11–13 years"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"puberty"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"hormones"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"testosterone"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"reproductive health (mental and emotional maturity are also discussed, but the chapter stresses total health including physical and mental health; the closest term in context is reproductive health with maturity)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"pituitary"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"father’s sperm"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"adolescence"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"puberty"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"secondary sexual"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"penis"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"uterus"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"blood"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"thyroxine"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"adrenal"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Adolescence is the period of life, between childhood and adulthood, when the body undergoes changes, leading to reproductive maturity."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Puberty is the period during adolescence when the body of boys and girls undergoes changes that lead to reproductive maturity."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Boys: growth of facial hair (moustache and beard), voice becomes hoarse.\nGirls: development of breasts, broadening of hips."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"The pituitary gland secretes hormones that control the functioning of other endocrine glands and also produces growth hormone that helps in body growth and reaching reproductive maturity."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Adolescents need a balanced diet to provide proper nourishment for rapid growth and development, to keep the body healthy and to cope with the increased activities during this period."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"The sex of a baby is determined by the type of sex chromosome carried by the sperm that fuses with the X-chromosome of the egg. If an X-bearing sperm fuses with the egg, the baby will be a girl (XX), and if a Y-bearing sperm fuses with the egg, the baby will be a boy (XY)."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"A–3, B–1, C–2, D–5, E–4\n(Thyroid–Thyroxine, Pancreas–Insulin, Adrenal gland–Adrenaline, Testes–Testosterone, Ovary–Oestrogen)"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"A–2, B–1, C–4, D–3\n(Larynx–Develops into Adam’s apple in boys, Pituitary gland–Controls growth and reproduction, Adolescence–Period of life from about 11 to 19 years, Puberty–Beginning of adolescence)"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-09T15:53:39.797Z"},{"id":84,"serialNumber":"CBSE-MAT-TimeAndCalander-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 1","board":"CBSE","subject":"Maths","chapter":"Time and calander","topic":"Every day events","difficulty":"medium","length":20,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Time and Calendar — Everyday Events (NCERT Math-Magic 1, Chapter: Time and Calendar)","instructions":"Dear child, look at each question carefully and choose or write your answer. Think about what you do in the morning, afternoon, evening and night, just like in your Math-Magic book chapter ‘Time and Calendar’.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful clock with big hour and minute hands, rays like the sun around it, and small stars in the background","position":"top-right","altText":"Smiling clock showing time with sun-like rays"},{"description":"Four small pictures in a row: a child brushing teeth (morning), a child eating lunch (afternoon), a child playing outside (evening), and a child sleeping in bed (night)","position":"between-sections","altText":"Everyday events of morning, afternoon, evening and night"},{"description":"A simple 7-day calendar strip with boxes labelled Sun, Mon, Tue, Wed, Thu, Fri, Sat in bright colors","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Colorful weekly calendar strip"}],"graphicEmojis":["⏰","🌞","🌙","📅","✏️"],"sections":[{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section A: Fill in the Blanks (Everyday Events and Time Words)","questions":[{"question":"1. We brush our teeth in the __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. We eat our dinner at __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. We go to school in the __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. We see the moon at __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. Sunday, Monday, Tuesday are names of __________ of the week.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. There are __________ days in a week.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The first day of the week is __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B: Multiple Choice Questions (Everyday Events)","questions":[{"question":"8. When do you usually wake up and get ready for school?","options":["morning","afternoon","evening","night"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. When do you usually play outside after coming back from school?","options":["morning","afternoon","evening","night"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. When do you usually sleep?","options":["morning","afternoon","evening","night"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. On which day do many children have a holiday from school?","options":["Monday","Wednesday","Sunday","Friday"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. Which of these is the correct order?","options":["morning, night, evening, afternoon","night, afternoon, evening, morning","morning, afternoon, evening, night","afternoon, morning, night, evening"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. When do you usually have lunch?","options":["morning","afternoon","evening","night"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section C: True or False (Tick the Correct Option)","questions":[{"question":"14. We see the sun in the morning.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"15. We go to school at night.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"16. There are 7 days in a week.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"17. We sleep at night.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"18. We eat breakfast in the evening.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section D: Match the Everyday Events with Time of Day","questions":[{"question":"19. Match each activity in Column A with the correct time of day in Column B.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"a) Brushing teeth","right":"morning"},{"left":"b) Eating lunch","right":"afternoon"},{"left":"c) Playing outside","right":"evening"},{"left":"d) Sleeping","right":"night"}]},{"question":"20. Match the day names in Column A with their correct order number in Column B.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"a) Sunday","right":"1st day"},{"left":"b) Monday","right":"2nd day"},{"left":"c) Tuesday","right":"3rd day"},{"left":"d) Wednesday","right":"4th day"}]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"morning"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"night"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"morning"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"night"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"days"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"7"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"Sunday"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"morning"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"evening"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"night"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Sunday"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"morning, afternoon, evening, night"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"afternoon"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"a) Brushing teeth – morning; b) Eating lunch – afternoon; c) Playing outside – evening; d) Sleeping – night"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"a) Sunday – 1st day; b) Monday – 2nd day; c) Tuesday – 3rd day; d) Wednesday – 4th day"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-08T07:51:01.805Z"},{"id":83,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-ENG-FromARailway-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"english","chapter":"from a railway carriage","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"From a Railway Carriage – Worksheet (English Balbharati Std 7)","instructions":"Read the poem carefully from your English Balbharati (Std 7) textbook before attempting this worksheet. Answer all questions neatly. Write the answers in complete sentences where required.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist drawing of a speeding train passing green fields and small houses","position":"top-right","altText":"Speeding train near fields and houses as seen from a railway carriage window"},{"description":"Simple line-art of children waving at a passing train near a small station","position":"between-sections","altText":"Children standing near tracks waving at a passing train"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of trees and telegraph posts flashing past in the background","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Trees and telegraph posts appearing to move quickly past a train window"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Who is the poet of the poem \"From a Railway Carriage\"?","options":["William Wordsworth","Robert Louis Stevenson","Rabindranath Tagore","Sarojini Naidu"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"2. The poem \"From a Railway Carriage\" describes mainly the experience of:","options":["walking along a road","sailing in a boat","looking out of a moving train","flying in an aeroplane"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"3. In the poem, how does the poet describe the movement of the train?","options":["Faster than honour","Faster than fairies, faster than witches","Slower than a snail","Slow and steady"],"answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks (from the poem)","questions":[{"question":"4. \"Faster than ________, faster than ________,\"","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"5. \"Here is a child who ______ and ______,\"","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"6. \"And charging along like _______\"","answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section C – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"7. What are the natural scenes that the poet sees from the railway carriage?","answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"8. What human activities does the poet notice as the train passes by?","answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"9. Why does everything seem to fly by quickly, according to the poem?","answerSpaceLines":2}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section D – Match the Following (Words from the Poem)","questions":[{"question":"10. Match the words in Column A with their correct meanings in Column B.","answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"a) Scramble","right":"i) Move quickly in an awkward way"},{"left":"b) Witches","right":"ii) Women thought to have magical powers"},{"left":"c) Ditches","right":"iii) Long narrow holes dug in the ground"},{"left":"d) Charging","right":"iv) Rushing forward with force"},{"left":"e) Cantering","right":"v) Moving at a gentle gallop"}]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Robert Louis Stevenson"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"looking out of a moving train"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Faster than fairies, faster than witches"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"fairies, witches"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"scrambles, scrambles"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"troops in a battle"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"The poet sees hills and plains, meadows, grassland, daisies, and also trees and houses that seem to run away as the train speeds by."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"He notices a tramp standing and gazing, a farmer in the field, a child clambering and scrambling, and people doing their work near the railway line."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Because the train is moving very fast, all the scenes, people, and objects outside the window seem to fly by quickly like a dream."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"a) Scramble – i) Move quickly in an awkward way\nb) Witches – ii) Women thought to have magical powers\nc) Ditches – iii) Long narrow holes dug in the ground\nd) Charging – iv) Rushing forward with force\ne) Cantering – v) Moving at a gentle gallop"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T17:57:59.130Z"},{"id":82,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-ENG-TheBrook-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"english","chapter":"the brook","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Brook – Worksheet (English Balbharati Std 7, Maharashtra Board)","instructions":"Read the poem ‘The Brook’ from your English Balbharati (Std 7) textbook carefully before attempting this worksheet. Answer all questions in the spaces provided. Write neatly and keep your answers brief and to the point.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple, colorful line-art drawing of a narrow brook flowing between green banks with a small bridge over it","position":"top-right","altText":"A small brook flowing under a bridge"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of pebbles and a small fish jumping out of the water of a tiny stream","position":"between-sections","altText":"Pebbles and fish in a brook"},{"description":"Simple line-art of hills with a brook starting from the hillside and winding down into the plain","position":"bottom-left","altText":"A brook flowing down from the hills"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1) Who is the speaker in the poem ‘The Brook’ in your English Balbharati textbook?","options":["The poet","The brook itself","A fisherman","A shepherd"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2) In the refrain, the brook says, “For men may come and men may go, ______________.”","options":["And I will stop one day","But I go on for ever","And I also go away","Yet I return again"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3) The brook says that it comes \"from haunts of coot and hern.\" What are ‘coot’ and ‘hern’?","options":["Types of fish","Types of birds","Types of insects","Types of plants"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks (from the poem)","questions":[{"question":"4) \"I come from ______ of coot and hern, I make a sudden sally.\"","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5) \"By thirty ______ I hurry down, or slip between the ridges.\"","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6) \"I murmur under _______ fern, I bicker down a valley.\"","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7) \"I chatter over stony ways, in little sharps and _______.\"","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section C – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"8) Who wrote the poem ‘The Brook’ given in your English Balbharati Std 7 textbook?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9) Quote the refrain (repeated line) that appears again and again in the poem ‘The Brook’.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10) What does the brook do to the ‘pebbles’? Write the exact word used in the poem and explain briefly in one sentence.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"Section D – Long Answer / Appreciation","questions":[{"question":"11) Describe the journey of the brook from its source in the hills till it joins the river, as described in the poem in your textbook. Mention at least four different things or places the brook passes by or through.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12) What is the central idea (theme) of the poem ‘The Brook’? How does the repeated line “For men may come and men may go, but I go on for ever.” help to bring out this idea?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section E – Match the Following (from the poem)","questions":[{"question":"13) Match the words from the poem with their meanings.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"a) bicker","right":"to flow noisily, with a flickering movement"},{"left":"b) sally","right":"a sudden rush or movement"},{"left":"c) brimming","right":"full to the top"},{"left":"d) haunts","right":"places where birds or animals usually live or visit"},{"left":"e) chattered","right":"made a series of quick, light sounds while flowing"}]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section F – Vocabulary and Figures of Speech","questions":[{"question":"14) The brook is given human qualities and speaks in the poem. Name this figure of speech and give one example line from the poem.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"15) Pick out any two pairs of rhyming words from the first two stanzas of the poem as given in your textbook.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"The brook itself"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"But I go on for ever"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Types of birds"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"haunts"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"bridges"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"cinquefoil"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"trebles"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Alfred Lord Tennyson"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"“For men may come and men may go,\nBut I go on for ever.”"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"The brook ‘frets’ over the pebbles; this means it rubs and wears them down as it flows quickly over them."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"In the poem, the brook begins from the ‘haunts of coot and hern’ high in the hills. It ‘makes a sudden sally’ and flows down the valley, slipping between ridges, sliding by twenty thorps and a little town. It flows by fields and lawns and under twenty bridges. It moves past villages, fairyland-like places with willow-weed and mallow, and finally ‘steals by lawns and grassy plots’ till it joins the ‘brimming river’ in the end."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"The central idea of the poem ‘The Brook’ is the everlasting, continuous flow of nature in contrast to the short and changing life of human beings. The brook keeps flowing from the hills to the river without stopping, while generations of people are born and die. The repeated line “For men may come and men may go, but I go on for ever.” clearly shows that men are temporary, but the brook (symbolising nature and the flow of life) is eternal and goes on forever. This refrain reminds the reader of the contrast again and again."},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"a) bicker – to flow noisily, with a flickering movement\nb) sally – a sudden rush or movement\nc) brimming – full to the top\nd) haunts – places where birds or animals usually live or visit\ne) chattered – made a series of quick, light sounds while flowing"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"The figure of speech is Personification.\nExample: “I chatter, chatter, as I flow” or “I wind about, and in and out” – here the brook speaks like a human being."},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Any two correct pairs from the first two stanzas, for example:\n• hern – fern\n• valley – sally\n(Other correct rhyming pairs from those stanzas as printed in the textbook are also acceptable.)"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T17:52:08.417Z"},{"id":81,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-ENG-TheSouvenir-010","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"english","chapter":"The Souvenir","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Souvenir – Worksheet (English Balbharati Std 7, Maharashtra Board)","instructions":"Read the lesson ‘The Souvenir’ from your English Balbharati (Std 7) textbook carefully before answering. Attempt all questions. Write neat and complete answers in the given space.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art of a small village house with a tree and a winding path, suggesting the boy’s hometown that he visits in ‘The Souvenir’.","position":"top-right","altText":"Village house and tree representing the setting of The Souvenir"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a boy holding a stone and smiling at an elderly man, showing the moment when the boy receives the souvenir.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Boy receiving a souvenir stone from an old man"},{"description":"Small colorful sketch of a notebook and pencil with a tiny stone kept on the page, indicating writing about the souvenir.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Notebook and pencil with a souvenir stone on it"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. In the lesson ‘The Souvenir’, why had the boy gone back to his native place?","options":["A. To spend his summer vacation","B. To attend a wedding","C. To meet his sick grandfather","D. To attend a festival"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"2. Where did the boy sit down to rest when he felt tired?","options":["A. On a rock near the river","B. On the steps of a small hut","C. Under a tree beside the road","D. On a bench at the bus stop"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"3. What did the old man finally give the boy as a souvenir?","options":["A. A coin","B. A colourful shell","C. A small stone","D. A book"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"4. What did the old man call the small presents that tourists usually take away?","options":["A. Gifts","B. Souvenirs","C. Prizes","D. Rewards"],"answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"5. The boy wanted to buy a __________ for himself from his native place as a memory of his visit.","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"6. The old man picked up a small __________ from the roadside and gave it to the boy.","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"7. The boy realised that it is the __________ behind a gift that really matters.","answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section C – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"8. Why was the boy disappointed when he looked at the shops in the village?","answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"9. What did the old man tell the boy about spending money on souvenirs?","answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"10. Why did the boy decide to keep the stone carefully?","answerSpaceLines":2}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"A. To spend his summer vacation"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"C. Under a tree beside the road"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"C. A small stone"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"B. Souvenirs"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"souvenir"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"stone"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"feeling"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"He was disappointed because the shops did not have anything special or attractive that he really wanted to buy as a souvenir. The things there looked ordinary and did not appeal to him."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"The old man told the boy that it was not necessary to spend a lot of money on souvenirs. Any simple thing, taken with love and good memories, could be a souvenir."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"He decided to keep the stone carefully because it reminded him of the old man’s kindness and the lesson that the value of a gift lies in the feeling and memory attached to it."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T17:46:13.237Z"},{"id":80,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-ENG-TheSouvenir-009","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"english","chapter":"The Souvenir","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Souvenir – Worksheet (English Balbharati Std 7, Maharashtra Board)","instructions":"Read the lesson ‘The Souvenir’ from your English Balbharati (Std 7) textbook carefully before answering. Answer all questions. Tick the correct option for MCQs and write only the missing words for Fill in the Blanks.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art of a boy carefully placing a small shell or pebble in a box labelled ‘Souvenirs’.","position":"top-right","altText":"Boy keeping a small souvenir safely in a box"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a calm seaside scene with a boat and a small house on the shore, drawn in soft colours.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Seaside with a boat and a house near the shore"},{"description":"Simple notebook and pencil icon with a tiny keepsake tied with a ribbon beside it, in bright colours.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Notebook, pencil and a small keepsake"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Where did the family go to spend their vacation in the lesson ‘The Souvenir’?","options":["To a hill station","To a seaside town","To a big crowded city","To a jungle camp"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Why did the parents decide not to buy any expensive things from the shops near the beach?","options":["They did not like anything in the shops.","They wanted to save money to buy a new car.","They did not want to waste money on useless things.","The children were not allowed to enter the shops."],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. What does the word ‘souvenir’ mean in the context of the lesson?","options":["A big and costly present","A small thing that reminds us of a person, place or event","A game that children play on the beach","A special type of food eaten on holidays"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. What did the children finally choose as their souvenir from the visit?","options":["A toy boat from the shop","An expensive shell necklace","A small shell/pebble from the beach","A postcard from the hotel"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. According to the lesson, what is MORE important than buying gifts and things from a place we visit?","options":["Taking many photographs","Bringing back lots of food items","Collecting many tickets and bills","The happy memories and experiences we have"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The children in the story are excited mainly because –","options":["they will miss their school homework","they are going on a vacation with their parents","they are going to write an exam","they will get new clothes for a festival"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. In the lesson, what did the mother suggest the children should do to remember the vacation?","options":["Write about it in their diary or notebook","Keep watching television","Sleep the whole day","Buy as many toys as possible"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"8. A __________ is a small thing that reminds us of a person, place or event.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. The children walked along the __________, looking at the waves and shells.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. Mother told the children that the best souvenir is the __________ we carry in our minds.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"To a seaside town"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"They did not want to waste money on useless things."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"A small thing that reminds us of a person, place or event"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"A small shell/pebble from the beach"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"The happy memories and experiences we have"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"they are going on a vacation with their parents"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"Write about it in their diary or notebook"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"souvenir"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"beach"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"memories"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T17:42:00.694Z"},{"id":76,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-ENG-TheSouvenir-008","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"english","chapter":"The Souvenir","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Souvenir – Worksheet (English Balbharati Std 7)","instructions":"Read the lesson 'The Souvenir' from your English Balbharati (Std 7) textbook carefully. Then fill in the blanks with suitable words or short phrases from the lesson. Write answers in neat handwriting and with correct spelling.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art of a schoolboy holding a small seashell carefully in his palm, with gentle sea waves drawn behind him","position":"top-right","altText":"Boy holding a souvenir seashell with the sea in the background"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a classroom desk with an open English textbook titled 'The Souvenir' and a pen beside it","position":"between-sections","altText":"Open English textbook on a school desk"},{"description":"Small colorful sketch of footprints in wet sand leading towards a suitcase, suggesting travel and memories","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Footprints in sand near a travel bag"}],"sections":[{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section A – Fill in the Blanks (Based on the Lesson)","questions":[{"question":"1) The lesson \"The Souvenir\" is about a boy named __________ and the special gift he receives after a trip.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2) The word \"souvenir\" in the lesson means a thing that we keep to remember a special __________ or place.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3) In the story, the family goes on a trip during the __________ vacation.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4) At the beach, the children enjoyed playing in the water and collecting beautiful __________ from the shore as souvenirs.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5) The boy carefully kept his favourite souvenir in a small __________ so that it would not get lost or broken.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Vocabulary from the Lesson","questions":[{"question":"6) Fill in the blank with the correct word from the lesson: A __________ is something that reminds you of a person, place or event you do not want to forget.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7) The boy felt very __________ when he remembered all the happy moments of the trip while looking at his souvenir.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8) The mother tells the children that real souvenirs are not always expensive things, but the __________ we carry in our hearts.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Grammar and Usage from the Lesson","questions":[{"question":"9) Fill in the correct form of the verb as used in the lesson: They __________ (decide) to go to the beach together and enjoy the day.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10) Choose the correct preposition from the lesson and fill in the blank: The boy kept the souvenir __________ his cupboard so that he could see it every day.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"the main boy-character’s name as given in the textbook (write the same name used in the lesson \"The Souvenir\")"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"event"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"vacation"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"shells"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"box"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"souvenir"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"happy"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"memories"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"decided"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"in / inside (as used in the textbook sentence)"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T17:33:15.390Z"},{"id":73,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-ENG-TheSouvenir-007","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"english","chapter":"The Souvenir","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Souvenir – Worksheet (English Balbharati Std 7, Maharashtra Board)","instructions":"Read the lesson 'The Souvenir' from your English Balbharati Std 7 textbook carefully before attempting this worksheet. Answer all questions. Choose the correct option for MCQs and fill in the blanks with suitable words from the lesson. Write neatly.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art of a boy and a girl standing at a hill-station viewpoint with trees and mountains behind them, each holding a small souvenir in hand.","position":"top-right","altText":"Children at a hill-station holding small souvenirs"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a diary, a small pressed flower, and a pen placed on a table.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Diary with a pressed flower souvenir and pen"},{"description":"Colorful line-art of a cupboard shelf with a few simple objects: a stone, a shell, and a small toy arranged like keepsakes.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Shelf with simple souvenir objects"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. In the lesson 'The Souvenir', what is the meaning of the word 'souvenir'?","options":["A kind of food eaten during a journey","A thing that is kept as a reminder of a person, place or event","A ticket used to travel by train","A place where tourists stay"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Where did the children go for their trip in the lesson 'The Souvenir'?","options":["To a village fair","To a beach","To a hill-station","To a museum in the city"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Who suggested that the children should collect something as a souvenir of the trip?","options":["Mother","Father","The teacher","The guide"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. What did the teacher tell the children to do in their notebooks during the trip?","options":["Write only the names of shops","Draw cartoons of each other","Note down what they saw and how they felt","Write only the time of departure and arrival"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. Which of the following is mentioned in the lesson as something children thought of buying as a souvenir?","options":["A bicycle","A big wooden box","A pen-stand and key-chains","A school uniform"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. Why did the teacher advise the children not to waste money on useless things?","options":["Because the shop was going to close","Because their bags were already full","Because a simple thing can also remind them of the trip","Because they were not allowed to buy anything ever"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. What did one of the children finally decide to keep as a souvenir from the hill-station?","options":["A giant toy","A pressed wild flower","An expensive watch","A packet of sweets"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"8. A __________ is something that we keep to remind us of a person, place or event.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. In the lesson, the children went to a __________ for their school trip.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. The teacher asked the children to write about what they saw and how they __________ during the trip.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"A thing that is kept as a reminder of a person, place or event"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"To a hill-station"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"The teacher"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Note down what they saw and how they felt"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"A pen-stand and key-chains"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Because a simple thing can also remind them of the trip"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"A pressed wild flower"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"souvenir"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"hill-station"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"felt"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T17:25:59.881Z"},{"id":72,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-ENG-TheSouvenir-006","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"english","chapter":"The Souvenir","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Souvenir – Multiple Choice Worksheet (English Balbharati Std. 7)","instructions":"Read each question carefully and choose the most appropriate answer from the four options given. Fill in the correct option (A/B/C/D) in your notebook.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple, colorful line-art drawing of a school corridor with a notice board and a girl holding a small wrapped gift in her hand","position":"top-right","altText":"Girl holding a small souvenir in a school corridor"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of two classmates sharing and comparing small objects like a stone, a leaf and a badge on a desk","position":"between-sections","altText":"Classmates sharing souvenirs on a school desk"},{"description":"Simple line-art of an open notebook with a tiny pressed flower and a ticket stub kept safely inside","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Notebook with small souvenir items preserved inside"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"In the lesson \"The Souvenir\", where were the students going on a visit?","options":["To a museum","To a science exhibition","To a fort near their town","To the zoo"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"What does the word \"souvenir\" mean in the context of the lesson?","options":["A special kind of game","A thing that reminds you of a person, place or event","A food item to share with friends","A poem written in memory of someone"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Who first suggested bringing back a souvenir from the visit?","options":["The class teacher","The monitor of the class","One of the students","The bus driver"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"According to the lesson, which of the following is given as an example of a souvenir?","options":["A maths textbook","An ordinary school pencil","A seashell collected on the beach","A water bottle"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Why did the teacher warn the students while talking about souvenirs?","options":["So that they would not get tired","So that they would not be late for the bus","So that they would not dirty their uniforms","So that they would not damage anything or take away what they were not supposed to"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"What did the teacher say was the best souvenir the students could bring back?","options":["Photographs of the place","Stones and leaves","Good memories and what they had learnt","Snacks from the canteen"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"In the lesson, what did one of the students want to do with the stone he picked up?","options":["Throw it into the river","Use it to decorate the classroom","Keep it safely in his bag as a memory","Gift it to the bus driver"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"What did the teacher ask the students to do after returning from the visit?","options":["Write an essay at home","Prepare a chart and share their souvenirs and experiences in class","Clean the classroom","Memorise a poem from the textbook"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Which of these best expresses the main message of \"The Souvenir\"?","options":["We should always collect expensive things.","We should compete to bring the biggest souvenir.","Memories and learning are more valuable than objects.","School trips are only for enjoyment."],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"In the lesson, what attitude does the teacher encourage when visiting new places?","options":["Carelessness and fun","Care, respect and observation","Silent and no questions","Collecting as many things as possible"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"To a fort near their town"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"A thing that reminds you of a person, place or event"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"One of the students"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"A seashell collected on the beach"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"So that they would not damage anything or take away what they were not supposed to"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"Good memories and what they had learnt"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"Keep it safely in his bag as a memory"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"Prepare a chart and share their souvenirs and experiences in class"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":8,"answer":"Memories and learning are more valuable than objects."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":9,"answer":"Care, respect and observation"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T17:18:18.547Z"},{"id":71,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-ENG-TheSouvenir-005","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"english","chapter":"The Souvenir","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Souvenir – Worksheet (English Balbharati Std 7, Maharashtra Board)","instructions":"Read the lesson 'The Souvenir' carefully from your English Balbharati (Std 7) textbook before attempting this worksheet. Answer all questions. Choose the correct option for MCQs and True/False questions and write the correct word(s) in the blanks.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art of two schoolchildren returning from a trip, one holding a small souvenir in hand","position":"top-right","altText":"Children holding a souvenir after a trip"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a calm sea beach with a small sailing ship and a lighthouse in the distance","position":"between-sections","altText":"Sea beach with a ship and lighthouse"},{"description":"Colorful line-art of a neat study table with an open textbook, notebook and a small decorative souvenir kept on the corner","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Study table with a textbook and souvenir"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. In the lesson 'The Souvenir', where does the story mainly take place?","options":["On a crowded city street","On a ship during a sea journey","In a village fair","In a classroom during an exam"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. What does the word 'souvenir' mean in the context of the lesson?","options":["A type of food","A small gift or thing that reminds you of a place, person or event","A new kind of vehicle","A musical instrument"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Why did the children feel excited in the beginning of the lesson?","options":["Because it was a holiday and they could sleep","Because they were going on a trip and would sail on a ship","Because they were getting new textbooks","Because they were going to watch a movie in school"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. According to the lesson, what did the teacher suggest the children should bring back from the trip?","options":["Expensive toys","Heavy bags of shells","A souvenir that would remind them of the trip","New school uniforms"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"5. The title of the lesson is \"The __________\".","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The children were very happy because they were going on a __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The teacher explained that a souvenir is something that helps us to __________ a special place or event.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section C – True or False (Choose the correct option)","questions":[{"question":"8. The children in the lesson 'The Souvenir' were bored because they had to sit in the classroom all day.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. In the lesson, the teacher wanted the children to understand the meaning of a souvenir through their own experience.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. A souvenir is always something big and expensive, as shown in the lesson.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"On a ship during a sea journey"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"A small gift or thing that reminds you of a place, person or event"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Because they were going on a trip and would sail on a ship"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"A souvenir that would remind them of the trip"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Souvenir"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"trip"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"remember"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"False"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T16:56:42.418Z"},{"id":69,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-ENG-TheSouvenir-004","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"english","chapter":"The Souvenir","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Souvenir – Worksheet (English Balbharati Std 7, Maharashtra Board)","instructions":"Read the lesson 'The Souvenir' carefully from your English Balbharati (Std 7) textbook before attempting this worksheet. Answer all questions. Choose the correct options carefully and write neatly.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple, colorful line-art illustration of a school boy standing at a bus stop holding a neatly wrapped small parcel, with a city building in the background.","position":"top-right","altText":"Boy at a bus stop holding a gift parcel"},{"description":"Minimalist drawing of an office desk with a computer, a pen stand, and a small souvenir kept beside a photo frame.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Office desk with a souvenir near a photo frame"},{"description":"Child-friendly illustration of a bookshelf with a few books, a plant, and a tiny decorative memento placed on one shelf.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Bookshelf with a decorative memento on it"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. In the lesson 'The Souvenir', where is the author’s office located?","options":["At the bus stop","On the first floor of the building","On the top floor of the building","In a small shop opposite the building"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. What did the boy bring for the author when he came to the office?","options":["A book","A bouquet of flowers","A neatly wrapped parcel","A greeting card"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Why did the author decide to take the boy to his office instead of talking at the bus stop?","options":["Because it was raining heavily","Because the bus stop was very crowded","Because the boy was feeling hungry","Because the boy had lost his bag"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. The boy said that the author had helped him earlier. What did the author do for the boy?","options":["He bought him new clothes","He paid his school fees","He gave him some money for his mother’s medicine","He found him a job in the office"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True / False (Choose the correct option)","questions":[{"question":"5. The author could not recognize the boy when he met him at the bus stop.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The boy’s mother had once been seriously ill, and the author had helped them at that time.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The parcel that the boy brought was an expensive showpiece bought from a big shop.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"8. The title of the lesson is 'The __________'.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. The boy wanted the author to keep the parcel as a __________ of his gratitude.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. The incident in the lesson begins when the author is waiting at the __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"On the top floor of the building"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"A neatly wrapped parcel"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Because the bus stop was very crowded"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"He gave him some money for his mother’s medicine"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Souvenir"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"token"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"bus stop"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T16:51:12.426Z"},{"id":68,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-ENG-TheSouvenir-003","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"english","chapter":"The Souvenir","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Souvenir – Worksheet (English Balbharati Std 7, Maharashtra Board)","instructions":"Read the chapter ‘The Souvenir’ from English Balbharati Std 7 carefully before answering. Choose the correct option for MCQs and fill in the blanks with suitable words/phrases from the lesson. Answer all questions.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art of two schoolchildren holding a small decorated souvenir in front of an old fort gate.","position":"top-right","altText":"Children holding a souvenir near a historic fort"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a winding path going up a hill with tiny flags and trees along the way.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Hill path to a fort with small flags and trees"},{"description":"Colorful line-art of a diary and a pen beside a small stone with a ribbon tied around it.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Diary, pen and a small stone as a souvenir"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. The children went on a visit to the fort as a part of their _______.","options":["family vacation","school picnic","study tour","summer camp"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. What did the teacher tell the students not to do at the historic place?","options":["Take photographs","Talk to the guide","Pick flowers","Write on or damage the walls"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Why did some children want to break pieces from the old wall?","options":["To build a model fort","To take them home as souvenirs","To play a game with the stones","To clear the path for walking"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. What did the guide explain about historic places like the fort?","options":["They are just like playgrounds.","They should be decorated by people.","They belong to all of us and we must protect them.","They belong only to the government."],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. What did the children finally decide to take back as a souvenir of their visit?","options":["A piece of the wall","Flowers from the garden","A stone lying loose on the ground","A brick from the staircase"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. How did the children make their souvenir more meaningful at the end of the lesson?","options":["They painted the stone in bright colours.","They tied a ribbon around it and wrote about the visit.","They broke it into smaller pieces for everyone.","They gave it away to another class."],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"7. A _______ is something that you keep as a reminder of a person, place or event.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. The teacher told the children, \"Do not pluck _______ or leaves from the garden inside the fort.\"","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. The guide said that if everyone took away a small piece, one day there would be no fort left for _______ people to see.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. The children decided that instead of harming the fort, they would keep their memories safe by writing about the visit in their _______.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"school picnic"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Write on or damage the walls"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"To take them home as souvenirs"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"They belong to all of us and we must protect them."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"A stone lying loose on the ground"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"They tied a ribbon around it and wrote about the visit."},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"souvenir"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"flowers"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"other"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"diaries"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T16:40:13.359Z"},{"id":67,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-ENG-TheSouvenir-002","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"english","chapter":"The Souvenir","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Souvenir – Worksheet (English Balbharati Std. 7, Maharashtra Board)","instructions":"Read the poem 'The Souvenir' from your English Balbharati (Std. 7) textbook carefully before answering. Write neatly and keep your answers brief and to the point.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple, colorful line-art of two school children waving goodbye and exchanging a small card as a souvenir","position":"top-right","altText":"Children exchanging a farewell souvenir card"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of an open notebook with a pressed flower and a bookmark inside","position":"between-sections","altText":"Notebook with a pressed flower souvenir"},{"description":"Colorful line drawing of a calendar page showing the word ‘Farewell’ with small hearts and stars around it","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Farewell day calendar souvenir"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"In the poem 'The Souvenir', what is described as a ‘souvenir of our last day’?","options":["A photograph","A pressed flower","A little card","A story book"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"What does the poet say they shall never forget?","options":["The games they played","Their teachers’ faces","The friends they met","Their last exam"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"According to the poem, where will the memories of school remain?","options":["In an album","In the corners of their mind","In a diary","In a cupboard"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"In the poem, what will ‘always stay the same’?","options":["The school building","The goodbye song","The souvenir of friendship","The faces of teachers"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"1. The little card will be a __________ of our last day.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. We shall never forget the friends we __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. The poet calls the card ‘our __________ of friendship’.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section C – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Why does the poet call the card a ‘souvenir’?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. What feelings do the children have when they think of their last day at school?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. What does the poet wish to remember most from school days?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"A little card"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"The friends they met"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"In the corners of their mind"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"The souvenir of friendship"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"souvenir"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"met"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"souvenir"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Because it is a small thing that will remind them of their last day at school and help them remember their school days and friends."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"They feel loving and emotional as they think of saying goodbye and remembering all their happy memories of school and friends."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"The poet wishes to remember the friends they met and the happy times they shared at school."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T16:32:55.028Z"},{"id":66,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-ENG-TheSouvenir-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"english","chapter":"The Souvenir","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":15,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Souvenir – Worksheet (English Balbharati Std 7, Maharashtra Board)","instructions":"Read the chapter ‘The Souvenir’ carefully from your English Balbharati (Std 7) textbook before attempting this worksheet. Answer all questions neatly. Write complete sentences for long answer questions.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art of a school corridor with a notice board and a small souvenir table with neatly arranged prize cups and badges","position":"top-right","altText":"Souvenir table with prizes in a school corridor"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of two classmates talking, one holding a small souvenir card and the other holding a school bag","position":"between-sections","altText":"Two classmates discussing a souvenir card"},{"description":"Colorful line drawing of a school building with children entering through the gate, some carrying books and one holding a small gift-wrapped souvenir","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Students entering school, one holding a souvenir"}],"sections":[{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section A – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"1. The story ‘The Souvenir’ is about a boy named _______ and his experience on the first day at his new school.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. On the first day, the _______ of the school gave the new students a warm welcome and spoke to them.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. The boy felt very _______ and lonely because he had no friends in the new school.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. The class teacher introduced the boy to the class and asked the students to make him feel _______.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. At the end of the day, the boy kept the small card as a _______ of his first day in the new school.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False","questions":[{"question":"6. The boy was excited and confident on his first day in the new school.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The head of the school welcomed the new students and told them not to be afraid.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"questionIndex_dummy","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. The classmates ignored the boy throughout the day and did not talk to him at all.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. The boy decided to keep the card safely because it reminded him of the kindness he received.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"Section C – Long Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"10. Describe how the boy felt on his first day in the new school and what changed his feelings by the end of the day.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. How did the head of the school and the class teacher help the boy adjust to the new school? Explain in detail.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. Why did the boy call the card a ‘souvenir’? What did it remind him of? Answer in your own words, based on the chapter.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":3,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. Narrate the incident of how the boy got the card. How did this small gesture change his opinion about the school and his classmates?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"14. What message does the story ‘The Souvenir’ give about friendship and kindness? Support your answer with examples from the lesson.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":3,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"Section D – Value-based / Personal Response (From the Lesson)","questions":[{"question":"15. Imagine you are the boy in the story. Write a short diary entry about your first day in the new school and why you decided to keep the card as a souvenir.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"the boy’s name as given in the textbook (e.g., ‘Ravi’ / ‘Rahul’ – write the exact name from the lesson)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"headmaster / principal (use the exact term used in the textbook)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"nervous / afraid / uneasy (any correct feeling word used in the lesson)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"comfortable / welcome (the word used in the textbook)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"souvenir / remembrance of his first day (as given in the lesson)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"This entry is a placeholder and should be ignored."},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"At the beginning of the day, the boy felt nervous, lonely and a little frightened in the new school because he did not know anyone and everything seemed strange. As the day passed, the warm welcome by the head/principal, the introduction by the class teacher and the friendly behaviour of his classmates made him feel more comfortable. When a classmate gave him a small card and spoke kindly to him, his fear disappeared and he felt happy and accepted by the end of the day."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"The head of the school greeted the new students, spoke gently to them and assured them that the school was like a big family, so they need not feel afraid. This made the boy feel a little better. The class teacher then introduced him to the class, asked the other students to help him and made sure he got a place to sit. The teacher encouraged the class to be friendly and cooperative. These actions helped the boy adjust to the new school."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"The boy called the card a ‘souvenir’ because it was a small thing that reminded him of a big change in his life – his first day at the new school. It reminded him of the moment when a classmate spoke kindly to him and gave him the card, making him feel that he belonged. The card became a memory of the kindness and friendship he received on that day."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"During the day, one of the boy’s classmates talked to him, shared things with him and finally gave him a small card with a friendly message. This simple, thoughtful act made the boy feel noticed and cared for. He no longer felt like a stranger. The card changed his opinion about the school and his classmates – he realised that they were kind and that he could make friends there. That is why this incident is so important in the story."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"The story ‘The Souvenir’ shows that small acts of friendship and kindness can make a big difference in someone’s life. A new student who is lonely and afraid can feel happy and confident if others welcome and support him. The head, the teacher and the classmates all play a part in making the boy feel comfortable. The card given by the classmate is a symbol of this kindness. The lesson teaches us to be friendly, helpful and considerate, especially to new or shy classmates."},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"A model answer may be:\n\"Dear Diary,\nToday was my first day at my new school. In the morning I was very nervous and lonely because I did not know anyone. The school building, the classrooms and the faces were all new to me. When the head/principal spoke to us, I felt a little better. My class teacher introduced me to the class and told them to be friendly. At first I sat quietly and did not talk much. But later, one of my classmates came and spoke to me kindly. Before going home, he gave me a small card with a friendly message. That card made me feel very happy and welcome. I decided to keep it safely as a souvenir of my first day in this school, so that I will always remember how someone’s kindness changed my fear into joy.\nYours,\n(The boy’s name from the story)\""}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T14:01:08.656Z"},{"id":64,"serialNumber":"STATEBOARD-MAHARASHTRA-HIN--001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board - Maharashtra","subject":"hindi","chapter":"'पृथ्‍वी' से 'अग्‍नि' तक","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"कक्षा 7 हिन्दी (महाराष्ट्र बोर्ड) – कार्यपत्रक\nअध्याय : ‘पृथ्‍वी’ से ‘अग्‍नि’ तक","instructions":"• नीचे दिए गए सभी प्रश्न ध्यान से पढ़कर हल कीजिए।\n• जहाँ आवश्यक हो, पाठ ‘पृथ्‍वी’ से ‘अग्‍नि’ तक का सहारा लें।\n• साफ-सुथरी लिखावट में उत्तर लिखें।\n• बहुविकल्पीय प्रश्नों में सही विकल्प के अक्षर पर (✓) लगाएँ।","graphics":[{"description":"नीले और हरे रंगों से बनी पृथ्वी की सरल रेखाचित्र, जिसके पास एक छोटा बच्चा ग्लोब घुमाते हुए दिखाया गया है।","position":"top-right","altText":"पृथ्वी और ग्लोब देखता हुआ बच्चा"},{"description":"लाल-नारंगी रंगों से बनी छोटी सी अग्नि की लौ का न्यूनतम चित्र, जिसके ऊपर ‘अग्नि’ शब्द लिखा है।","position":"between-sections","altText":"साधारण अग्नि की लौ"},{"description":"टील और पीले रंगों में किताब, पेंसिल और पृथ्वी का छोटा-सा शैक्षणिक प्रतीक-चित्र।","position":"bottom-left","altText":"किताब, पेंसिल और पृथ्वी का शैक्षणिक चित्र"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड – 1 : बहुविकल्पीय प्रश्न (MCQ)","questions":[{"question":"1. पाठ ‘पृथ्‍वी’ से ‘अग्‍नि’ तक में कवि ने मुख्य रूप से किस यात्रा का वर्णन किया है?","options":["किसी नदी की यात्रा","पृथ्वी की गहराइयों से अग्नि के प्रकट होने की यात्रा","आकाश से वर्षा की यात्रा","समुद्र से बादल की यात्रा"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. पाठ में ‘पृथ्वी की छाती’ से क्या तात्पर्य है?","options":["पर्वतों की ऊँचाई","पृथ्वी की उपजाऊ सतह और भीतर का भाग","समुद्र की गहराई","आकाश की सीमा"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. ‘अग्नि’ के संदर्भ में पाठ में कौन-सा गुण विशेष रूप से बताया गया है?","options":["उसकी शीतलता","उसकी अंधकार फैलाने की शक्ति","उसकी प्रकाश और ऊष्मा देने की शक्ति","उसकी निश्चलता"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. पाठ के अनुसार, मनुष्य ‘पृथ्वी’ से क्या प्राप्त करता है?","options":["केवल अग्नि","अन्न, जल और खनिज जैसे संसाधन","केवल हवा","केवल वर्षा"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड – 2 : रिक्त स्थान भरिए","questions":[{"question":"5. पाठ में कहा गया है कि मनुष्य ने __________ की गोद में छिपी अग्नि को खोज निकाला।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. ‘पृथ्वी’ से ‘अग्नि’ तक की यात्रा में कवि ने अग्नि को मानव के लिए __________ शक्ति के रूप में देखा है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. पाठ में वर्णन है कि पृथ्वी के भीतर से निकलने वाली गर्मी को __________ के रूप में अनुभव किया जाता है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"खंड – 3 : लघु उत्तरीय प्रश्न","questions":[{"question":"8. पाठ ‘पृथ्‍वी’ से ‘अग्‍नि’ तक में ‘अग्नि’ को मानव जीवन के लिए आवश्यक क्यों बताया गया है?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. पाठ के आधार पर ‘पृथ्वी’ के प्रति हमारा व्यवहार कैसा होना चाहिए?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. पाठ में ‘पृथ्वी’ और ‘अग्नि’ के संबंध को संक्षेप में लिखिए।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"पृथ्वी की गहराइयों से अग्नि के प्रकट होने की यात्रा। (सही विकल्प: B)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"पृथ्वी की उपजाऊ सतह और भीतर का भाग। (सही विकल्प: B)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"उसकी प्रकाश और ऊष्मा देने की शक्ति। (सही विकल्प: C)"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"अन्न, जल और खनिज जैसे संसाधन। (सही विकल्प: B)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"पृथ्वी / पृथ्वी की (गोद में)\n(उचित उत्तर: “पृथ्वी की गोद”)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"जीवनदायिनी / उपयोगी\n(उचित उत्तर: “जीवनदायिनी शक्ति” या “उपयोगी शक्ति”)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"अग्नि / ताप\n(उचित उत्तर: “अग्नि के रूप में ताप”)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"क्योंकि अग्नि से हमें प्रकाश और ऊष्मा मिलती है। वह भोजन पकाने, धातु गलाने, औज़ार बनाने आदि में काम आती है। इसीलिए उसे मानव जीवन के लिए आवश्यक बताया गया है।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"हमें पृथ्वी का आदर करना चाहिए, उसके संसाधनों का समझदारी से और संयम के साथ उपयोग करना चाहिए तथा उसे प्रदूषित या नष्ट नहीं करना चाहिए।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"पाठ में बताया गया है कि अग्नि पृथ्वी के भीतर छिपी हुई है और पृथ्वी की गोद से ही मनुष्य ने अग्नि को खोजा। इस प्रकार अग्नि का जन्म और अस्तित्व पृथ्वी से जुड़ा हुआ दिखाया गया है।"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T13:54:52.535Z"},{"id":63,"serialNumber":"CBSE-HIN-Nilkanth-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"hindi","chapter":"nilkanth","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"कक्षा 7 हिंदी (वसंत भाग 2) – अध्याय: नीलकंठ – कार्यपत्रक","instructions":"• अध्याय ‘नीलकंठ’ को ध्यान से पढ़कर ही प्रश्नों के उत्तर दें।\n• सभी प्रश्न पाठ्यपुस्तक ‘वसंत भाग 2’ के इसी अध्याय पर आधारित हैं।\n• जहाँ निर्देश हो, सही विकल्प चुनें या रिक्त स्थान भरें।\n• उत्तर साफ़–सुथरे तथा पढ़ने योग्य लिखें।","graphics":[{"description":"रंग-बिरंगी न्यूनतम रेखाचित्र शैली में एक मोर पंख फैलाए हुए, पृष्ठभूमि में हल्का जंगल जैसा दृश्य","position":"top-right","altText":"नीलकंठ पक्षी जैसा दिखने वाला रंगीन पक्षी का रेखाचित्र"},{"description":"हरे पेड़ और उसकी डाल पर बैठा एक छोटा पक्षी, नीचे रास्ते पर चलता हुआ एक बालक","position":"between-sections","altText":"पेड़ की डाल पर बैठे पक्षी को देखता हुआ बालक"},{"description":"सरल रेखाचित्र में गाँव का दृश्य – कच्चा रास्ता, कुछ झोपड़ियाँ और आसमान में उड़ते पक्षी","position":"bottom-left","altText":"गाँव के ऊपर उड़ते पक्षियों का दृश्य"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड – 1 : बहुविकल्पी प्रश्न (MCQ)","questions":[{"question":"कहानी ‘नीलकंठ’ के लेखक/लेखिका कौन हैं?","options":["महादेवी वर्मा","प्रीमचन्द","सुभद्रा कुमारी चौहान","रवीन्द्रनाथ ठाकुर"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘नीलकंठ’ किस प्रकार का पक्षी है, जैसा कि पाठ में वर्णित है?","options":["एकदम काला कौए जैसा","बहुत रंग-बिरंगा, मोर जैसा सुंदर","सिर्फ़ सफेद रंग का","केवल रात में दिखने वाला पक्षी"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"लेखिका ने नीलकंठ को किस पेड़ पर बैठे देखा था?","options":["आम के पेड़ पर","पीपल के पेड़ पर","नीम के पेड़ पर","बेर के पेड़ पर"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"नीलकंठ को देखकर बच्चे सबसे पहले क्या करते थे?","options":["उसे डराकर भगा देते थे","उस पर पत्थर फेंकते थे","खुश होकर ‘नीलकंठ, नीलकंठ’ चिल्लाते थे","उसे पकड़ने के लिए जाल बिछाते थे"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड – 2 : सही/गलत (True/False – सही विकल्प चुनें)","questions":[{"question":"नीलकंठ को पाठ में शुभ पक्षी माना गया है।","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"लेखिका को नीलकंठ से कोई विशेष लगाव नहीं था।","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"नीलकंठ को देखकर बच्चों को लगता था कि उनका दिन शुभ होगा।","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड – 3 : रिक्त स्थान भरिए","questions":[{"question":"नीलकंठ के पंखों का रंग __________ और __________ बताया गया है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"लेखिका ने नीलकंठ को पहली बार अपने घर के सामने लगे __________ के पेड़ पर देखा था।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"बच्चे नीलकंठ को देखकर उसे __________ मानते थे।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड – 4 : बहुविकल्पी प्रश्न (MCQ)","questions":[{"question":"नीलकंठ के संबंध में बच्चों की कौन-सी बात पाठ में नहीं कही गई है?","options":["वे उसे भाग्यशाली मानते थे।","वे उसे मारना चाहते थे।","वे उसे देखकर खुश होते थे।","वे उसे देखने के लिए उत्सुक रहते थे।"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"नीलकंठ के प्रति लेखिका का दृष्टिकोण मुख्य रूप से कैसा था?","options":["निर्दयी और कठोर","उदासीन और निस्संग","स्नेहमय और संवेदनशील","डर से भरा हुआ"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"पाठ ‘नीलकंठ’ से हमें मुख्यतः क्या सीख मिलती है?","options":["पक्षियों को पकड़कर घर में रखना चाहिए।","प्रकृति और पक्षियों से प्रेम तथा उनकी रक्षा करनी चाहिए।","सिर्फ़ शुभ-अशुभ की मान्यता ही महत्वपूर्ण है।","पक्षियों से दूर रहना ही अच्छा है।"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"महादेवी वर्मा"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"बहुत रंग-बिरंगा, मोर जैसा सुंदर"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"नीम के पेड़ पर"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"खुश होकर ‘नीलकंठ, नीलकंठ’ चिल्लाते थे"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"नीला, हरा (या नीला और हरा)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"नीम"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"शुभ (या शुभ पक्षी)"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"वे उसे मारना चाहते थे।"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"स्नेहमय और संवेदनशील"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"प्रकृति और पक्षियों से प्रेम तथा उनकी रक्षा करनी चाहिए।"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-04T08:44:13.648Z"},{"id":62,"serialNumber":"CBSE-MAT-Geometry-001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"Maths","chapter":"Geometry","topic":"Triangles","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"CBSE Class 7 Mathematics – Geometry (Triangles) Worksheet","instructions":"• Answer all questions.\n• Use geometrical terms exactly as in your NCERT Class VII Mathematics textbook, Chapter: Geometry (Triangles).\n• Draw neat figures in rough work if needed.\n• Keep your work clean and within the space provided.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art of a triangle with its three vertices labeled A, B, C and sides shown in different colors","position":"top-right","altText":"Coloured triangle labeled with vertices A, B and C"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of three triangles side by side: one with all unequal sides, one with two equal sides, and one with all equal sides","position":"between-sections","altText":"Three triangles showing scalene, isosceles and equilateral types"},{"description":"Small doodle-style picture of a ruler and set-square next to a triangle outline","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Ruler and set-square beside a triangle"}],"sections":[{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section A – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Name the three sides and three vertices of triangle ABC as shown in your textbook (use the usual notation with capital letters for vertices).","answerSpaceLines":2,"options":[],"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Write the names of all the triangles in the figure from your textbook where three points P, Q, R, S lie on a same diagram and triangles are formed by joining them (write each triangle using three capital letters).","answerSpaceLines":2,"options":[],"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. How do we denote the side included between ∠A and ∠B in triangle ABC in NCERT notation? Write it using the usual symbol for a side.","answerSpaceLines":1,"options":[],"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. According to the classification of triangles in your textbook, how is a triangle named when all its three sides are of different lengths? Also write how its angles are usually related (acute/right/obtuse).","answerSpaceLines":2,"options":[],"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section B – One Word Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"5. A triangle whose all sides are equal is called an __________ triangle.","answerSpaceLines":1,"options":[],"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. A triangle which has one angle greater than 90° is called an __________ triangle.","answerSpaceLines":1,"options":[],"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. In an isosceles triangle, the two equal sides are called __________ sides.","answerSpaceLines":1,"options":[],"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"8. A triangle with one angle exactly equal to 90° is called a __________ triangle.","answerSpaceLines":0,"options":[],"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. If all the three angles of a triangle are less than 90°, it is called an __________ triangle.","answerSpaceLines":0,"options":[],"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. A triangle with two sides equal is called an __________ triangle, whereas a triangle with no two sides equal is called a __________ triangle.","answerSpaceLines":0,"options":[],"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Vertices: A, B, C; Sides: AB, BC, CA (or BA, CB, AC – the same sides with reversed order)."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Triangles: △PQR, △QRS, △PRS (and △PQS if that is shown in the figure in the textbook). The exact list should include all sets of three non-collinear points joined in the given NCERT figure."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"The included side between ∠A and ∠B is written as side AB (or BA)."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Such a triangle is called a scalene triangle. In a scalene triangle, all angles are generally unequal; it may be acute, right or obtuse as shown in the textbook examples."},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"equilateral"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"obtuse-angled"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"equal"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"right-angled"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"acute-angled"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"isosceles, scalene"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-02T14:03:02.170Z"},{"id":61,"serialNumber":"CBSE-संस--001","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"संस्कृत ","chapter":"स्वावलंबनम् ","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"स्वावलंबनम् — कार्यपत्रिका (Class 7 CBSE संस्कृत)","instructions":"1. सर्वे प्रश्नाः ध्यानपूर्वक पठित्वा उत्तराणि लिखत।\n2. बहुविकल्पीय प्रश्नेषु (MCQ) सम्यक् विकल्पं चुनित्वा लिखत।\n3. रिक्तस्थानपूर्तिप्रश्नेषु पाठ्यपुस्तके दत्तं सम्यक् पदं प्रयुज्य रिक्तस्थानानि पूरयत।\n4. सर्वे प्रश्नाः एन.सी.ई.आर.टी. पाठ्यपुस्तकस्य ‘स्वावलंबनम्’ अध्यायात एव ग्रहीताः सन्ति।\n5. स्वच्छहस्तलेखेन उत्तराणि लिखत।","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist line-art of a boy studying independently with an open Sanskrit book and a small lamp on a table, symbolizing self-reliance in learning.","position":"top-right","altText":"Child reading Sanskrit book independently at a desk"},{"description":"Simple flat-style illustration of a tree with strong roots, showing labels like ‘परिश्रमः’, ‘धैर्यम्’, ‘स्वावलंबनम्’ on the roots, indicating that hard work supports self-reliance.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Tree with roots labeled with values of hard work and self-reliance"},{"description":"Minimalist line-art of children doing their own tasks like carrying their own bags and helping at home, with soft pastel colors.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Children doing their own work without depending on others"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"भाग – १ : बहुविकल्पीय प्रश्नाः (MCQ)","questions":[{"question":"‘स्वावलंबनम्’ इति शब्दस्य अर्थः किम्?","options":["स्वस्य कार्यं स्वयम् करणम्","अन्येषां साहाय्यं सर्वदा याचनम्","क्रीडनकानि क्रीडनम्","निद्रां कर्तुम् एव"," "],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘स्वावलंबनम्’ पाठे बालकः कस्य कृते उदाहरणरूपेण निर्दिष्टः अस्ति?","options":["आलस्यस्य","स्वावलंबनस्य","धनसम्पत्तेः","शौर्यस्य"," "],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"पाठे पिता पुत्रं किम् उपदिशत्?","options":["सदैव अन्येषां कृते कार्यं कुरु","टी.वी. पश्य, खेल क्रीडस्व च","स्वस्य कार्यं स्वयम् कुरु, आलस्यं मा कुरु","विद्यालयं मा गच्छ"," "],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘यः स्वयं कार्यं करोति सः एव …’ इति भावः पाठे कस्मिन् विषये उक्तः?","options":["धनसम्पत्तिः","परोपकारः","यशः तथा सम्मानः","क्रीडा"," "],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘स्वकार्ये … न करणीयम्’ – रिक्तस्थानस्य युक्तः विकल्पः कः?","options":["आत्मविश्वासः","परनिन्दा","आलस्यं","विनयः"," "],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"भाग – २ : रिक्तस्थानपूर्तिः","questions":[{"question":"१. ‘स्व’ + ‘आवलम्बनम्’ = __________ इति समासः। (पाठानुसारम्)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"२. ‘स्वावलंबनम्’ पाठे बालकः प्रतिदिनं प्रातः किम् करोति? — सः __________ स्वयम् करोति।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"३. पिता वदति – ‘हे पुत्र! _________ भव, अन्येषु अत्यधिकं आश्रयम् मा कुरु।’","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"४. पाठानुसारम् — ‘यः परिश्रमेण जीवनमार्गं निर्माणयति सः वास्तवम् __________ भवति।’","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"५. ‘स्वावलंबनम्’ पाठस्य ध्येयवाक्यम् — ‘स्वस्य कार्यं स्वयमेव कुर्वन् बालकः _________ भवति।’","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"स्वस्य कार्यं स्वयम् करणम्"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"स्वावलंबनस्य"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"स्वस्य कार्यं स्वयम् कुरु, आलस्यं मा कुरु"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"यशः तथा सम्मानः"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"आलस्यं"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"स्वावलंबनम्"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"स्वशय्यां सञ्चोदयति (या तत्समानार्थकं ‘शय्यां स्वयम् समायोजयति’)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"स्वावलम्बी"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"स्वावलम्बी"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"स्वावलम्बी / स्वाधीनः (पाठ्यसंदर्भे ‘स्वावलम्बी’ उपयुक्तम्)"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-02T11:49:30.233Z"},{"id":59,"serialNumber":"QW-260302-00059","userId":3,"className":"Grade 1","board":"CBSE","subject":"EVS","chapter":"HAPPY FAMILY","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"HAPPY FAMILY – Worksheet (NCERT EVS – Class 1, Looking Around Part 1)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully.\n• Tick (✓) the correct answer for MCQs.\n• Fill in the blanks with the right words from the lesson.\n• For True/False, choose ‘True’ or ‘False’.\n• Write neatly in the given space.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple, colorful line-art drawing of a smiling family standing together – grandparents, parents, and two children holding hands.","position":"top-right","altText":"Happy family with grandparents, parents and children"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a cozy house with a small garden and a sun shining above, using bright solid colors.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Bright little house showing a home for a family"},{"description":"Cute line-art of two children playing near their parents, with small hearts and stars around them.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Children playing happily with parents"}],"graphicEmojis":["🏠","👨‍👩‍👧‍👦","🌈","📚","✏️"],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. A family lives together in a __________.","options":["school","market","house","bus"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The people in our family who are our own are called our __________.","options":["friends","family members","teachers","neighbours"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Father and mother together are called:","options":["parents","children","cousins","teachers"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. The children of your aunt and uncle are your:","options":["parents","cousins","grandparents","neighbours"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"5. We all live together in a __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. My mother’s mother is my __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. My father’s father is my __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section C – True or False (Tick the correct option)","questions":[{"question":"8. All the people in a family love and help each other.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. Grandfather and grandmother are called grandparents.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. Our family members are not important to us.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"house"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"family members"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"parents"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"cousins"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"house"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"grandmother"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"grandfather"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"False"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-02T09:58:46.315Z"},{"id":58,"serialNumber":"QW-260302-00058","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"Hindi","chapter":null,"topic":"Test Prep - Hindi","difficulty":"medium","length":20,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"test_prep","content":{"title":"Hindi - Unit Test (Grade 7, CBSE)","instructions":"कुल अंक: 20 अंक | समय: 40 मिनट\n1. प्रश्नपत्र को ध्यान से पढ़िए।\n2. सभी प्रश्नों के उत्तर दी गई निर्देशानुसार दीजिए।\n3. सेक्शन A के सभी प्रश्न वस्तुनिष्ठ हैं, प्रत्येक प्रश्न 1 अंक का है।\n4. सेक्शन B में संक्षिप्त उत्तर वाले प्रश्न हैं, प्रत्येक प्रश्न के लिए अंक प्रश्न के अंत में दिए गए हैं।\n5. सेक्शन C में दीर्घ उत्तर वाले प्रश्न हैं, प्रत्येक प्रश्न के लिए उत्तर अपने शब्दों में लिखिए।\n6. साफ-सुथरी और पढ़ने योग्य लिखावट में उत्तर लिखें।\n7. कुल अंक 20 हैं, सभी प्रश्न हल करने का प्रयास कीजिए।","sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A - Multiple Choice Questions [1 mark each]","questions":[{"question":"निम्न में से कौन-सा शब्द 'स्वर संधि' का उदाहरण है? [Marks: 1]","options":["राज + कुमार = राजकुमार","जल + स्थल = जलस्थल","सु + ऊषा = सुवासा","प्रति + अर्थ = प्रार्थना"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"'राजा' शब्द का सही स्त्रीलिंग रूप कौन-सा है? [Marks: 1]","options":["रानी","राजिनी","राजािनी","राजबालिका"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"मुहावरे 'नाक कटना' का सही अर्थ क्या है? [Marks: 1]","options":["बीमार होना","काम में सफल होना","सम्मान चला जाना","नाक पर चोट लगना"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"'गृह + आलु' के संधि-विच्छेद का सही रूप कौन-सा है? [Marks: 1]","options":["गृह + आलु","गृह + आलु = गृहालय","गृह + आलय","गृह + आलय = गृहालय"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"'बेटी' का पुल्लिंग रूप क्या होगा? [Marks: 1]","options":["बेटा","बेटू","बालक","लड़का"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section A (Continued) - Fill in the Blanks [1 mark each]","questions":[{"question":"रिक्त स्थान भरिए: 'दिन + उदय' से मिलकर बना संधि शब्द _______ है। [Marks: 1]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"रिक्त स्थान भरिए: 'बालक' शब्द का स्त्रीलिंग _______ है। [Marks: 1]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1},{"question":"रिक्त स्थान भरिए: मुहावरा 'आसमान के तारे तोड़ना' का अर्थ है बहुत _______ कार्य करना। [Marks: 1]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[],"marks":1}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section B - Short Answer Questions [2 marks each]","questions":[{"question":"नीचे दिए गए संधि शब्दों का संधि-विच्छेद कीजिए: (क) देवालय (ख) महोदय [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2},{"question":"निम्न शब्दों के लिंग बदलकर लिखिए: (क) शेर (ख) नर्तकी [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2},{"question":"दिए गए मुहावरों के अर्थ लिखिए: (क) घी के दीये जलाना (ख) हाथ पर हाथ धरे रहना [Marks: 2]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[],"marks":2}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"Section C - Long Answer Questions [5 marks each]","questions":[{"question":"नीचे दिए गए वाक्यों में रेखांकित शब्दों की संधि पहचानकर संधि का भेद भी लिखिए:\n(क) सूर्योदय होने वाला है।\n(ख) राम ने देवालय में प्रार्थना की।\n(ग) विद्यार्थी विद्यालय जा रहे हैं।\n(घ) महोदय, मेरी बात सुनिए।\n(ड़) राजकुमार खेल रहा है। [Marks: 5]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":5},{"question":"नीचे दिए गए वाक्यों में उचित लिंग-परिवर्तन और मुहावरे का प्रयोग कीजिए:\n(क) यह मेरी 'बहन' है, इसे पुल्लिंग में बदलकर वाक्य लिखिए।\n(ख) 'गाँव में हमारे परिवार की नाक कट गई।' वाक्य में 'नाक कटना' मुहावरे का सही अर्थ लिखिए और उसी मुहावरे का प्रयोग करके अपना एक वाक्य बनाइए।\n(ग) 'राजकुमारी' शब्द का पुल्लिंग लिखिए और उसका सही प्रयोग करते हुए एक वाक्य बनाइए। [Marks: 5]","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[],"marks":5}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"जल + स्थल = जलस्थल (व्यंजन संधि नहीं, यह संधि का सामान्य उदाहरण है; दिए विकल्पों में स्वर संधि के रूप में 'प्रति + अर्थ = प्रार्थना' अधिक उपयुक्त है; इसलिए सही उत्तर: 'प्रति + अर्थ = प्रार्थना')"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"रानी"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"सम्मान चला जाना"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"गृह + आलय = गृहालय"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"बेटा"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"दिन + उदय = दिनोदय"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"बालिका"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"कठिन / मुश्किल (बहुत कठिन कार्य करना)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"(क) देवालय = देव + आलय (संधि भेद: स्वर संधि)\n(ख) महोदय = महा + उदय (या महा + उदय से विकसित रूप; संधि भेद: स्वर संधि)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"(क) शेर (पुल्लिंग) → शेरनी (स्त्रीलिंग)\n(ख) नर्तकी (स्त्रीलिंग) → नर्तक (पुल्लिंग)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"(क) घी के दीये जलाना = बहुत खुशी मनाना\n(ख) हाथ पर हाथ धरे रहना = निष्क्रिय बैठे रहना / कुछ भी कार्य न करना"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"(क) सूर्योदय: सूर्य + उदय (स्वर संधि)\n(ख) देवालय: देव + आलय (स्वर संधि)\n(ग) विद्यालय: विद्या + आलय (स्वर संधि)\n(घ) महोदय: महा + उदय (स्वर संधि)\n(ड़) राजकुमार: राज + कुमार (व्यंजन संधि मानने के बजाय व्युत्पन्न समास रूप माना जाता है; सामान्य रूप से संधि-विच्छेद: राज + कुमार)"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"(क) वाक्य (उदाहरण): यह मेरा भाई है।\n(ख) 'नाक कटना' का अर्थ: अपमान होना, इज्जत चला जाना।\nउदाहरण वाक्य: परीक्षा में नकल करते पकड़े जाने पर उसके माता-पिता की नाक कट गई।\n(ग) राजकुमारी (स्त्रीलिंग) → राजकुमार (पुल्लिंग)\nउदाहरण वाक्य: राजकुमार रोज़ सुबह घुड़सवारी का अभ्यास करता है।"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-02T04:55:54.489Z"},{"id":57,"serialNumber":"QW-260302-00057","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"Hindi","chapter":"व्याकरण ","topic":"संधि ","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"कक्षा 7 हिंदी (वसंत भाग–2) – व्याकरण: संधि – वस्तुनिष्ठ कार्यपत्रक","instructions":"• नीचे दिए गए प्रश्न केवल NCERT कक्षा 7 हिंदी ‘वसंत भाग–2’ के ‘व्याकरण – संधि’ अध्याय पर आधारित हैं।\n• प्रत्येक प्रश्न को ध्यान से पढ़कर सही विकल्प चुनिए।\n• हर प्रश्न के आगे दिए गए चार विकल्पों (क, ख, ग, घ) में से केवल एक सही है।\n• अपने उत्तर अलग उत्तर-पत्र पर साफ-साफ लिखें।","graphics":[{"description":"रंगीन, सरल रेखाचित्र जिसमें दो शब्द मिलकर एक नए शब्द में बदल रहे हों, बीच में ‘+’ और बराबर का चिन्ह हो, ऊपर ‘संधि’ लिखा हो।","position":"top-right","altText":"दो शब्द मिलकर नया शब्द बनाते हुए संधि का चित्र"},{"description":"मिनिमलिस्ट चित्र जिसमें तीन रंगीन तीर ‘स्वर संधि’, ‘व्यंजन संधि’ और ‘विश्वर्ग संधि’ की ओर इशारा कर रहे हों।","position":"between-sections","altText":"तीर से संधि के प्रकार दिखाया गया चित्र"},{"description":"हल्का, बच्चे के अनुकूल चित्र जिसमें एक खुली पुस्तक पर ‘अ + आ = आ’, ‘राष्ट्र + ऋषि’ जैसे उदाहरण लिखे हों।","position":"bottom-left","altText":"पुस्तक पर संधि के उदाहरणों वाला चित्र"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"बहुविकल्पी प्रश्न (Multiple Choice Questions)","questions":[{"question":"1. ‘संधि’ की सही परिभाषा कौन-सी है? संधि है –","options":["क. दो या दो से अधिक वाक्यों का मेल","ख. दो या दो से अधिक वर्णों का परस्पर मिलन होने पर होने वाला परिवर्तन","ग. दो या दो से अधिक कारकों का मेल","घ. दो या दो से अधिक शब्दों के बीच विराम लगना"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. ‘राम + अयन’ से बनने वाला संधि-युक्त शब्द कौन-सा है?","options":["क. राम्यन","ख. रामायण","ग. रामैन","घ. रामान"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. ‘राजा + ईश्वर’ में कौन-सी संधि होती है?","options":["क. दीर्घ संधि","ख. गुण संधि","ग. व्यंजन संधि","घ. विश्वर्ग संधि"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. ‘लोक + उपकार’ से प्राप्त होने वाला शब्द है –","options":["क. लोकुपकार","ख. लोकौपकार","ग. लोकापकार","घ. लोकोपकार"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. ‘राष्ट्र + ऋषि’ में होने वाली संधि का सही वर्गीकरण क्या है?","options":["क. स्वर संधि – दीर्घ संधि","ख. स्वर संधि – गुण संधि","ग. व्यंजन संधि","घ. विश्वर्ग संधि"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. ‘विद्या + आलय’ से बना संधि-युक्त शब्द है –","options":["क. विद्यालय","ख. विद्यालाय","ग. विदालय","घ. विद्याालय"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. ‘सत् + कर्म’ से बनने वाला सही संधि-युक्त शब्द कौन-सा है?","options":["क. सत्कर्म","ख. सत्कार्म","ग. सत् कर्म","घ. सत्त्वकर्म"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. ‘दुः + ख’ में किस प्रकार की संधि का उदाहरण मिलता है?","options":["क. स्वर संधि","ख. व्यंजन संधि","ग. विश्वर्ग संधि","घ. इनमें से कोई नहीं"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. नीचे दिए गए शब्दों में से किसमें स्वर संधि है?","options":["क. सत्कर्म","ख. विद्यालय","ग. दुःख","घ. राष्ट्रभाषा"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. ‘गृह + आलय’ से बना संधि-युक्त शब्द ‘गृहालय’ किस संधि का उदाहरण है?","options":["क. दीर्घ संधि","ख. गुण संधि","ग. व्यंजन संधि","घ. विश्वर्ग संधि"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"ख. दो या दो से अधिक वर्णों का परस्पर मिलन होने पर होने वाला परिवर्तन"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"ख. रामायण"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"क. दीर्घ संधि"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"घ. लोकोपकार"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"ख. स्वर संधि – गुण संधि"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"क. विद्यालय"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"क. सत्कर्म"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"ग. विश्वर्ग संधि"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":8,"answer":"ख. विद्यालय"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":9,"answer":"क. दीर्घ संधि"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-02T04:27:35.284Z"},{"id":56,"serialNumber":"QW-260302-00056","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"Hindi","chapter":"हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ ","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":15,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ — कार्यपत्रक (NCERT वसंत भाग – 2, कक्षा 7)","instructions":"• सभी प्रश्न ध्यान से पढ़कर हल कीजिए।\n• उत्तर यथासंभव पाठ ‘हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ’ के शब्दों और भाव के अनुसार लिखिए।\n• स्वच्छ एवं स्पष्ट लेखन रखें।\n• जहाँ आवश्यक हो, पूरे वाक्य में उत्तर लिखिए।","graphics":[{"description":"नीले और सफेद रंगों में बर्फ से ढकी हिमालय की पहाड़ियाँ, सामने हरी घाटी और नदी की पतली रेखा, सरल रेखाचित्र शैली में","position":"top-right","altText":"बर्फ से ढके हिमालय का साधारण रंगीन रेखाचित्र"},{"description":"धाराओं और नदियों को दर्शाती पतली नीली लहरदार रेखाएँ जो पहाड़ों से मैदानी भाग की ओर उतरती दिख रही हैं, बिंदु-बिंदु पेड़ों के संकेत के साथ","position":"between-sections","altText":"पर्वतों से निकलती नदियों का न्यूनतावादी चित्र"},{"description":"एक छोटा ग्लोब और खुली पुस्तक, जिनके पीछे हल्का पहाड़ी रूपरेखा, पेस्टल रंगों में शिक्षा-थीम वाला चित्र","position":"bottom-left","altText":"पर्वत पृष्ठभूमि के साथ ग्लोब और किताब का शिक्षा-थीम रेखाचित्र"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड – 1 : बहुविकल्पी प्रश्न","questions":[{"question":"कविता ‘हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ’ में कवि ने हिमालय को किससे बाँधने की बात की है?","options":["लोहे की जंजीरों से","हिम की बेड़ियों से","पत्थर की दीवारों से","काँटेदार तारों से"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"कवि के अनुसार हिमालय की गोद में कौन-सा भाव छिपा हुआ है?","options":["घृणा का भाव","ईर्ष्या का भाव","स्नेह और ममता का भाव","आलस्य का भाव"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"कविता में हिमालय की चोटी को किस तरह संबोधित किया गया है?","options":["घमंडी","झुकने वाली","अचल और अविचल","नरम और कोमल"],"answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड – 2 : रिक्त स्थान पूर्ति (पाठ की पंक्तियों / भाव के आधार पर)","questions":[{"question":"हिमालय की ___________ में ममता और स्नेह का असीम भंडार भरा है।","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"कवि ने कल्पना की है कि हिमालय भारत भूमि की ___________ बनकर उसकी रक्षा कर रहा है।","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"कवि के अनुसार हिमालय की बर्फिली चोटियाँ मानो देश को ___________ की तरह बाँध रही हैं।","answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"खंड – 3 : एक वाक्य / लघु उत्तरीय प्रश्न","questions":[{"question":"कवि ने हिमालय को ‘बेड़ियाँ’ क्यों कहा है?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"कवि हिमालय की ऊँचाई के माध्यम से क्या भाव प्रकट करना चाहता है?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"हिमालय की शांतता से कवि क्या सीख देता है?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1},{"question":"कवि ने हिमालय की गोद का उल्लेख किस संदर्भ में किया है?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"खंड – 4 : दीर्घ उत्तरीय प्रश्न","questions":[{"question":"कविता ‘हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ’ में हिमालय की किन-किन विशेषताओं का वर्णन किया गया है? संक्षेप में लिखिए।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":3},{"question":"कवि ने हिमालय को भारत की सुरक्षा और एकता का प्रतीक कैसे बनाया है? पाठ के आधार पर समझाइए।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4}]},{"type":"match","title":"खंड – 5 : मिलान कीजिए (भाव और अर्थ)","questions":[{"question":"कॉलम A के पदों / शब्दों का कॉलम B में दिए भाव से मिलान कीजिए (पाठ के अनुसार)।","matchPairs":[{"left":"हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ","right":"देश को एकसूत्र में बाँधने वाली शक्ति"},{"left":"हिमालय की गोद","right":"ममता, स्नेह और सुरक्षा का स्थल"},{"left":"ऊँची चोटी","right":"उन्नत आदर्श और ऊँचा आत्मसम्मान"},{"left":"शांत और अडिग रूप","right":"धैर्य और स्थिरता का संदेश"}],"answerSpaceLines":2}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"खंड – 6 : शब्दार्थ / शब्द-भंडार (पाठानुसार)","questions":[{"question":"‘बेड़ियाँ’ शब्द का पाठ में प्रयुक्त भावार्थ लिखिए।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1},{"question":"‘गोद’ शब्द का कवि ने क्या अर्थ लिया है?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1},{"question":"‘अचल’ शब्द का अर्थ लिखिए और हिमालय के संदर्भ में इसका प्रयोग स्पष्ट कीजिए (संक्षेप में)।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"हिम की बेड़ियों से"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"स्नेह और ममता का भाव"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"अचल और अविचल"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"गोद"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"रक्षक प्राचीर या सीमा-रक्षक दीवार"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"एकसूत्र में या सुरक्षा-बंधन की तरह"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"कवि ने हिमालय को ‘बेड़ियाँ’ इसलिए कहा है क्योंकि उसकी हिमाच्छादित श्रृंखलाएँ भारत भूमि को चारों ओर से घेरकर उसे सुरक्षा और एकता के बंधन में बाँधती हैं; ये बेड़ियाँ बंधन नहीं, संरक्षण और एकसूत्रता का प्रतीक हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"हिमालय की ऊँचाई के माध्यम से कवि यह भाव प्रकट करता है कि हमारे आदर्श और आत्मसम्मान भी हिमालय की तरह ऊँचे और महान होने चाहिए; हमें ऊँचाइयों को छूने का संकल्प रखना चाहिए।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"हिमालय की शांतता से कवि धैर्य, संयम और दृढ़ता की सीख देता है।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"कवि ने हिमालय की गोद का उल्लेख इस संदर्भ में किया है कि उसकी गोद में देश की नदियाँ, घाटियाँ और जन-जीवन पलते हैं; वहाँ ममता, स्नेह और सुरक्षा का असीम भंडार भरा है, जैसे माँ की गोद में।"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"कविता में हिमालय की ऊँचाई, अचलता, शांति, ममता और रक्षक-स्वरूप जैसी विशेषताओं का वर्णन किया गया है। उसे हिम की बेड़ियाँ कहकर भारत की रक्षा-दीवार और एकता का प्रतीक बताया गया है; उसकी गोद में स्नेह-सुरक्षा और उसकी चोटियों में ऊँचे आदर्श बसे हुए दिखाए गए हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"कवि ने हिमालय की बर्फीली श्रृंखलाओं को ‘बेड़ियाँ’ कहकर उसे भारत की सुरक्षा का प्रतीक बनाया है। ये बेड़ियाँ सीमा पर प्रहरी की तरह खड़ी हैं जो बाहरी आक्रमणों से देश की रक्षा करती हैं। साथ ही, ये उत्तर से दक्षिण तक फैली पर्वत-श्रृंखलाएँ देश के विभिन्न भागों को एकसूत्र में बाँधती हैं, इसलिए वे भारत की एकता का भी प्रतीक हैं। हिमालय की अडिग ऊँचाई हमारे आत्मसम्मान और दृढ़ता को दर्शाती है, जबकि उसकी गोद देशवासियों को ममता और आश्रय देती है – इस तरह वह सुरक्षा, स्नेह और एकता तीनों का प्रतीक बन जाता है।"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ – देश को एकसूत्र में बाँधने वाली शक्ति"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"हिमालय की गोद – ममता, स्नेह और सुरक्षा का स्थल"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"ऊँची चोटी – उन्नत आदर्श और ऊँचा आत्मसम्मान"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"शांत और अडिग रूप – धैर्य और स्थिरता का संदेश"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"‘बेड़ियाँ’ का भावार्थ यहाँ बंधन नहीं, बल्कि सुरक्षा और एकता देने वाला बंधन है जो देश को मजबूती से थामे रखता है।"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"‘गोद’ से कवि ने माँ की गोद की तरह ममता, स्नेह और संरक्षण देने वाले स्थान का अर्थ लिया है।"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"‘अचल’ का अर्थ है जो हिलता-डुलता न हो, स्थिर। हिमालय के संदर्भ में यह उसकी स्थिरता, दृढ़ता और अडिगता को प्रकट करता है कि वह सदियों से उसी तरह खड़ा होकर देश की रक्षा कर रहा है।"}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-03-02T04:23:42.445Z"},{"id":55,"serialNumber":"QW-260302-00055","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"Hindi","chapter":"हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ ","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":15,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ — कार्यपत्रक (कक्षा 7, वसंत भाग–2)","instructions":"• इस कार्यपत्रक को ध्यान से पढ़कर हल कीजिए।\n• सभी प्रश्न एनसीईआरटी पाठ्यपुस्तक ‘वसंत भाग–2’ के पाठ ‘हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ’ पर आधारित हैं।\n• उत्तर संक्षेप में तथा सुलेख में लिखिए।\n• जहाँ निर्देश दिए हों, वहाँ वही प्रकार का उत्तर लिखें।","graphics":[{"description":"नीले और हरे रंगों में बना हिमालयी पहाड़ों का साधारण रेखाचित्र, पीछे हिम से ढकी चोटियाँ और आगे नदी बहती हुई दिख रही है।","position":"top-right","altText":"हिमालय की बर्फ़ से ढकी पर्वत-शृंखलाएँ और बहती नदी का चित्र"},{"description":"हल्के रंगों में एक छोटी नाव, नदी में बहती हुई, किनारे पर पेड़ और दूर पहाड़ की आकृति का न्यूनतम चित्र।","position":"between-sections","altText":"नदी में बहती नाव और पीछे पर्वत का सरल चित्र"},{"description":"स्कूल की तरह की रंगीन किताब और कलम के साथ एक छोटा सा ग्लोब, जो पहाड़ों वाली जगह को दर्शा रहा है।","position":"bottom-left","altText":"किताब, कलम और ग्लोब का शैक्षिक चित्र"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"बहुविकल्पी प्रश्न","questions":[{"question":"‘हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ’ पाठ के लेखक/लेखिका कौन हैं?","options":["महादेवी वर्मा","सुमित्रानंदन पंत","जयशंकर प्रसाद","सुबहानंद"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"पाठ में ‘हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ’ से अभिप्राय मुख्यतः क्या है?","options":["हिमालय की ऊँचाई","हिमालय की पर्वत-शृंखलाएँ जो भारत को बाँधती-सी लगती हैं","हिमालय की नदियाँ","हिमालय के जंगल"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"हिमालय की गोद में ‘लाखों वर्षों की जमा हुई बर्फ़’ किसका प्रतीक मानी गई है?","options":["शक्ति और स्थिरता का","अंधकार का","अज्ञान का","शोर-गुल का"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"लेखिका ने हिमालय को किस रूप में देखा है?","options":["केवल पर्यटन स्थल के रूप में","केवल वन-संपदा के रूप में","सुरक्षा-कवच और प्रेरणा-स्रोत के रूप में","व्यापार के साधन के रूप में"],"answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"रिक्त स्थान पूर्ति","questions":[{"question":"हिमालय की ऊँची-ऊँची चोटियाँ भारत के लिए एक प्रकार की __________ की तरह हैं।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"लेखिका को हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ उनके देश की __________ और __________ का प्रतीक लगती हैं।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"हिमालय की गोद से निकलने वाली नदियाँ मैदानों में __________ और __________ फैलाती हैं।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"हिमालय की शांत, गंभीर और स्थिर मुद्रा हमारे मन में __________, __________ और साहस भर देती है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"लघु उत्तरीय प्रश्न","questions":[{"question":"लेखिका को हिमालय की पर्वत-शृंखलाएँ ‘बेड़ियाँ’ जैसी क्यों लगती हैं?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"हिमालय हमारे देश की रक्षा किस प्रकार करता है?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"हिमालय से निकलने वाली नदियों का हमारे लिए क्या महत्त्व है?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"पाठ के अनुसार हिमालय की ‘शांत एवं गंभीर मुद्रा’ मनुष्य को क्या सिखाती है?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"दीर्घ उत्तरीय प्रश्न","questions":[{"question":"पाठ के आधार पर ‘हिमालय भारत के लिए केवल प्राकृतिक सौंदर्य नहीं, बल्कि प्रेरणा और शक्ति का भी स्रोत है’ – इस कथन को स्पष्ट कीजिए।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4},{"question":"‘हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ’ शीर्षक आपको कैसा प्रतीत होता है? पाठ की घटनाओं और वर्णनों के आधार पर समझाइए कि यह शीर्षक क्यों उपयुक्त है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4},{"question":"हिमालय को लेकर लेखिका के मन में उपजे भावों और उसके स्वभाव-चित्रण को पाठ के आधार पर अपने शब्दों में लिखिए।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4}]},{"type":"match","title":"स्तंभ मिलान कीजिए","questions":[{"question":"स्तंभ ‘क’ को स्तंभ ‘ख’ से मिलाइए:","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"हिमालय की चोटियाँ","right":"दूर-दूर तक उजाला और जीवन बाँटती हैं"},{"left":"हिमालय की नदियाँ","right":"शांति, धीरज और साहस का संचार करती हैं"},{"left":"हिमालय की गोद","right":"लाखों वर्षों की जमाई हुई बर्फ़ का भंडार"},{"left":"हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ","right":"देश की सुरक्षा और एकता का प्रतीक"},{"left":"हिमालय का स्वरूप","right":"प्रेरणा और शक्ति का स्रोत"}]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"महादेवी वर्मा"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"हिमालय की पर्वत-शृंखलाएँ जो भारत को बाँधती-सी लगती हैं"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"शक्ति और स्थिरता का"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"सुरक्षा-कवच और प्रेरणा-स्रोत के रूप में"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"किले / सुरक्षा-कवच (उपयुक्त शब्द में से कोई भी स्वीकार्य)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"सुरक्षा और एकता (या अखंडता)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"उपजाऊपन (उर्वरता) और समृद्धि"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"शांति, धैर्य और साहस"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"लेखिका को हिमालय की पर्वत-शृंखलाएँ चारों ओर से देश को घेरती हुई, बाँधती हुई प्रतीत होती हैं। इन्हीं घिरी हुई पर्वतमालाओं को वे ‘हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ’ कहती हैं, जो भारत को मजबूती से थामे हुए हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"हिमालय उत्तर दिशा में एक ऊँची, मज़बूत दीवार की तरह है जो शीत हवाओं और बाहरी शत्रुओं से देश की रक्षा करता है। उसकी ऊँची-ऊँची चोटियाँ प्राकृतिक सुरक्षा-कवच का काम करती हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"हिमालय से निकलने वाली नदियाँ मैदानों को सिंचाई के लिए जल देती हैं, मिट्टी को उपजाऊ बनाती हैं और दूर-दूर तक बसने वाले लोगों के जीवन में समृद्धि तथा प्रकाश फैलाती हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"हिमालय की शांत, गंभीर और स्थिर मुद्रा मनुष्य को धैर्य, संयम, साहस और ऊँचे आदर्शों के लिए अडिग रहने की सीख देती है।"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"हिमालय भारत के लिए केवल प्राकृतिक सौंदर्य नहीं, बल्कि प्रेरणा और शक्ति का स्रोत भी है क्योंकि उसकी हिमाच्छादित चोटियाँ दूर से ही मन में श्रद्धा और आश्चर्य भर देती हैं। हिमालय की गोद में जमा बर्फ़ हमारे देश की संचित शक्ति और दृढ़ता का प्रतीक है।\nहिमालय से निकलने वाली नदियाँ भारत के विशाल मैदानों को जीवनदायिनी जल-संपदा प्रदान करती हैं और दूर-दूर तक समृद्धि फैलाती हैं। उसकी स्थिर और गंभीर मुद्रा मनुष्य को भी स्थिर, धैर्यवान और साहसी बनने की प्रेरणा देती है। इस प्रकार हिमालय हमें बाहरी सुरक्षा के साथ-साथ भीतर से भी बल और प्रेरणा प्रदान करता है।"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"‘हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ’ शीर्षक पहली नज़र में बंधन का संकेत देता है, परंतु पाठ में यह बंधन सुरक्षा और एकता का प्रतीक है। लेखिका ने हिमालय को ऐसी बेड़ियों के रूप में देखा है जो भारत को चारों ओर से घेरकर उसकी रक्षा करती हैं और उसे मज़बूती से बाँधे रहती हैं।\nये बेड़ियाँ दासता की नहीं, शक्ति और सुरक्षा की बेड़ियाँ हैं। हिमालय की ये पर्वत-शृंखलाएँ देश को प्राकृतिक रूप से बाँधती हैं, उसे अलग पहचान देती हैं और उसके गौरव की रक्षा करती हैं। इस दृष्टि से ‘हिमालय की बेड़ियाँ’ शीर्षक अत्यंत सार्थक और उपयुक्त है।"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"पाठ में लेखिका ने हिमालय को अत्यंत भव्य, शांत, गंभीर और स्थिर स्वरूप में चित्रित किया है। उसकी ऊँची-ऊँची चोटियाँ जैसे आकाश से बातें करती हैं, फिर भी वे विनम्रता के साथ धरती की गोद में स्थित हैं। उसकी गोद में लाखों वर्षों से जमा बर्फ़ है जो उसकी संचित शक्ति और दृढ़ता को दर्शाती है।\nहिमालय के प्रति लेखिका के मन में श्रद्धा, प्रेम और गर्व की भावना है। उन्हें हिमालय भारत की सुरक्षा-कवच, उसकी शक्ति, एकता और प्रेरणा का प्रतीक लगता है। हिमालय की नदियाँ, उसकी चोटियाँ और उसकी गंभीरता – ये सब मिलकर लेखिका के मन में मातृभूमि के प्रति और भी अधिक लगाव और आत्मविश्वास भर देती हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"हिमालय की चोटियाँ – किले / सुरक्षा-कवच\nहिमालय की नदियाँ – दूर-दूर तक उजाला और जीवन बाँटती हैं\nहिमालय की गोद – लाखों वर्षों की जमाई हुई बर्फ़ का भंडार\nहिमालय की बेड़ियाँ – देश की सुरक्षा और एकता का प्रतीक\nहिमालय का स्वरूप – प्रेरणा और शक्ति का स्रोत"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-02T04:23:22.400Z"},{"id":54,"serialNumber":"QW-260302-00054","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board","subject":"English","chapter":"In time of silver rain","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"In Time of Silver Rain – Worksheet (Grade 7 English)","instructions":"Read the poem 'In Time of Silver Rain' carefully from your textbook before attempting this worksheet. Answer all questions. Choose the correct option in MCQs, fill in the blanks with suitable words from the poem, and mark True or False as instructed.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist illustration of gentle silver raindrops falling on the ground with tiny green shoots sprouting up","position":"top-right","altText":"Silver rain falling on soil with new plants growing"},{"description":"Simple line-art of children joyfully running and jumping in a light rain with small flowers blooming around them","position":"between-sections","altText":"Children playing happily in the rain among flowers"},{"description":"Minimalist drawing of trees with fresh green leaves and birds flying in a bright sky after the rain","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Trees with new leaves and birds in the sky after rain"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. In the poem, what happens \"in time of silver rain\"?","options":["Snow begins to fall on the hills","The earth puts forth new life again","The leaves fall from the trees","The sun shines very brightly"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The poet compares the rain to \"silver\" mainly to show that it is","options":["heavy and dangerous","cold and painful","bright and beautiful","dark and frightening"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. According to the poem, what happens to the grass when the silver rain falls?","options":["It dries up and turns brown","It disappears under the soil","It grows greening all around","It is eaten by animals"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. What do the \"happy flowers\" in the poem do in the time of silver rain?","options":["They sleep under the snow","They rise and dance beneath the sun","They fall down from the trees","They change into birds and fly away"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"5. In time of silver rain, the ______ puts forth new life again.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The poet says that in the time of silver rain, the \"happy ______\" rise and dance beneath the sun.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The grass grows ______ all around in the time of silver rain.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section C – True or False","questions":[{"question":"8. In the poem, birds are described as flying through the sky in time of silver rain.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. The poem says that in time of silver rain, \"the wonder spreads of life, of life, of life.\"","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. In the poem, children are completely sad and afraid when the silver rain falls.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"The earth puts forth new life again"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"bright and beautiful"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"It grows greening all around"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"They rise and dance beneath the sun"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"earth"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"flowers"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"greening"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"False"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-02T02:58:24.403Z"},{"id":53,"serialNumber":"QW-260302-00053","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board","subject":"English ","chapter":"It’s a small world","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"It’s a Small World – Worksheet (English, Grade 7)","instructions":"Read the lesson ‘It’s a Small World’ carefully before attempting the worksheet. Answer all questions in the space provided. Choose the most appropriate options for MCQs and write neatly.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist globe with small children holding hands around it, symbolising unity of the world","position":"top-right","altText":"Children holding hands around a globe"},{"description":"Simple line-art of different houses connected by dotted lines to a central globe, showing that people everywhere are connected","position":"between-sections","altText":"Houses from different places connected to a globe"},{"description":"A minimalist illustration of a girl looking at a world map with flags of different countries in soft colors","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Girl looking at a colorful world map with flags"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. In the lesson ‘It’s a Small World’, when does the narrator feel that the world is really small?","options":["When he sees people quarrelling","When he realises that people everywhere have similar feelings and needs","When he reads a story book","When he goes on a picnic"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"2. According to the lesson, what makes people in different parts of the world feel close to each other?","options":["Their different languages","Their clothes and food","Their common hopes, dreams and emotions","Their festivals and holidays"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"3. The title ‘It’s a Small World’ mainly suggests that:","options":["The Earth is very tiny in size","We can travel quickly by aeroplane","People everywhere are connected and similar in many ways","There are very few countries on the Earth"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"4. In the lesson, what helps us know more about people living in far-off places?","options":["Television, books and the internet","Only school textbooks","Only letters","Only newspapers"],"answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"5. The lesson ‘It’s a Small World’ tells us that in spite of different languages and customs, people share the same human __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"6. The narrator realises that children all over the world like to play, laugh and __________ together.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"7. The world seems small because we can easily know about people in other countries through __________ and other modern means of communication.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section C – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"8. Why does the narrator say that the world is ‘small’ even though the Earth is big?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"9. Mention any two things that are common between children everywhere, as described in the lesson.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"10. What message does the lesson ‘It’s a Small World’ give to the readers?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"When he realises that people everywhere have similar feelings and needs."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Their common hopes, dreams and emotions."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"People everywhere are connected and similar in many ways."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Television, books and the internet."},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"feelings"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"learn"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"television"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"He says the world is ‘small’ because modern means of communication and travel bring people closer, and he finds that people everywhere are similar in their basic needs and feelings."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Any two: They like to play; they like to laugh; they like to make friends; they go to school; they love their families."},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"The lesson tells us that all human beings are connected, share common feelings, and should live with understanding and friendship, seeing the world as one big family."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-02T02:55:01.241Z"},{"id":52,"serialNumber":"QW-260301-00052","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"हिंदी ","chapter":"हम पंछी उन्मुक्त गगन के","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"हम पंछी उन्मुक्त गगन के — कार्यपत्रक (कक्षा 7, CBSE)","instructions":"• इस कार्यपत्रक को ध्यान से पढ़कर हल कीजिए।\n• जहाँ आवश्यक हो, पुस्तक में दिए गए पद्यांश को पढ़कर उत्तर लिखिए।\n• उत्तर संक्षिप्त और स्पष्ट लिखें।\n• सभी प्रश्न ‘हम पंछी उन्मुक्त गगन के’ (NCERT कक्षा 7 हिंदी) पाठ पर आधारित हैं।","graphics":[{"description":"नीले आकाश में उड़ते हुए कई छोटे रंग-बिरंगे पक्षियों की सरल, रंगीन रेखाचित्र शैली की चित्रकारी","position":"top-right","altText":"खुले गगन में उड़ते पक्षी"},{"description":"हरी घास, कुछ पेड़ों और एक खुले पिंजरे के पास बैठे दो-तीन पक्षियों का मिनिमलिस्ट चित्र","position":"between-sections","altText":"खुला पिंजरा और स्वतंत्र पक्षी"},{"description":"एक बच्चे की किताब और उसके ऊपर बैठा एक छोटा पक्षी, चारों ओर हल्के बादलों और सूरज के साथ रंगीन चित्र","position":"bottom-left","altText":"किताब और उस पर बैठा पक्षी"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड–1 : बहुविकल्पी प्रश्न","questions":[{"question":"कविता ‘हम पंछी उन्मुक्त गगन के’ में पक्षियों की सबसे बड़ी इच्छा क्या है?","options":["दाना चुगना","स्वतंत्र होकर खुले गगन में उड़ना","पेड़ पर बैठना","पानी पीना"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"कविता में पिंजरे को किससे भरा हुआ बताया गया है?","options":["सोना और चाँदी से","नारियल और मिठाई से","दुख, वेदना और आँसुओं से","खुशियों से"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"कवि ने पिंजरे में बंद रहने की तुलना किससे की है?","options":["स्वर्ग से","नरक से","बगीचे से","समुद्र से"],"answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड–2 : रिक्त स्थान भरिए","questions":[{"question":"1. हम पंछी __________ गगन के, __________ क्यों बाँधें हम।","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"2. साँसों में बसती है _________, पिंजरे में कैसे _________ हम।","answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"3. पिंजरे के अंदर तो केवल _________, _________ और _________ हैं।","answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"खंड–3 : लघु उत्तरीय प्रश्न","questions":[{"question":"कविता में पक्षी ‘उन्मुक्त गगन’ से क्या अभिप्राय रखते हैं?","answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"पक्षी पिंजरे में बंद होने को क्यों पसंद नहीं करते?","answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"‘हम पंछी उन्मुक्त गगन के’ कविता में पक्षियों का मनोभाव क्या है?","answerSpaceLines":2}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"खंड–4 : दीर्घ उत्तरीय प्रश्न","questions":[{"question":"कविता ‘हम पंछी उन्मुक्त गगन के’ में स्वतंत्रता और बंधन के विरोधाभास को अपने शब्दों में संक्षेप में लिखिए।","answerSpaceLines":4}]},{"type":"match","title":"खंड–5 : मिलान कीजिए","questions":[{"question":"कॉलम ‘क’ का कॉलम ‘ख’ से मिलान कीजिए:","answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"उन्मुक्त गगन","right":"स्वतंत्रता और खुलापन"},{"left":"पिंजरा","right":"बंधन और कैद का प्रतीक"},{"left":"दुख, वेदना, आँसू","right":"पिंजरे के भीतर का वातावरण"},{"left":"स्वर्ग-सुख","right":"खुले आकाश में उड़ने का आनंद"}]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"खंड–6 : एक शब्द / संक्षिप्त उत्तर लिखिए","questions":[{"question":"पक्षी किस प्रकार के गगन में उड़ना चाहते हैं? (एक शब्द में)","answerSpaceLines":1},{"question":"पक्षियों के रहने की स्वाभाविक जगह क्या है? (एक या दो शब्द में)","answerSpaceLines":1}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"स्वतंत्र होकर खुले गगन में उड़ना"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"दुख, वेदना और आँसुओं से"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"नरक से"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"उन्मुक्त, बंधन"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"स्वतंत्रता, रह सकते"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"दुख, वेदना, आँसू"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"‘उन्मुक्त गगन’ से तात्पर्य खुले, विशाल और स्वतंत्र आकाश से है जहाँ पक्षी बिना किसी बंधन के स्वतंत्र रूप से उड़ सकें।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"पक्षी पिंजरे में इसलिए बंद नहीं रहना चाहते क्योंकि वहाँ उन्हें बंधन, दुख, वेदना और आँसू मिलते हैं; उनकी स्वतंत्रता छिन जाती है और वे स्वाभाविक जीवन नहीं जी पाते।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"कविता में पक्षियों का मनोभाव स्वतंत्रता की तीव्र चाह, बंधन के प्रति घृणा और खुले आकाश में निर्बाध उड़ान भरने की लालसा का है।"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"कविता में स्वतंत्रता और बंधन के बीच स्पष्ट विरोधाभास दिखाया गया है। पक्षी ‘उन्मुक्त गगन’ के हैं, वे खुले, विस्तृत आकाश में उड़कर स्वर्ग-सुख पाना चाहते हैं। उनकी साँसों में स्वतंत्रता बसती है, इसलिए वे पिंजरे के बंधन में नहीं रह सकते। दूसरी ओर पिंजरा दुख, वेदना और आँसुओं से भरा नरक जैसा स्थान बताया गया है, जहाँ उनकी स्वाभाविक खुशी और उड़ान छिन जाती है। इस प्रकार कविता में स्वतंत्रता को सबसे बड़ा सुख और बंधन को सबसे बड़ा दुख बताया गया है।"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"उन्मुक्त गगन — स्वतंत्रता और खुलापन; पिंजरा — बंधन और कैद का प्रतीक; दुख, वेदना, आँसू — पिंजरे के भीतर का वातावरण; स्वर्ग-सुख — खुले आकाश में उड़ने का आनंद"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"उन्मुक्त"},{"sectionIndex":5,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"खुला आकाश / उन्मुक्त गगन / प्रकृति"}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-03-01T19:07:57.206Z"},{"id":51,"serialNumber":"QW-260301-00051","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"Hindi","chapter":"रहीम के दोहे ","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Class 7 Hindi – रहीम के दोहे (NCERT Vasant – भाग 2) Worksheet","instructions":"• सभी प्रश्न ध्यान से पढ़कर हल करें।\n• उत्तर देते समय पाठ्यपुस्तक ‘वसंत भाग–2’ के पाठ ‘रहीम के दोहे’ की भाषा और भाव पर ध्यान दें।\n• जहाँ पूछा गया हो, वहाँ दोहे भी उद्धृत कर सकते हैं।\n• साफ-सुथरी लिखावट में उत्तर लिखें।","graphics":[{"description":"रंग-बिरंगी रेखाचित्र शैली में एक संत-स्वरूप वृद्ध कवि, सिर पर पगड़ी और हाथ में कलम, सामने ताड़पत्र पर दोहे लिखते हुए।","position":"top-right","altText":"कलम से लिखते हुए रहीम जैसे कवि का सरल चित्र"},{"description":"मिनिमलिस्ट, रंगीन लाइन-आर्ट में दो हाथ – एक हाथ दूसरे की मदद करता हुआ, पृष्ठभूमि में छोटे-छोटे दिल के प्रतीक, दया और करुणा दिखाते हुए।","position":"between-sections","altText":"दया और करुणा दर्शाता दो हाथों का चित्र"},{"description":"सरल चित्र जिसमें एक व्यक्ति अपने होंठों पर उंगली रखकर चुप रहने का संकेत कर रहा है, पृष्ठभूमि में हल्के रंगों के बादल।","position":"bottom-left","altText":"कम बोलने और संयम दिखाता चित्र"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड – 1 : बहुविकल्पी प्रश्न (MCQs)","questions":[{"question":"रहीम के एक दोहे में ‘देनहार’ किसे कहा गया है?","options":["राजा को","प्रजा को","ईश्वर को","माता–पिता को"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"‘रहिमन धागा प्रेम का’ दोहे में ‘धागा’ किस चीज़ का प्रतीक है?","options":["धन का","प्रेम का","शक्ति का","ज्ञान का"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"रहीम के अनुसार, किसकी निंदा नहीं करनी चाहिए?","options":["अपने मित्र की","तेज धूप की","छोटी नदी और छोटे व्यक्ति की","गुरु की"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड – 2 : रिक्त स्थान भरिए","questions":[{"question":"1. रहीम कहते हैं – \"देनहार कोउ _____ हैं, देखि रहत जगत सारा\"।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. \"रहिमन धागा प्रेम का, मत _____ चटकाय\" – यहाँ प्रेम संबंधों को धागे से तुलना करते हुए उसे न तोड़ने की बात कही गई है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. रहीम के अनुसार, \"निवहिं जल में रहि करि _____, सीप समाना पाकर\" – सीप जैसे अच्छा मिलते ही अपने अंदर समा लेती है।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"खंड – 3 : संक्षिप्त उत्तर प्रश्न","questions":[{"question":"1. रहीम ‘रहिमन धागा प्रेम का’ दोहे में प्रेम के संबंध को किससे जोड़कर समझाते हैं? संक्षेप में लिखिए।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. \"रहिमन निज मन की व्यथा, मन ही राखो गोय\" – इस दोहे से रहीम क्या सीख देते हैं?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. रहीम ‘देनहार’ वाले दोहे के माध्यम से किस प्रकार के व्यवहार की आलोचना करते हैं?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"खंड – 4 : दीर्घ उत्तर प्रश्न","questions":[{"question":"1. रहीम के दोहों में दया और करुणा का भाव कैसे व्यक्त हुआ है? पाठ में दिए गए दोहों के आधार पर 3–4 पंक्तियों में उत्तर लिखिए।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. \"छीके ऊपर रखे अन्न को देखकर कबूतरों का व्यवहार\" और रहीम के ‘देनहार’ वाले दोहे के बीच क्या समानता है? पाठ के अनुसार समझाइए।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"खंड – 5 : मिलान कीजिए (दोहा और भाव)","questions":[{"question":"निम्नलिखित दोहों को उनके उचित अर्थ/भाव से मिलाइए:","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"क. रहिमन धागा प्रेम का, मत तोरो चटकाय","right":"i. भीतर की पीड़ा सबको बताने से अपमान होता है"},{"left":"ख. रहिमन निज मन की व्यथा, मन ही राखो गोय","right":"ii. प्रेम का संबंध एक बार टूट जाए तो फिर नहीं जुड़ता"},{"left":"ग. देनहार कोउ और है, भेजत जो दिन रात","right":"iii. दान-उपहार का असली देने वाला ईश्वर है"},{"left":"घ. निंदक नियरे राखिए","right":"iv. आलोचक हमें हमारी कमियाँ बताकर सुधार में मदद करता है"}]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"ईश्वर को"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"प्रेम का"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"छोटी नदी और छोटे व्यक्ति की"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"कोउ और"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"तोरो"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"मेघ"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"इस दोहे में रहीम प्रेम के संबंध को ‘धागा’ मानते हैं। जैसे धागा एक बार टूट जाए तो गाँठ पड़ जाती है और पहले जैसा नहीं रहता, वैसे ही प्रेम का संबंध भी टूटने पर वैसा नहीं रह जाता, इसलिए उसे नहीं तोड़ना चाहिए।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"इस दोहे में रहीम कहते हैं कि अपने मन की व्यथा सबके सामने प्रकट नहीं करनी चाहिए। मन की पीड़ा मन में ही रखनी चाहिए, क्योंकि सब लोग उसे समझेंगे नहीं, उलटे अपमान हो सकता है।"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"‘देनहार’ वाले दोहे में रहीम उन लोगों की आलोचना करते हैं जो किसी दान या उपहार के लिए केवल सामने वाले को ही बड़ा मानते हैं और असली देने वाले ईश्वर को भूल जाते हैं। वे दिखावे और चाटुकारिता वाले व्यवहार की निंदा करते हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"रहीम के दोहों में दया और करुणा का भाव इस बात से व्यक्त होता है कि वे प्रेम का धागा न तोड़ने, किसी की निंदा न करने, और दूसरों के दुख–दर्द को समझने की सीख देते हैं। वे संबंधों को संभालकर रखने, दूसरों की मदद करने और ईश्वर की करुणा को याद रखने की बात करते हैं।"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"कबूतर छीके पर रखे अन्न को देखकर यह नहीं समझते कि असली देने वाला कौन है, वे केवल सामने दिख रहे व्यक्ति पर ही ध्यान देते हैं। रहीम भी ‘देनहार’ वाले दोहे में कहते हैं कि लोग केवल सामने वाले दाता को ही मान देते हैं, पर असली देनहार ईश्वर को भूल जाते हैं। दोनों जगह यह सीख दी गई है कि हमें वास्तविक स्रोत यानी ईश्वर को नहीं भूलना चाहिए।"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"क – ii, ख – i, ग – iii, घ – iv"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-01T19:05:33.251Z"},{"id":50,"serialNumber":"QW-260301-00050","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"hindi","chapter":"nilkanth","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"कक्षा 7 हिंदी (वसंत भाग – 2) — अध्याय: नीलकंठ — कार्यपत्रक","instructions":"• नीचे दिए गए सभी प्रश्न ध्यान से पढ़कर हल कीजिए।\n• जहाँ विकल्प दिए हों वहाँ सही विकल्प चुनकर लिखिए।\n• रिक्त स्थानों में केवल उचित शब्द/शब्द समूह लिखिए।\n• कार्यपत्रक को स्वच्छ और सुगठित रूप में पूरा कीजिए।","graphics":[{"description":"रंग-बिरंगे पेड़ों और रास्ते के साथ गाँव से गुजरती एक पतली पगडंडी का सादा रेखाचित्र, जिस पर एक छोटा सा लड़का उत्सुकता से दूर देख रहा है","position":"top-right","altText":"गाँव की पगडंडी पर खड़ा उत्सुक बालक"},{"description":"हल्के रंगों में झील के किनारे उड़ते पक्षियों और पानी में झलकते आकाश का न्यूनतम रेखाचित्र","position":"between-sections","altText":"झील और उड़ते पक्षियों का सरल चित्र"},{"description":"रंगीन रेखाओं से बना छोटा सा मंदिर, पास में पेड़ और ऊपर नीला आकाश","position":"bottom-left","altText":"पेड़ों के बीच स्थित छोटा मंदिर"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड – 1 : बहुविकल्पी प्रश्न (MCQ)","questions":[{"question":"नीलकंठ के अंदर ‘हिलोरें लेती हुई बेचैनी’ किस बात को लेकर थी?","options":["घर वापस जाने को लेकर","यात्रा की अवधि और उसका उद्देश्य जानने को लेकर","भोजन न मिलने को लेकर","दोस्तों से न मिलने को लेकर"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"नीलकंठ यात्रा पर निकलने से पहले माँ ने उसके लिए क्या किया?","options":["उसे बहुत सारा धन दिया","उसके लिए नए कपड़े खरीदे","उसके लिए खाना बाँधा और मार्ग के लिए आवश्यक चीज़ें रखीं","उसके साथ स्वयं यात्रा पर चली गईं"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"नीलकंठ यात्रा के दौरान रात में अक्सर कहाँ ठहरता था?","options":["सरायों और धर्मशालाओं में","स्कूल में","रेलवे स्टेशन पर","किसान के खेत में"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"नीलकंठ को अपना घर क्यों याद आता था?","options":["क्योंकि उसे गाँव पसंद नहीं था","क्योंकि उसे माँ की ममता और स्नेह की कमी महसूस होती थी","क्योंकि उसे अपना कमरा बड़ा लगता था","क्योंकि उसे स्कूल की पढ़ाई नहीं अच्छी लगती थी"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड – 2 : सत्य / असत्य (True / False)","questions":[{"question":"नीलकंठ बिना किसी को बताए घर से चुपचाप निकल गया था।","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"यात्रा के दौरान नीलकंठ को हर जगह बहुत आराम और सुविधा मिलती थी।","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"नीलकंठ ने रास्ते में मिलने वाले लोगों से बहुत कुछ सीखा।","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड – 3 : रिक्त स्थान भरिए","questions":[{"question":"1. नीलकंठ के मन में यात्रा के प्रति गहरा ___________ था।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. माँ की आँखों में नीलकंठ के लिए ___________ और चिंता दोनों झलकते थे।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. यात्रा के दौरान नीलकंठ ने कठिनाइयों का सामना ___________ के साथ किया।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"यात्रा की अवधि और उसका उद्देश्य जानने को लेकर"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"उसके लिए खाना बाँधा और मार्ग के लिए आवश्यक चीज़ें रखीं"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"सरायों और धर्मशालाओं में"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"क्योंकि उसे माँ की ममता और स्नेह की कमी महसूस होती थी"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"जिज्ञासा"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"ममता"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"धैर्य"}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-03-01T18:46:17.773Z"},{"id":49,"serialNumber":"QW-260301-00049","userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"hindi","chapter":"nilkanth","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"हिंदी कार्यपत्रक – नीलकंठ (कक्षा 7, CBSE)","instructions":"• नीचे दिए गए प्रश्न ध्यान से पढ़कर हल कीजिए।\n• सभी प्रश्न पुस्तक ‘नीलकंठ’ पाठ पर आधारित हैं।\n• जहाँ आवश्यक हो, पूर्ण वाक्य में उत्तर लिखें।\n• अनुमान से नहीं, सोच–समझकर उत्तर चुनें।","graphics":[{"description":"रास्ते पर चलते एक साधु का सरल, रंगीन रेखाचित्र, पीठ पर गठरी और हाथ में लाठी, पीछे पहाड़ और पेड़","position":"top-right","altText":"यात्रा करते हुए नीलकंठ का चित्र"},{"description":"एक गाँव का रंगीन, न्यूनतम चित्र – कुछ मिट्टी के घर, पेड़ और पास से बहती पतली नदी","position":"between-sections","altText":"गाँव और प्रकृति का दृश्य"},{"description":"मंदिर की सीढ़ियों पर बैठा एक किशोर साधु, पास में जल से भरा लोटा और फूल, हल्के रंगों में रेखाचित्र","position":"bottom-left","altText":"धार्मिक स्थान पर ध्यान में लीन नीलकंठ"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड – 1 : बहुविकल्पीय प्रश्न (MCQ)","questions":[{"question":"‘नीलकंठ’ पाठ के नायक नीलकंठ किस रूप में यात्रा पर निकले थे?","options":["व्यापारी के रूप में","किशोर साधु के रूप में","किसान के रूप में","सैनिक के रूप में"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"नीलकंठ की यात्रा का मुख्य उद्देश्य क्या था?","options":["देश भ्रमण और व्यापार करना","परिवार से दूर रहना","जीवन को समझना और अनुभव प्राप्त करना","नई–नई वस्तुएँ इकट्ठी करना"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"नीलकंठ को रास्ते में भोजन अधिकतर किससे मिलता था?","options":["होटलों से","दुकानदारों से","गाँव के दयालु लोगों से","सरकारी रसोई से"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"नीलकंठ की कौन–सी विशेषता ग्रामीणों को सबसे अधिक प्रभावित करती थी?","options":["उनका क्रोध","उनकी धन–सम्पत्ति","उनकी शालीनता और विनम्रता","उनकी ऊँची आवाज़"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड – 2 : रिक्त स्थान पूर्ति (Fill in the Blanks)","questions":[{"question":"1. नीलकंठ कम से कम सामान लेकर ______ पर निकल पड़े।","options":["यात्रा","कक्षा","खेल","विश्राम"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. नीलकंठ को रात में ठहरने के लिए अक्सर ______ या मंदिर मिल जाते थे।","options":["बाज़ार","स्कूल","धर्मशाला","अस्पताल"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. नीलकंठ हर स्थिति में ______ और धैर्य से काम लेते थे।","options":["क्रोध","शांति","शोर","भय"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड – 3 : सत्य / असत्य (True / False)","questions":[{"question":"1. नीलकंठ यात्रा के दौरान किसी से भी बात नहीं करते थे।","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. नीलकंठ हर जगह स्वयं काम करने और सेवा करने में विश्वास रखते थे।","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. नीलकंठ को कठिनाइयों से डर लगता था, इसलिए वे जल्दी घर लौट आए।","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड – 4 : रिक्त स्थान पूर्ति (शब्द–चयन आधारित)","questions":[{"question":"1. नीलकंठ ने यात्रा के दौरान प्रकृति की ______ को निकट से देखा। (सुंदरता / थकान)","options":["सुंदरता","थकान","भूल","कठोरता"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. नीलकंठ के सरल स्वभाव ने लोगों के ______ को छू लिया। (दिल / घर)","options":["दिल","घर","मार्ग","कपड़े"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. नीलकंठ की यात्रा हमें ______ और त्याग का संदेश देती है। (सेवा / क्रोध)","options":["सेवा","क्रोध","ईर्ष्या","आलस्य"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"किशोर साधु के रूप में"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"जीवन को समझना और अनुभव प्राप्त करना"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"गाँव के दयालु लोगों से"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"उनकी शालीनता और विनम्रता"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"यात्रा"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"धर्मशाला"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"शांति"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"सुंदरता"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"दिल"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"सेवा"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-03-01T18:30:08.120Z"},{"id":40,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"history","chapter":"the making of regional culture.","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Making of Regional Cultures – Worksheet (CBSE Class 7 History)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully.\n• Answer briefly and to the point in the space provided.\n• Use examples from the chapter ‘The Making of Regional Cultures’ wherever possible.\n• Draw neat and clear labelling lines if you choose to sketch any part in the margin.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple, colorful line-art illustration of a medieval Indian temple with a curved shikhara, small flags on top and a few trees in the background.","position":"top-right","altText":"Minimalist colorful sketch of a medieval Indian temple"},{"description":"Minimalist, child-friendly illustration of two classical dancers in traditional costume, one in Bharatanatyam pose and another in Kathak pose, with soft pastel colors.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Colorful line drawing of two Indian classical dancers"},{"description":"Simple line-art of a royal court scene with a king on a throne, a bard with a musical instrument, and a scribe writing on a palm leaf.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Minimalist illustration of a medieval Indian royal court"}],"sections":[{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section A – Identify from Sketch","questions":[{"question":"Q1. Look at the sketch described below:\nA simple line drawing shows a tall temple structure with a curving tower rising upward like a mountain peak. The tower is made of many horizontal layers that gradually become smaller as they go up. A small flag is drawn on the top of the tower. At the base, there is a rectangular structure representing the main shrine.\nWhat kind of temple architectural style does this sketch represent?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Q2. Look at the sketch described below:\nA simple line drawing shows a woman standing in a graceful dance posture. One leg is slightly bent, the other stretched, with arms raised in a curved form. She wears a fan-shaped garment around her waist, and there is a temple-like backdrop behind her. Small bells are marked at her ankles.\nWhich classical dance form from South India does this sketch most likely represent?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Q3. Look at the sketch described below:\nA line drawing shows a long, narrow boat with raised ends. Many tiny stick figures are seated closely together, holding long oars. The boat is shown on wavy lines that indicate a river. On the bank, coconut trees and a few small houses with sloping roofs are drawn.\nWhich regional cultural practice or event from Kerala does this sketch most closely represent?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Q4. Look at the sketch described below:\nA simple outline map of the Indian subcontinent is drawn. On the eastern coast, near the Bay of Bengal, a small star is marked and labelled “A”. Near this star, a small temple symbol (a tiny tower) is drawn.\nName one famous temple or temple-town from this eastern coastal region that became an important centre of regional culture.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Q5. Look at the sketch described below:\nA small rectangular drawing shows a man playing a stringed instrument that looks like a lute. He is sitting in front of a king who is seated on a throne. Behind the man, there is another small figure holding a rolled-up manuscript.\nWhich type of courtly cultural figure, important for spreading regional traditions through stories and songs, is being shown here?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Q6. Look at the sketch described below:\nA line drawing shows a manuscript page. The top portion has pictures of people wearing crowns and rich clothes. Below the pictures, there are neat horizontal lines representing writing in a local language script, not in Sanskrit.\nWhat does this sketch represent about the development of regional cultures?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Q7. Look at the sketch described below:\nA simple rectangular panel shows a scene of warriors riding horses, with swords raised. Beneath the horses are small designs of lotuses and vines. The panel looks like it is carved in stone and is part of a wall.\nWhat type of architectural decoration is suggested in this sketch, commonly found on regional temples and palaces?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Q8. Look at the sketch described below:\nA large hall is drawn with many pillars. At one end, a slightly raised platform shows musicians with drums and string instruments. In front of them, a dancer is performing while a small audience sits on the floor.\nWhich aspect of regional culture is best shown in this sketch?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Q9. Look at the sketch described below:\nA map outline of India is drawn. In the north-western region, a small shield and sword symbol is drawn and labelled “B”. Near it, a small fort is sketched on a hill.\nWhich regional group, known for its heroic traditions and ballads, is most likely represented by label “B”?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Q10. Look at the sketch described below:\nA line drawing shows a small classroom in olden times. Children sit on the floor with wooden writing boards. On the wall is a hanging scroll with writing in a regional language. Outside the window, a temple spire is visible.\nWhat does this sketch show about the link between temples and the growth of regional cultures?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"The Nagara style of temple architecture (North Indian style with a curving shikhara)."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Bharatanatyam, a classical dance form from Tamil Nadu (South India)."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"The snake-boat races (Vallamkali) of Kerala, linked to Onam and regional culture."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"One correct example: Jagannatha temple at Puri in Odisha (or the temple-town of Puri)."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"A bard or court poet/singer who recites stories and ballads to the king (such as Charans and Bhopas in Rajasthan)."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"It represents regional language manuscripts and literature being produced, showing the growth of regional languages and courts using them instead of only Sanskrit."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"Stone carvings or sculpted panels used as decorative reliefs on regional temples and palaces."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"Courtly performances of music and dance as part of regional cultural traditions."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":8,"answer":"The Rajputs, known for their heroic traditions, forts and ballads about bravery."},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":9,"answer":"It shows that temples acted as centres of learning where regional languages were taught, helping regional cultures to grow around temple institutions."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T20:16:00.800Z"},{"id":39,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"history","chapter":"18th century political formation","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"18th Century Political Formations – Worksheet (CBSE Class 7 History)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully and answer in the space provided.\n• For MCQs and True/False, tick (✓) the correct option.\n• For Fill in the Blanks, write the correct word(s) in the blank.\n• Do not use rough work in the answer spaces.\n• Maintain neat and legible handwriting.","graphics":[{"description":"Colorful minimalist map outline of India with small icons showing a fort, a palace, and a marching army to depict different 18th-century kingdoms.","position":"top-right","altText":"Simple map of India with symbols for kingdoms and armies"},{"description":"Child-friendly line-art of a Mughal-style fort gateway with flags in soft colors, representing regional kingdoms.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Mughal-style fort gate with flags"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a scroll and quill with tiny crowns around it, symbolising treaties and rulers of the 18th century.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Scroll and quill with crowns symbolising rulers and treaties"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Who was the Mughal emperor whose death in 1707 led to the decline of Mughal power and rise of regional kingdoms?","options":["Akbar","Aurangzeb","Bahadur Shah Zafar","Jahangir"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The states which were formally under the Mughal Empire but became practically independent in the 18th century are called:","options":["New states","Successor states","Dependent states","Allied states"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Which of the following is a correct example of a successor state?","options":["Mysore under Haidar Ali","Awadh under Saadat Khan","The Maratha kingdom under Shivaji","The Sikh kingdom under Ranjit Singh"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. The Jats in the 18th century were powerful mainly in the region around:","options":["Awadh","Delhi and Agra","Hyderabad","Bengal"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False (Choose the correct option)","questions":[{"question":"5. Awadh, Bengal and Hyderabad were all former Mughal provinces that became almost independent in the 18th century.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The Marathas organised their rule under a confederacy system, where different chiefs controlled different regions.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The Rajput states did not play any political role in the 18th century after the decline of the Mughals.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"8. ____________ Khan founded the state of Awadh in the early 18th century.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. The ruler who made Hyderabad an independent state was ____________-ul-Mulk, also known as Asaf Jah I.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. The kingdom of ________ under rulers like Haidar Ali and Tipu Sultan emerged as a strong power in south India during the 18th century.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Aurangzeb"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Successor states"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Awadh under Saadat Khan"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Delhi and Agra"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Saadat"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Chin Qilich Khan"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Mysore"}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T20:06:38.728Z"},{"id":38,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"history","chapter":"18th century political formation","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"18th Century Political Formations – CBSE Class 7 History Worksheet","instructions":"• Read each question carefully.\n• For MCQs and True/False, tick (✓) the correct option.\n• For Fill in the Blanks, write the correct word(s) in the space provided.\n• Attempt all questions.\n• Keep your work neat and legible.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple, colorful line-art map of the Indian subcontinent with small flags marking Delhi, Awadh, Hyderabad, and Bengal to show rising regional powers in the 18th century.","position":"top-right","altText":"Minimalist map of India with markers for major 18th century regional kingdoms"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of an 18th century Indian court scene with a ruler on a low throne, a few courtiers, and scribes holding scrolls, using soft, bright colors.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Colorful line-art of an Indian ruler in court with courtiers and scribes"},{"description":"Simple colorful icons of a fort, a coin, and a sword representing military power, revenue collection, and administration.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Minimalist icons of a fort, coin, and sword showing power and revenue"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Which of the following was a major reason for the decline of the Mughal Empire in the 18th century?","options":["Strong control of distant provinces","Succession conflicts and weak rulers after Aurangzeb","Increase in agricultural productivity","Peaceful relations with all regional powers"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Who among the following was the founder of the independent state of Awadh?","options":["Murshid Quli Khan","Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah","Saadat Khan Burhan-ul-Mulk","Haider Ali"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. The Jats emerged as powerful rulers in the 18th century in the region around:","options":["Benares and Patna","Agra and Mathura","Hyderabad and Golconda","Bombay and Surat"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. Murshid Quli Khan became virtually independent while ruling which province of the Mughal Empire?","options":["Awadh","Hyderabad","Bengal","Punjab"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False (Choose the correct option)","questions":[{"question":"5. After Aurangzeb’s death, Mughal emperors could easily control distant provinces without any difficulty.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The Marathas built a powerful kingdom with their capital at Poona and collected chauth from many regions.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah tried to carve out an independent state of Hyderabad while still pretending to be a loyal Mughal noble.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"8. The rulers who were officially Mughal governors but acted as independent kings in the 18th century were often called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. The __________ were originally service gentry and peasant–pastoral groups who rose in revolt and became powerful in regions like Rajasthan and the North-West.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. The system by which the Marathas claimed a share of land revenue, usually one-fourth of the total, from other rulers was known as __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Succession conflicts and weak rulers after Aurangzeb"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Saadat Khan Burhan-ul-Mulk"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Agra and Mathura"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Bengal"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"successor states / autonomous states"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Rajputs"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"chauth"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T20:06:37.722Z"},{"id":37,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"history","chapter":"18th century political formation","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"18th Century Political Formations – Worksheet (CBSE Class 7 History)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully.\n• For MCQs and True/False, tick (✓) the correct option.\n• For Fill in the Blanks, write your answers clearly in the space provided.\n• Do not overcrowd your answers; write neatly.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist map outline of India around the 18th century with simple icons showing a crown for the Mughals in the north, a sword for the Marathas in the Deccan, and a fort for regional kingdoms.","position":"top-right","altText":"Simple map of 18th-century India with icons for major powers"},{"description":"Line-art of a small 18th-century Indian town scene with a fort, a market, and a few soldiers, in soft primary colors.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Minimalist drawing of a fort and town market in the 18th century"},{"description":"Colorful minimalist illustration of a royal durbar with a ruler on a low throne and courtiers standing around.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Simple royal court scene from 18th-century India"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. The invasion of which ruler in 1739 seriously weakened the Mughal Empire?","options":["A. Ahmad Shah Abdali","B. Nadir Shah","C. Sher Shah Suri","D. Tipu Sultan"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"2. The local rulers who collected land revenue and became powerful in the 18th century were mainly called:","options":["A. Mansabdars","B. Zamindars","C. Jagirdars only","D. Peshwas"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"3. Who was the founder of the Hyderabad state in the 18th century?","options":["A. Saadat Khan","B. Murshid Quli Khan","C. Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah","D. Raghunath Rao"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"4. The Jats established themselves mainly in the region around:","options":["A. Awadh","B. Poona","C. Bharatpur","D. Arcot"],"answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False (Choose the Correct Option)","questions":[{"question":"5. After Aurangzeb’s death, the central authority of the Mughal Empire became weak and many regional powers emerged.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"6. The nawabs of Awadh and Bengal always strictly obeyed the Mughal emperor in Delhi in all matters.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"7. The Marathas became powerful under the leadership of the Peshwas during the 18th century.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"8. The system by which revenue-collecting rights (jagirs) were assigned to nobles in the Mughal Empire was called the __________ system.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"9. Saadat Khan was the founder of the state of __________ in the 18th century.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0},{"question":"10. The Marathas divided their territory into units called __________, each under a powerful chief.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"B. Nadir Shah"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"B. Zamindars"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"C. Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"C. Bharatpur"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"jagir or jagirdari"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Awadh"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"swarajyas or spheres of influence; commonly referred to as regions under different Maratha chiefs (e.g., Sindhia, Holkar, Gaekwad, Bhonsle). For Class 7 CBSE, you may accept: 'regions under different Maratha chiefs'."}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T20:06:36.424Z"},{"id":36,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"history","chapter":"18th century political formation","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"18th Century Political Formations – Worksheet (CBSE Class 7 History)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully and answer in the space provided.\n• For MCQs, tick (✓) the correct option.\n• For picture-based questions, read the scene and write your answer in 1–2 words.\n• Attempt all questions. Maximum marks as per teacher’s instructions.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist illustration of an 18th-century Indian map outline with small icons of forts, crowns, and swords placed over regions like Bengal, Mysore, Awadh, and Hyderabad.","position":"top-right","altText":"Simple map of 18th-century India with forts and crowns marking regional kingdoms"},{"description":"Line-art of a Mughal-style fort gate with fluttering flags, and smaller houses around it to show a regional capital city growing around a fort.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Fort gate of an 18th-century regional capital with houses around it"},{"description":"Minimalist drawing of three figures side by side: a Mughal emperor on a throne, a Maratha warrior on horseback, and a nawab in a decorated robe holding a royal farman.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Mughal emperor, Maratha warrior and nawab representing different political powers"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Who was the Mughal emperor whose death in 1707 marked the beginning of the rapid decline of the Mughal Empire?","options":["A. Akbar","B. Aurangzeb","C. Shah Jahan","D. Bahadur Shah Zafar","True"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Which regional power emerged in western India and challenged the Mughals in the 18th century?","options":["A. The Marathas","B. The Rajputs","C. The Nawabs of Awadh","D. The Nizam of Hyderabad"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Which of the following was NOT a cause of the weakening of the Mughal Empire in the 18th century?","options":["A. Successive wars of succession","B. Rising power of regional nobles","C. Efficient central administration","D. Foreign invasions like Nadir Shah’s","None"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. Who founded the independent state of Hyderabad while remaining a nominal supporter of the Mughal emperor?","options":["A. Saadat Khan","B. Murshid Quli Khan","C. Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah","D. Haider Ali"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. Murshid Quli Khan became virtually independent in which province of the former Mughal Empire?","options":["A. Awadh","B. Bengal","C. Mysore","D. Hyderabad"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The Nawab who made Awadh an independent regional kingdom in the early 18th century was:","options":["A. Saadat Khan","B. Tipu Sultan","C. Balaji Vishwanath","D. Murshid Quli Khan"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. Which Maratha leader is associated with the office of the ‘Peshwa’ becoming very powerful and controlling Maratha affairs?","options":["A. Shivaji","B. Baji Rao I","C. Asaf Jah","D. Saadat Khan"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section B – Identify from Picture (Scene-based Questions)","questions":[{"question":"8. Picture in words:\nYou see a large, bustling port city on the eastern coast of India in the early 18th century. Ships are anchored in the harbour. Nearby, a grand building houses the offices of a powerful nawab who controls trade and collects taxes. The region around the city is known for fertile rice-growing lands, and the nawab is named Murshid Quli Khan.\nIdentify the province/region that this scene most likely represents.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. Picture in words:\nA fort-city in the Deccan is shown. Inside the court hall, a noble with the title ‘Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah’ sits on a seat of authority. Behind him hangs an imperial Mughal farman (order) on the wall, showing that he still claims to serve the emperor, but outside the court his own soldiers, officers and coins show that he rules independently.\nIdentify the state/kingdom that is being described.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. Picture in words:\nIn the western plateau region of India, you see a warrior on horseback wearing a turban and armour, leading a group of cavalrymen. They are collecting chauth and sardeshmukhi from local rulers in return for protection. A council of Maratha chiefs meets at a hill-fort under the leadership of the Peshwa.\nIdentify the political power or group being described.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"B. Aurangzeb"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"A. The Marathas"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"C. Efficient central administration"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"C. Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"B. Bengal"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"A. Saadat Khan"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"B. Baji Rao I"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Bengal"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Hyderabad"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"The Marathas"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T20:06:30.999Z"},{"id":35,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"social science","chapter":"18th century political formation","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"18th Century Political Formations – Worksheet (CBSE Class 7 Social Science)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully and answer in the space provided.\n• For MCQs and True/False, choose the most appropriate option.\n• For Fill in the Blanks, write only the correct word/phrase in the blank.\n• For Identify from Picture questions, read the description of the scene and then write the correct answer.\n• Attempt all questions. Marks are not indicated, but all questions are important.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple colorful line-art map outline of the Indian subcontinent with small flags marking Awadh, Hyderabad, and Bengal, and a scroll reading '18th Century India'.","position":"top-right","altText":"Colorful outline map of 18th century India with key regional states marked"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a Mughal-style fort with domes and arches, a fading imperial emblem above it, and smaller banners rising around it symbolizing regional powers.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Mughal fort with fading empire and rising regional powers"},{"description":"Child-friendly drawing of three nobles in different regional dresses labelled Nawab, Nizam, and Maratha chief, standing near piles of revenue records and coins.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Regional rulers of 18th century India with revenue records and coins"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Which Mughal ruler’s death in 1707 is generally taken as the beginning of the decline of the Mughal Empire?","options":["Akbar","Aurangzeb","Shah Jahan","Bahadur Shah II"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The term ‘subadar’ in the 18th century referred to:","options":["A village headman","A provincial governor under the Mughals","A local moneylender","A religious priest"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Who among the following was the founder of the state of Awadh as an autonomous region under the Mughals?","options":["Murshid Quli Khan","Saadat Khan","Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah","Hyder Ali"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah was associated with the founding of which 18th-century regional state?","options":["Awadh","Mysore","Hyderabad","Bengal"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False (Choose the correct option)","questions":[{"question":"5. The later Mughal emperors were strong rulers who firmly controlled all their nobles and provinces.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The Jats, Sikhs and Marathas emerged as important new political groups in the 18th century.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. Murshid Quli Khan strengthened the position of the Bengal nawabs by strictly controlling revenue collection and reducing Mughal interference.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"8. As the Mughal Empire declined, several ___________________ states like Awadh, Hyderabad and Bengal began to act independently while still accepting the Mughal emperor in name.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. In the 18th century, the ___________________ emerged as a powerful warrior group in western India under leaders like Peshwas.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D – Identify from Picture (Read the scene carefully and answer)","questions":[{"question":"10. Picture Scene 1 (Described): The picture shows a grand Mughal-style throne in the centre of a faded, slightly ruined court hall. On the walls, portraits of earlier mighty Mughal emperors look bright, but the emperor currently on the throne looks weak and worried. Around him, strong nobles and regional rulers sit confidently on separate, well-decorated seats. At the back of the hall, a map shows different provinces slowly separating from the centre.\n\nQuestion: What major political process or trend of the 18th century does this scene represent? (Identify it in 2–3 words.)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. Picture Scene 2 (Described): The picture shows a map of India with three areas highlighted in different colours: an area around Lucknow ruled by a nawab, an area around Hyderabad ruled by a powerful noble, and an area in eastern India around Murshidabad and Kolkata ruled by another nawab. Each area has a small label: one says ‘Nawab’, another says ‘Nizam’, and another says ‘Nawab of Bengal’. At the top is a small, faint Mughal crown symbol.\n\nQuestion: What common term is used for such 18th-century regional kingdoms that were once part of the Mughal Empire but became practically independent?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. Picture Scene 3 (Described): The picture shows sturdy farmers wearing simple clothes, some holding spears and swords. Their leader is on horseback, collecting revenue from a village headman while also promising protection from bandits. Behind them, a fort with a Sikh flag (with traditional Sikh symbol) flies on top, and people are bringing grain and money into storehouses.\n\nQuestion: Which 18th-century community or group, known for combining agriculture, trade and military power in the north-western region, is being shown here?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Aurangzeb"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"A provincial governor under the Mughals"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Saadat Khan"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Hyderabad"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"provincial (or successor / breakaway) – most appropriate: provincial"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Marathas"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Decline of the Mughal Empire (or Fragmentation of the Mughal Empire)"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Successor states (or regional successor states)"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Sikhs"}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T20:05:23.112Z"},{"id":34,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"social science","chapter":"18th century political formation","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"18th Century Political Formations – Worksheet (CBSE Class 7 Social Science)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully and answer in the space provided.\n• For MCQs and True/False, choose the correct option.\n• For fill in the blanks, write only the correct word(s).\n• For picture-based questions, observe the described scene and answer briefly.\n• Attempt all questions.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist illustration of a map of India with small icons of forts, crowns, and scrolls showing different regional kingdoms in the 18th century.","position":"top-right","altText":"Map of 18th century India with symbols for various regional powers."},{"description":"Simple line-art of a royal court scene with a nawab on a throne, courtiers around, and a European trader ship in the background, all in soft pastel colors.","position":"between-sections","altText":"18th century Indian ruler holding court with European traders in the background."},{"description":"Minimalist drawing of three soldiers: a Mughal horseman, a Maratha warrior, and a Sikh soldier, each in distinct traditional attire and weapons.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Different types of 18th century Indian soldiers representing various regional powers."}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Which of the following was a major reason for the decline of the Mughal Empire in the 18th century?","options":["Strong control over nobles","Succession conflicts and weak rulers after Aurangzeb","Continuous victories in foreign wars","Increasing support from powerful zamindars"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The term ‘subadar’ in the 18th century referred to:","options":["A village headman","A Mughal provincial governor","A merchant guild leader","A religious scholar"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Which regional power was closely associated with the city of Pune in the 18th century?","options":["Rajputs","Marathas","Jats","Sikhs"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"4. After the decline of Mughal power, many ______ and governors began to act as independent rulers in the 18th century.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. The powerful banking and moneylending community that supported regional powers like the Marathas and Rajputs were called ______.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The kingdom of Awadh was founded by the Mughal governor ______, who later became practically independent.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section C – True or False (Tick the Correct Option)","questions":[{"question":"7. The Jats emerged as a powerful peasant community in the region around Delhi and Agra during the 18th century.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. The Marathas built a strong navy and controlled most of the coastal trade of the Bay of Bengal in the 18th century.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section D – Multiple Choice Questions (Regional Powers)","questions":[{"question":"9. Who among the following was an important 18th century ruler of Mysore who opposed the British?","options":["Raja Sawai Jai Singh","Tipu Sultan","Ranjit Singh","Baji Rao I"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. The Sikhs in the 18th century organized themselves into armed bands or groups known as:","options":["Misls","Subas","Jagirs","Iqta"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. Hyderabad, Awadh and Bengal in the 18th century were:","options":["New independent kingdoms formed by Mughal governors","European colonies","Small tribal chiefdoms","Religious states ruled by priests"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section E – Identify from Picture (Answer in One or Two Words)","questions":[{"question":"12. Imagine a painting showing a large walled fort on a rocky hilltop with sturdy bastions. Below the fort is a bustling town with narrow lanes. In the foreground, a group of mounted warriors wearing turbans, carrying long spears and shields, ride out under a saffron flag. This scene is set near the Deccan plateau in the 18th century. Identify the regional power most likely represented in this scene.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. Visualise a scene where a ruler sits in a richly decorated durbar hall in Lucknow, wearing fine silk robes and jewels. Around him are Persian-speaking nobles, and outside the palace, traders and bankers are busy in the bazaar. This 18th century state was once a Mughal province but later became virtually independent. Name this kingdom.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Succession conflicts and weak rulers after Aurangzeb"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"A Mughal provincial governor"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Marathas"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"zamindars"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"bankers (or shroffs/mahajans – any one correct term acceptable; preferred: bankers)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Saadat Khan"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Tipu Sultan"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Misls"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"New independent kingdoms formed by Mughal governors"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Marathas"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Awadh"}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T20:05:22.517Z"},{"id":33,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"social science","chapter":"18th century political formation","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"18th Century Political Formations – Worksheet (CBSE Class 7 Social Science)","instructions":"Read all questions carefully. Answer in the spaces provided. For MCQs and True/False, tick (✓) the correct option. Write neatly and keep your answers brief and to the point.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple, colorful line-art map of India around the 18th century showing a fading Mughal Empire in the center and rising regional kingdoms shaded in different colors.","position":"top-right","altText":"Minimalist map of 18th century India with Mughal and regional powers"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of three rulers: a Mughal emperor on a throne, a Maratha warrior on horseback, and a Nawab of Bengal holding a farman (royal order).","position":"between-sections","altText":"Cartoon-style rulers representing Mughal, Maratha and Bengal Nawab"},{"description":"Colorful line-art of a busy 18th century Indian market town with a small fort, caravans, and merchants trading under tents.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Illustration of an 18th century Indian town with a fort and market"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Which Mughal ruler’s death in 1707 is generally seen as marking the beginning of the decline of the Mughal Empire?","options":["Akbar","Aurangzeb","Bahadur Shah I","Shah Jahan"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. The Marathas were originally the powerful chiefs of which region?","options":["Punjab","Awadh","Western Deccan","Bengal"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Which of the following was a major cause for the weakening of the Mughal Empire in the 18th century?","options":["Strong, honest nobles","Efficient administration","Frequent wars of succession","Abundance of revenue"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. Who was the founder of the state of Awadh as an autonomous regional power under the Mughals?","options":["Murshid Quli Khan","Sa‘adat Khan","Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah","Tipu Sultan"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"5. As the Mughal power declined, many ____________________ (central / regional) kingdoms such as Awadh, Hyderabad and Bengal emerged as strong political powers.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. ____________________ Khan became the first powerful Nawab of Bengal and shifted the capital from Dacca to Murshidabad.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The Jats established their power around the region of ____________________ near Delhi and Agra.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section C – True or False (Tick the Correct Option)","questions":[{"question":"8. In the 18th century, the Mughal emperors were still very powerful and directly controlled all regional rulers.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah tried to reduce Mughal interference and gradually made Hyderabad almost independent.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. The Sikh power under Maharaja Ranjit Singh became a strong kingdom in the region of Punjab during the early 19th century.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D – Identify from Picture (Answer in One or Two Words)","questions":[{"question":"11. Imagine a colorful painting from the early 18th century: A richly dressed nobleman sits in a small but grand court hall in Murshidabad. Behind him is a large chest of coins symbolising Bengal’s wealth. On the wall hangs a farman (imperial order) from the Mughal emperor, but the nobleman is shown consulting his own advisors and tax collectors rather than the emperor’s men. Identify this regional ruler or his office: Who is this powerful provincial leader of Bengal?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. Picture a rugged hill-fort on a plateau in the western Deccan. Outside the fort gate, soldiers in light armour and turbans, some mounted on fast horses, are ready to move quickly. A saffron battle flag flutters above the fort, and nearby villagers bring supplies, showing their support. Which rising power in the 18th century does this scene most likely represent?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. Visualise a busy fair near the city of Amritsar: farmers and traders arrive with goods, while armed warriors in turbans and long robes stand guard. In the distance, a fortified city with golden domes reflects growing power and prosperity under a single strong leader called the ‘Maharaja’. Which kingdom or community’s political formation does this scene depict?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Aurangzeb"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Western Deccan"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Frequent wars of succession"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Sa‘adat Khan"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"regional"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Murshid Quli"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Bharatpur"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Nawab of Bengal (Murshid Quli Khan or a Bengal Nawab)"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"The Marathas"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"The Sikh kingdom under Maharaja Ranjit Singh"}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T20:05:19.279Z"},{"id":32,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"social science","chapter":"18th century political formation","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"18th Century Political Formations – Worksheet (CBSE Class 7 Social Science)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully and answer in the space provided.\n• For MCQs, tick (✔) the correct option.\n• For True/False, choose the correct option.\n• For Fill in the Blanks, write only the correct word(s).\n• For Picture-based questions, carefully read the scene description and identify as asked.\n• Attempt all questions.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist map outline of the Indian subcontinent around 18th century with small icons showing a mughal crown in the north, a maratha horseman in the west, and a nawab’s turban in the east.","position":"top-right","altText":"Simple map of 18th century India showing Mughal, Maratha and regional powers."},{"description":"Line-art of a fort with triangular flags on the walls and a few soldiers carrying spears and shields, drawn in bright but simple colors.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Colorful drawing of an 18th century Indian fort with soldiers."},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a royal durbar scene: a ruler on a low throne, courtiers standing around, and a scribe writing on a scroll.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Durbar of an 18th century Indian ruler with courtiers and a scribe."}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Who was the Mughal emperor whose death in 1707 led to the decline of central Mughal authority?","options":["Akbar","Aurangzeb","Bahadur Shah II","Jahangir"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Which of the following was the capital of the Maratha power under the Peshwas in the 18th century?","options":["Delhi","Pune","Lucknow","Ahmedabad"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Murshid Quli Khan was the first Nawab of which region?","options":["Awadh","Bengal","Hyderabad","Mysore"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"4. Who founded the state of Hyderabad as an independent kingdom in the 18th century?","options":["Saadat Khan","Murshid Quli Khan","Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah","Raja Sawai Jai Singh"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False (Choose the Correct Option)","questions":[{"question":"5. The later Mughal emperors were strong rulers who controlled all parts of the empire effectively.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. In the 18th century, many powerful nobles and regional governors became practically independent of the Mughal emperor.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. The Jats, Sikhs and Marathas were some of the new political groups that emerged in the 18th century.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"8. After the decline of the Mughal Empire, many ________ kingdoms such as Awadh, Bengal and Hyderabad emerged.","options":["","","",""],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. The Sikh community in the 18th century was organised into small military bands known as ________, which later united into a powerful confederacy.","options":["","","",""],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. The Marathas collected a kind of tax called ________ (one-fourth of the land revenue) and sardeshmukhi (an additional tax) from many parts of India.","options":["","","",""],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D – Identify from Picture (Scene-based Short Answers)","questions":[{"question":"11. Imagine a painting: A ruler dressed in rich robes and a turban sits in a durbar at Lucknow. European traders and local merchants stand before him with gifts. Behind the throne, you see a banner showing a fish emblem, which was a famous symbol of this court. Which 18th century regional kingdom is being shown in this scene?","options":["","","",""],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. Picture a rugged landscape near Delhi: armed peasants on horseback attack a Mughal revenue convoy. They snatch the collected revenue and distribute it among local villagers. These rebels are known for frequent raids and for setting up small forts (garhis) in the countryside. Which community or group from 18th century North India is best represented in this scene?","options":["","","",""],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. Visualise a map of western and central India: light horsemen move quickly across a wide area, collecting chauth and sardeshmukhi. Their main base is shown near Pune, and they are led by a Peshwa. Which powerful political group is shown spreading its influence in this imagined map?","options":["","","",""],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Aurangzeb"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Pune"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Bengal"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"regional"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"misls"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"chauth"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Awadh"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Jats"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"The Marathas"}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T20:05:15.867Z"},{"id":31,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"social science","chapter":"18th century political formation","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"18th Century Political Formations – Worksheet (CBSE Class 7 Social Science)","instructions":"• Read each question carefully and answer in the space provided.\n• For MCQs and True/False, choose the correct option.\n• For Fill in the Blanks, write the correct word(s) in the blank.\n• For Picture-based questions, carefully read the scene described and identify what is asked.\n• Attempt all questions.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful, minimalist map outline of India with small icons of forts, flags, and royal umbrellas marking different regions to show various 18th century kingdoms and states.","position":"top-right","altText":"Map of India with icons showing different 18th century regional powers"},{"description":"Simple line-art of a Mughal-style fort with arches and domes, a fading imperial flag on top, and in the background some rising smaller flags representing regional kingdoms like Awadh, Hyderabad, and Bengal.","position":"between-sections","altText":"Mughal fort with fading power and regional kingdoms rising"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of three figures: a Mughal emperor on a throne, a Maratha noble on horseback, and a Sikh warrior holding the Khalsa flag, all drawn in a child-friendly cartoon style.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Cartoon-style figures representing Mughal, Maratha and Sikh powers"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Who was the Mughal emperor during whose reign Nadir Shah invaded India and sacked Delhi in 1739?","options":["Aurangzeb","Bahadur Shah I","Muhammad Shah","Shah Alam II"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Who among the following is considered the founder of the autonomous state of Awadh in the 18th century?","options":["Murshid Quli Khan","Saadat Khan","Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah","Alivardi Khan"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. The title ‘Peshwa’ in the Maratha administration referred to the:","options":["King of the Marathas","Prime Minister of the Maratha state","Chief of the army","Collector of land revenue"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Section B – True or False (Choose the Correct Option)","questions":[{"question":"4. After Aurangzeb’s death, the Mughal Empire became stronger and more centralized.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. The Jats emerged as a powerful peasant community around Delhi and Agra in the 18th century.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. The Nawabs of Bengal, like Murshid Quli Khan, tried to exercise greater control over local zamindars and revenue collection.","options":["True","False"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section C – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"7. The Mughal Empire began to decline after the death of Emperor __________ in 1707.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. The powerful state founded by Nizam-ul-Mulk Asaf Jah in the Deccan region was called __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"9. In the Maratha Empire, the system of collecting land revenue through assignment of villages to military chiefs was known as __________.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D – Picture-based Identification (Identify from Description)","questions":[{"question":"10. Imagine a painting: A royal court scene inside a grand Mughal-style hall in Delhi. In the centre sits a Mughal emperor on a magnificent throne, but around him, many nobles are whispering among themselves. Outside the palace, small groups of armed horsemen belonging to Maratha, Jat and Sikh forces are shown controlling different roads leading into the city. The caption says: “India in the early 18th century.”\n\nBased on this scene, identify which major political change is being shown in the picture (use 3–4 words).","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"11. Imagine another picture: A map of the Deccan region with a large city marked as Hyderabad. Near it stands a nobleman in Mughal dress, turning his back slightly from the Mughal emperor in the distance and raising his own standard (flag). The caption reads: “A new dynasty in the Deccan.”\n\nIdentify the regional state or dynasty being referred to in this picture.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"12. Picture this scene: A group of warriors in blue and saffron robes, some on horseback and some on foot, carrying swords and spears. They are gathered around a triangular flag with a Khanda (double-edged sword) symbol. Behind them are green fields of Punjab, and in the distance, a fort flying their flag. The caption says: “Rise of a new power in the north-west.”\n\nIdentify the community or power shown in this picture.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"13. Imagine a drawing: In the foreground, a fortified town with high walls and a busy market. Farmers with turbans and simple clothes are seen bringing grain on bullock carts. On the walls, soldiers stand guard under a banner labelled “Bharatpur”. A note on the side says: “A powerful peasant community forms its own kingdom.”\n\nIdentify the community that is being represented in this scene.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Muhammad Shah"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Saadat Khan"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Prime Minister of the Maratha state"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"False"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"True"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Aurangzeb"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Hyderabad"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Chauth and sardeshmukhi system (or simply: Maratha revenue system)"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Decline of Mughal power and rise of regional states"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Hyderabad under the Nizam (Asaf Jah dynasty)"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"The Sikhs / Sikh power / Khalsa"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"The Jats"}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T20:05:15.330Z"},{"id":30,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 1","board":"CBSE","subject":"evs","chapter":"superstars","topic":"match the sports with the name","difficulty":"medium","length":15,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Superstars – Match the Sport with the Player","instructions":"Dear children, look at the names of the sports and the players. Draw a line to match the sport with the correct superstar. Read with an adult if you need help. Match carefully and neatly.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful, simple illustration of children playing different sports like cricket, football, and badminton on a playground","position":"top-right","altText":"Children playing different sports on a playground"},{"description":"Minimalist line-art of a trophy, a football, a cricket bat, and a racket with bright solid colors","position":"between-sections","altText":"Sports equipment and a trophy"},{"description":"Cute cartoon-style medals and stars around a smiling child holding a small cup","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Child holding a winner’s cup with medals and stars"}],"graphicEmojis":["⚽","🏏","🎾","⭐","🏅"],"sections":[{"type":"match","title":"Section A – Match the Sport with the Superstar","questions":[{"question":"Q1. Match the sport with the superstar player.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Cricket","right":"Sachin Tendulkar"},{"left":"Badminton","right":"P. V. Sindhu"},{"left":"Hockey","right":"Major Dhyan Chand"},{"left":"Football","right":"Sunil Chhetri"}]},{"question":"Q2. Match these games with the correct sportsperson.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Tennis","right":"Sania Mirza"},{"left":"Kabaddi","right":"Anup Kumar"},{"left":"Boxing","right":"Mary Kom"},{"left":"Cricket","right":"Virat Kohli"}]},{"question":"Q3. Match the sport with the Indian superstar.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Wrestling","right":"Sushil Kumar"},{"left":"Badminton","right":"Saina Nehwal"},{"left":"Athletics (Running)","right":"Milkha Singh"},{"left":"Chess","right":"Viswanathan Anand"}]},{"question":"Q4. Match and learn more superstars.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Cricket","right":"M. S. Dhoni"},{"left":"Badminton","right":"Kidambi Srikanth"},{"left":"Hockey","right":"Rani Rampal"},{"left":"Shooting","right":"Abhinav Bindra"}]},{"question":"Q5. Match the game with the player.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Cricket","right":"Rohit Sharma"},{"left":"Table Tennis","right":"Manika Batra"},{"left":"Boxing","right":"Vijender Singh"},{"left":"Weightlifting","right":"Mirabai Chanu"}]},{"question":"Q6. Match the players to the sports they play.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"P. T. Usha","right":"Athletics (Running)"},{"left":"Leander Paes","right":"Tennis"},{"left":"Dipa Karmakar","right":"Gymnastics"},{"left":"Bhaichung Bhutia","right":"Football"}]},{"question":"Q7. Match these star players with their games.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Deepika Kumari","right":"Archery"},{"left":"Saina Nehwal","right":"Badminton"},{"left":"Sunil Chhetri","right":"Football"},{"left":"Mary Kom","right":"Boxing"}]},{"question":"Q8. Match the sport with its famous Indian player.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Cricket","right":"Harmanpreet Kaur"},{"left":"Wrestling","right":"Sakshi Malik"},{"left":"Badminton","right":"P. V. Sindhu"},{"left":"Hockey","right":"Sardara Singh"}]},{"question":"Q9. Match the name of the game with the right champion.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Chess","right":"Praggnanandhaa R."},{"left":"Shooting","right":"Aishwary Pratap Singh Tomar"},{"left":"Cricket","right":"Smriti Mandhana"},{"left":"Badminton","right":"Lakshya Sen"}]},{"question":"Q10. Match the sports to the correct superstars.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Football","right":"Gurpreet Singh Sandhu"},{"left":"Tennis","right":"Rohan Bopanna"},{"left":"Kabaddi","right":"Pardeep Narwal"},{"left":"Cricket","right":"Shikhar Dhawan"}]},{"question":"Q11. Match each sport with one well-known Indian sportsperson.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Hockey","right":"Sandeep Singh"},{"left":"Boxing","right":"Lovlina Borgohain"},{"left":"Wrestling","right":"Bajrang Punia"},{"left":"Weightlifting","right":"Karnam Malleswari"}]},{"question":"Q12. Match the name of the game with a famous player.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Badminton","right":"Ashwini Ponnappa"},{"left":"Shooting","right":"Manu Bhaker"},{"left":"Tennis","right":"Mahesh Bhupathi"},{"left":"Cricket","right":"Anil Kumble"}]},{"question":"Q13. Match the Indian superstars to their main sport.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Mithali Raj","right":"Cricket"},{"left":"Ritu Phogat","right":"Wrestling"},{"left":"Annu Rani","right":"Javelin Throw"},{"left":"Deepa Malik","right":"Para Athletics"}]},{"question":"Q14. Match each game with the correct champion.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Gymnastics","right":"Dipa Karmakar"},{"left":"Cricket","right":"Rahul Dravid"},{"left":"Chess","right":"Koneru Humpy"},{"left":"Football","right":"Jeje Lalpekhlua"}]},{"question":"Q15. Match and revise all the sports superstars.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Athletics (Running)","right":"Hima Das"},{"left":"Archery","right":"Atanu Das"},{"left":"Cricket","right":"Kapil Dev"},{"left":"Badminton","right":"Pullela Gopichand"}]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Cricket – Sachin Tendulkar; Badminton – P. V. Sindhu; Hockey – Major Dhyan Chand; Football – Sunil Chhetri"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Tennis – Sania Mirza; Kabaddi – Anup Kumar; Boxing – Mary Kom; Cricket – Virat Kohli"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Wrestling – Sushil Kumar; Badminton – Saina Nehwal; Athletics (Running) – Milkha Singh; Chess – Viswanathan Anand"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"Cricket – M. S. Dhoni; Badminton – Kidambi Srikanth; Hockey – Rani Rampal; Shooting – Abhinav Bindra"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":4,"answer":"Cricket – Rohit Sharma; Table Tennis – Manika Batra; Boxing – Vijender Singh; Weightlifting – Mirabai Chanu"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":5,"answer":"P. T. Usha – Athletics (Running); Leander Paes – Tennis; Dipa Karmakar – Gymnastics; Bhaichung Bhutia – Football"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":6,"answer":"Deepika Kumari – Archery; Saina Nehwal – Badminton; Sunil Chhetri – Football; Mary Kom – Boxing"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":7,"answer":"Cricket – Harmanpreet Kaur; Wrestling – Sakshi Malik; Badminton – P. V. Sindhu; Hockey – Sardara Singh"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":8,"answer":"Chess – Praggnanandhaa R.; Shooting – Aishwary Pratap Singh Tomar; Cricket – Smriti Mandhana; Badminton – Lakshya Sen"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":9,"answer":"Football – Gurpreet Singh Sandhu; Tennis – Rohan Bopanna; Kabaddi – Pardeep Narwal; Cricket – Shikhar Dhawan"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":10,"answer":"Hockey – Sandeep Singh; Boxing – Lovlina Borgohain; Wrestling – Bajrang Punia; Weightlifting – Karnam Malleswari"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":11,"answer":"Badminton – Ashwini Ponnappa; Shooting – Manu Bhaker; Tennis – Mahesh Bhupathi; Cricket – Anil Kumble"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":12,"answer":"Mithali Raj – Cricket; Ritu Phogat – Wrestling; Annu Rani – Javelin Throw; Deepa Malik – Para Athletics"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":13,"answer":"Gymnastics – Dipa Karmakar; Cricket – Rahul Dravid; Chess – Koneru Humpy; Football – Jeje Lalpekhlua"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":14,"answer":"Athletics (Running) – Hima Das; Archery – Atanu Das; Cricket – Kapil Dev; Badminton – Pullela Gopichand"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T19:49:09.283Z"},{"id":29,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 1","board":"CBSE","subject":"maths","chapter":"data handling","topic":"organising","difficulty":"hard","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Grade 1 Maths – Data Handling: Organising Worksheet","instructions":"Look carefully at the pictures and tables. Count slowly and neatly. Then answer the questions. Use a pencil and show your thinking where needed.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful line-art of three baskets labeled A, B, and C with different fruits inside, showing sorted groups","position":"top-right","altText":"Baskets of fruits sorted into groups"},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a simple table with rows of smiling shapes (circles, triangles, squares) neatly arranged","position":"between-sections","altText":"Shapes organised in a table"},{"description":"Child-friendly drawing of four children dropping picture cards of toys into labeled boxes: cars, balls, dolls, and blocks","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Children organising toys into groups"}],"graphicEmojis":["🍎","🍌","🐱","🟦","🔺"],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A: Look, Count and Choose","questions":[{"question":"In a fruit basket there are 4 apples, 3 bananas and 2 mangoes. According to the data, which fruit is the most?","options":["Apples","Bananas","Mangoes","All are same"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Riya has 5 red balloons, 5 blue balloons and 2 green balloons. Which two colours have equal number of balloons?","options":["Red and green","Blue and green","Red and blue","Only green"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"A table shows: Cars = 6, Buses = 3, Bikes = 4. Which vehicle is the least?","options":["Cars","Buses","Bikes","Cars and Bikes"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B: Fill in the Blanks (Using Data)","questions":[{"question":"In a box there are 2 ⚽ balls, 5 🧸 teddy bears and 3 🚗 cars. The total number of toys is ______.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"A picture chart shows 3 cats and 4 dogs. There are more ______ than ______.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"In a class, 7 children like milk and 3 children like juice. The number of children who like milk is ______ than the number who like juice.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section C: Organise the Data","questions":[{"question":"Rohan has these crayons: red, blue, red, green, blue, red. Make groups by colour and write how many of each colour he has.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"In a basket there are 3 small balls and 5 big balls. How can you organise them in two groups? Write the group names and count.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"Here are shapes: 🔺 🔺 ⬜ ⬜ ⬜ 🔵 🔵. Organise them and write how many triangles, squares and circles there are.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section D: Match the Group to the Correct Description","questions":[{"question":"Look at the groups and match them to the correct sentence about the data.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"Group 1: 5 apples, 2 oranges","right":"More apples than oranges"},{"left":"Group 2: 3 pens, 3 pencils","right":"Equal number of pens and pencils"},{"left":"Group 3: 1 car, 4 buses","right":"More buses than cars"},{"left":"Group 4: 2 cats, 5 dogs","right":"Dogs are the biggest group"}]}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"Section E: Use the Table and Answer","questions":[{"question":"The table shows the favourite fruits of some children:\n\nFruit | Number of children\nApple | 4\nBanana | 6\nGrapes | 2\n\n(a) Which fruit is liked by the most children?\n(b) Which fruit is liked by the least children?\n(c) How many children like apples and bananas altogether?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":3,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"The picture chart shows toys in a toy shop:\n\n🧸 Teddy bears: 3\n🚗 Cars: 5\n⚽ Balls: 4\n\n(a) Which toy is in the middle when we arrange from smallest to biggest number?\n(b) How many toys are there in all?\n(c) Which toy is the biggest group?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":3,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"A class data shows how many children come by different ways:\n\nWalk: 5\nBus: 7\nCar: 3\n\n(a) Which way of coming to school is used by the most children?\n(b) How many children come by bus and car together?\n(c) How many more children walk than come by car?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":3,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Apples"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Red and blue"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Buses"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"10"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"dogs; cats"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"more"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Red: 3, Blue: 2, Green: 1"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"Two groups: small balls = 3, big balls = 5"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"Triangles: 2, Squares: 3, Circles: 2"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"Group 1 → More apples than oranges; Group 2 → Equal number of pens and pencils; Group 3 → More buses than cars; Group 4 → Dogs are the biggest group"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"(a) Banana\n(b) Grapes\n(c) 10"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"(a) Balls (⚽) with 4\n(b) 12\n(c) Cars (🚗) with 5"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"(a) Bus\n(b) 10\n(c) 2"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T19:21:28.989Z"},{"id":28,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 1","board":"CBSE","subject":"english","chapter":"be polite","topic":"compound words","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Be Polite – Fun with Compound Words (CBSE Grade 1 English)","instructions":"Read each question carefully. Join two small words to make one big word (compound word). Write neatly in the space given. Do not copy from your friend. Be polite and wait for your turn to answer.","graphics":[{"description":"A simple, colorful line-art of two children saying 'please' and 'thank you' with speech bubbles shaped like joined puzzle pieces.","position":"top-right","altText":"Two polite children with speech bubbles joined like a puzzle, showing compound words fit together."},{"description":"Minimalist illustration of a big friendly book with two smaller word-cards joining together to form one compound word.","position":"between-sections","altText":"A book and two word cards joining to make a compound word."},{"description":"Colorful line drawing of a sun wearing sunglasses next to a joined word card reading 'sunshine'.","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Sun with sunglasses and the compound word sunshine."}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Choose the Correct Compound Word","questions":[{"question":"1. Which of these is a compound word?","options":["sun","shine","sunshine","sunny"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. Which word is made by joining \"rain\" and \"bow\"?","options":["rainbow","rainbowy","rainbook","bowrain"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. Tick the compound word that we use when we walk and cross the road politely at the corner.","options":["playground","classroom","sunlight","corner"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Join the Words to Make Compound Words","questions":[{"question":"4. We say \"good\" + \"bye\" politely when we leave: ________","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. \"class\" + \"room\" = ________ (We sit here and listen quietly.)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. \"rain\" + \"coat\" = ________ (We wear this in the rain.)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"7. \"butter\" + \"fly\" = ________ (A beautiful insect that we watch quietly.)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section C – Match to Make Compound Words","questions":[{"question":"8. Match the words in Column A with the correct words in Column B to make compound words.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"sun","right":"light"},{"left":"note","right":"book"},{"left":"play","right":"ground"},{"left":"tooth","right":"brush"}]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D – Write the Compound Word","questions":[{"question":"9. Join these polite words: \"thank\" + \"you\". Write the new word:","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":1,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"10. Join these words and write the compound word:\n\"door\" + \"bell\" = __________________","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"sunshine"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"rainbow"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"playground"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"goodbye"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"classroom"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"raincoat"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":3,"answer":"butterfly"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"sunlight, notebook, playground, toothbrush"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"thankyou (often written as two words: thank you)"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"doorbell"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T19:02:57.480Z"},{"id":27,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 1","board":"CBSE","subject":"hindi","chapter":"swar","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"हिंदी कार्यपत्रक – स्वर (अ, आ, इ, ई, उ, ऊ, ए, ऐ, ओ, औ, अं, अः)","instructions":"प्रिय बच्चों, यह कार्यपत्रक ‘स्वर’ पर आधारित है। प्रत्येक प्रश्न ध्यान से पढ़कर हल करो। साफ-सुथरा लिखो और जहाँ माँगा है वहाँ सही विकल्प या अक्षर लिखो।","graphics":[{"description":"रंग-बिरंगी पेंसिलों और किताबों के साथ बड़े-बड़े स्वर अक्षर (अ, आ, इ, ई) दिखाते हुए सरल चित्र","position":"top-right","altText":"स्वर अक्षरों के साथ पेंसिल और किताब का चित्र"},{"description":"ब्लैकबोर्ड पर रंगीन चॉक से लिखे स्वर और पास में मुस्कुराता हुआ बच्चा पढ़ते हुए","position":"between-sections","altText":"ब्लैकबोर्ड पर लिखे स्वर पढ़ता हुआ बच्चा"},{"description":"इंद्रधनुष के रंगों में बने स्वर अक्षर और उनके नीचे छोटी-छोटी किताबें","position":"bottom-left","altText":"इंद्रधनुषी स्वर अक्षरों का चित्र"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"खंड – 1 : सही स्वर चुनो (Multiple Choice)","questions":[{"question":"1. ‘आम’ शब्द की शुरुआत किस स्वर से होती है?","options":["अ","आ","इ","उ"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"2. ‘इमली’ शब्द की शुरुआत वाला स्वर कौन-सा है?","options":["ए","इ","ओ","अ"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"3. ‘ऊन’ शब्द में कौन-सा स्वर आता है?","options":["उ","ऊ","ओ","औ"],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"खंड – 2 : रिक्त स्थान में सही स्वर भरो","questions":[{"question":"4. क _ ता  (खाली जगह पर सही स्वर भरकर पूरा शब्द बनाओ। संकेत: कुत्ता)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"5. म _ छली  (संकेत: मछली)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"6. ब _ ल  (संकेत: बाल)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":0,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"खंड – 3 : स्वर लिखो (Short Answer)","questions":[{"question":"7. कोई दो छोटे स्वर (जिनका उच्चारण जल्दी होता है) लिखो।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]},{"question":"8. कोई दो बड़े स्वर (जिनका उच्चारण थोड़ा लंबा होता है) लिखो।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[]}]},{"type":"match","title":"खंड – 4 : मिलान करो (स्वर और शब्द)","questions":[{"question":"9. स्तंभ ‘क’ के स्वर का स्तंभ ‘ख’ में सही शब्द से मिलान करो।","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2,"matchPairs":[{"left":"अ","right":"अंगूर"},{"left":"ई","right":"ईख"},{"left":"ओ","right":"ओखली"},{"left":"औ","right":"औजार"}]}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"खंड – 5 : शब्द बनाओ","questions":[{"question":"10. नीचे दिए गए स्वरों से शुरू होने वाले एक-एक सरल शब्द लिखो:\n(क) आ  ________\n(ख) उ  ________\n(ग) ए  ________","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":3,"matchPairs":[]}]}],"answerKey":[{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"आ"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"इ"},{"sectionIndex":0,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"ऊ"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"उ  (कुत्ता = क + उ + त्ता)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"अ  (मछली = म + अ + छी + ली)"},{"sectionIndex":1,"questionIndex":2,"answer":"आ  (बाल = ब + आ + ल)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"उदाहरण: अ, इ, उ (इनमें से कोई भी दो छोटे स्वर स्वीकार्य हैं)"},{"sectionIndex":2,"questionIndex":1,"answer":"उदाहरण: आ, ई, ऊ, ए, ऐ, ओ, औ (इनमें से कोई भी दो बड़े स्वर स्वीकार्य हैं)"},{"sectionIndex":3,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"अ → अंगूर, ई → ईख, ओ → ओखली, औ → औजार"},{"sectionIndex":4,"questionIndex":0,"answer":"(क) आ : आम / आटा\n(ख) उ : उल्लू / उंगली\n(ग) ए : एक / एड़ी  \n(इन जैसे किसी भी सही, सरल शब्द को सही माना जाए।)"}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T18:56:13.649Z"},{"id":26,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board","subject":"english","chapter":"home sweet home poem","topic":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Home Sweet Home – Multiple Choice Worksheet (Grade 7 English)","instructions":"Read the poem 'Home Sweet Home' carefully from your textbook before answering. For each question, choose the correct option (A, B, C, or D) and write the letter in the space provided. Answer all questions.","graphics":[{"description":"A cozy, colorful little house with smoke gently rising from the chimney and a small garden in front","position":"top-right","altText":"Colorful illustration of a small cozy home"},{"description":"A minimalist line-art of a family sitting together inside a house, with soft warm colors in the background","position":"between-sections","altText":"Simple drawing of a happy family in their home"},{"description":"A cheerful, colorful doormat with the words 'Home Sweet Home' written on it in playful letters","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Doormat showing the words Home Sweet Home"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. In the poem 'Home Sweet Home', what does the poet mainly express about home?","options":["A. It is a place full of danger and fear","B. It is more precious than any other place","C. It is only a place to sleep and eat","D. It is less important than travel and adventure"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"2. Which line from the poem best shows that nothing can replace one’s own home?","options":["A. 'Though we may roam, with joy we come'","B. 'An humble roof, a homely fare'","C. 'Be it ever so humble, there’s no place like home'","D. 'The world is wide, with wonders bright'"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"3. In the poem, the word 'humble' in the line 'Be it ever so humble' suggests that the home is:","options":["A. Very grand and luxurious","B. Simple but dearly loved","C. Broken and unsafe","D. Strange and unfamiliar"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"4. According to the poem, why does the poet value home more than rich or royal places?","options":["A. Because home has more money and gold","B. Because people at home obey all his orders","C. Because home gives love, comfort, and peace","D. Because home is always new and changing"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"5. When the poet says there is 'no place like home', what feeling is mainly expressed?","options":["A. Anger","B. Pride","C. Jealousy","D. Deep affection"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"6. The poem suggests that even a poor cottage is better than:","options":["A. A school classroom","B. A palace without love","C. A busy marketplace","D. A garden full of flowers"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"7. Which of these ideas is MOST closely linked to the message of the poem?","options":["A. Home is important only when it is big","B. Travelling is better than staying at home","C. Real happiness is in one’s own home","D. One should never talk about home"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"8. In the poem, the comfort of home is contrasted with:","options":["A. The silence of the night","B. The noise of the city","C. Foreign lands and grand buildings","D. The beauty of flowers and trees"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"9. Which of the following BEST describes the tone (overall mood) of the poem?","options":["A. Sad and hopeless","B. Loving and appreciative","C. Angry and complaining","D. Confused and doubtful"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"10. What can we learn from the poem 'Home Sweet Home'?","options":["A. We should always live alone","B. Only rich people can have a real home","C. We should value and respect our own home","D. A home is only made of bricks and stones"],"answerSpaceLines":2}]}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T18:17:05.332Z"},{"id":25,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"State Board","subject":"geography","chapter":"tides","topic":"types of tides","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"bw","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Types of Tides – Grade 7 Geography Worksheet","instructions":"1. Read each question carefully.\n2. Answer in your own words where required.\n3. For multiple choice questions, write the correct option (A/B/C/D).\n4. Do not use a calculator; use logical reasoning and what you have learned in class.\n5. Keep your work neat and label diagrams if you draw any.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful, minimalist illustration of the Earth, Moon, and Sun in a line, showing high tides on the sides of Earth facing and opposite the Moon","position":"top-right","altText":"Earth, Moon, and Sun aligned to show tidal effect"},{"description":"A simple blue wave icon with arrows pointing up and down to represent rising and falling tides","position":"between-sections","altText":"Rising and falling sea waves showing tide levels"},{"description":"A small coastal scene with a beach, a pier, and two water levels marked as high tide and low tide using clear, colorful lines","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Beach with high tide and low tide levels marked"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Which of the following best describes a spring tide?","options":["A. A tide that occurs only in the spring season","B. A tide with the smallest difference between high and low tide","C. A tide with the greatest difference between high and low tide","D. A tide caused only by the Sun"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"2. During which Moon phases do spring tides usually occur?","options":["A. New Moon and Full Moon","B. First Quarter and Last Quarter","C. Only during Full Moon","D. Only during New Moon"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"3. Neap tides are tides in which:","options":["A. The high tides are very high and low tides are very low","B. The difference between high tide and low tide is small","C. There is no high tide at all","D. They occur only once a year"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"4. Neap tides occur when the Sun, Earth, and Moon are positioned at:","options":["A. A straight line (180°)","B. A right angle (90°)","C. Random angles","D. All on the same side of the Earth"],"answerSpaceLines":2}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"5. Tides in which the difference between high tide and low tide is the greatest are called __________ tides.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"6. Tides in which the difference between high tide and low tide is the least are called __________ tides.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"7. Spring tides generally occur during the __________ Moon and the __________ Moon phases.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section C – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"8. What is the basic difference between spring tides and neap tides in terms of the height of water?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4},{"question":"9. Explain why neap tides are weaker than spring tides. Mention the role of the Sun and the Moon.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":5}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"Section D – Long Answer / Diagram-based Question","questions":[{"question":"10. Draw a simple labelled diagram to show the positions of the Sun, Earth, and Moon during:\n(a) Spring tide\n(b) Neap tide\nThen, in 4–5 sentences, explain how these positions affect the height of tides.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":10}]}]},"rating":null,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T18:14:02.960Z"},{"id":24,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 1","board":"CBSE","subject":"evs","chapter":"the animal kingdom","topic":"types of animal","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"The Animal Kingdom – Types of Animals (Grade 1 EVS)","instructions":"1. Write neatly and clearly.\n2. Read each question carefully before answering.\n3. Choose the correct answer or fill in the blanks.\n4. Ask your teacher if you do not understand a question.\n5. Do your work on your own.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful, smiling lion, elephant, and monkey standing together on green grass with a blue sky","position":"top-right","altText":"Smiling lion, elephant, and monkey on grass"},{"description":"A simple, colorful line-art of a fish swimming in blue water with small bubbles","position":"between-sections","altText":"Colorful fish in water"},{"description":"A cute, minimalist bird flying in the sky near a small tree and a butterfly","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Bird flying near a tree and butterfly"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A: Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Which of these animals lives on land?","options":["A. Fish","B. Frog","C. Cow","D. Duck"],"answerSpaceLines":1},{"question":"2. Which of these is a water animal?","options":["A. Dog","B. Fish","C. Cat","D. Tiger"],"answerSpaceLines":1},{"question":"3. Which animal can fly in the sky?","options":["A. Bird","B. Goat","C. Rabbit","D. Turtle"],"answerSpaceLines":1},{"question":"4. Which of these is a wild animal?","options":["A. Lion","B. Cow","C. Dog","D. Goat"],"answerSpaceLines":1},{"question":"5. Which of these is a domestic animal that lives on a farm?","options":["A. Tiger","B. Deer","C. Horse","D. Fox"],"answerSpaceLines":1}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B: Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"6. Animals that live in our homes or on farms are called __________ animals. (wild / domestic)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"7. Animals that live in forests and jungles are called __________ animals. (wild / domestic)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"8. Animals that live in water are called __________ animals. (water / land)","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section C: Match the Animals to Their Type","questions":[{"question":"9. Match the animal in Column A with its correct type in Column B.\n\nColumn A:\n1) Dog\n2) Lion\n3) Fish\n4) Sparrow\n\nColumn B:\nA) Water animal\nB) Pet animal\nC) Wild animal\nD) Flying animal\n\nWrite the correct letter (A, B, C or D) next to each number.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section D: Short Answer Question","questions":[{"question":"10. Name one animal that lives in water and one animal that lives on land.\nWater animal: __________\nLand animal: __________","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":3}]}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T18:08:02.218Z"},{"id":23,"serialNumber":null,"userId":3,"className":"Grade 7","board":"CBSE","subject":"geography","chapter":"water","topic":"","difficulty":"medium","length":10,"colorMode":"color","worksheetType":"worksheet","content":{"title":"Water – Class 7 Geography (CBSE) Worksheet","instructions":"1. Read each question carefully and attempt all questions.\n2. Write your answers in the space provided.\n3. Draw neat, labeled diagrams wherever necessary.\n4. Do not use unfair means. Try to answer in your own words.\n5. Maintain clean handwriting and proper spelling.","graphics":[{"description":"A colorful minimalist illustration of a blue water droplet with a smiling face and small white sparkles around it","position":"top-right","altText":"Smiling blue water droplet"},{"description":"Simple line-art of the water cycle showing a blue ocean, clouds, arrows for evaporation, condensation, and rainfall, in soft pastel colors","position":"between-sections","altText":"Water cycle with evaporation, condensation, and precipitation"},{"description":"A minimalist illustration of gentle ocean waves in different shades of blue with a small boat outline","position":"bottom-left","altText":"Gentle blue ocean waves with a small boat"}],"sections":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Section A – Multiple Choice Questions","questions":[{"question":"1. Which of the following processes of the water cycle is mainly responsible for the formation of clouds?","options":["Evaporation","Condensation","Precipitation","Infiltration"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"2. The continuous movement of water from the land and water bodies to the air and back to the land and water bodies is called:","options":["Water conservation","Water management","Water cycle","Water table"],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"3. Which of these water bodies contains only freshwater?","options":["Oceans","Seas","Lakes and rivers","Bays"],"answerSpaceLines":2}]},{"type":"fill_blanks","title":"Section B – Fill in the Blanks","questions":[{"question":"4. About ______ percent of the Earth’s surface is covered with water.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"5. The average height of the ocean surface is called the ______ level.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2},{"question":"6. The rhythmic rise and fall of ocean water twice in a day is known as ______.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":2}]},{"type":"short_answer","title":"Section C – Short Answer Questions","questions":[{"question":"7. What is precipitation? Name any two forms of precipitation.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4},{"question":"8. Why is the ocean water not fit for direct human consumption?","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":4}]},{"type":"match","title":"Section D – Match the Following","questions":[{"question":"9. Match the items in Column A with those in Column B:\n\nColumn A:\nA. Evaporation\nB. Condensation\nC. Tides\nD. Tsunami\n\nColumn B:\n1. Sudden movement of the ocean floor\n2. Change of water vapour into water droplets\n3. Rise and fall of ocean water due to the gravitational pull of the Sun and Moon\n4. Change of water into water vapour by heat","options":["A - 4, B - 2, C - 3, D - 1","A - 2, B - 4, C - 1, D - 3","A - 3, B - 1, C - 4, D - 2","A - 1, B - 3, C - 2, D - 4"],"answerSpaceLines":3}]},{"type":"long_answer","title":"Section E – Long Answer Question","questions":[{"question":"10. Explain the water cycle with the help of a neat, labelled diagram. In your answer, describe the processes of evaporation, condensation, and precipitation.","options":[],"answerSpaceLines":10}]}]},"rating":5,"createdAt":"2026-02-28T18:02:08.654Z"}]
